// PulseTrack exercise list. One exercise per line:
//   { name: "Rope Pushdown", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Triceps Rope Pushdown"] }
// "aka" = other names for the SAME exercise. They are searchable in the picker, and anything logged under
// one of those names still counts as this exercise (for "Done before" and the best-swap suggestions).
// "tips" = 3 or 4 form cues for the exercise, "avoid" = the common mistake. They show up under "Form tips". Custom exercises you add without them use general tips.
// Add your own lines anywhere. The order of the categories in this file is the order of the filter chips.
const EXERCISE_DATABASE = [
  // --- CHEST ---
  { name: "Bench Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Barbell Bench Press", "Barbell Flat Bench Press", "Flat Bench Press", "Bench Press HIIT 100's", "Bench Press HIIT 100's (0s Rest)", "Flat Press"], tips: ["Lie with your eyes under the bar, feet flat, shoulder blades pinched together and down", "Unrack with straight arms, then lower to your mid-chest with elbows about 45 to 60 degrees from your sides", "Keep your wrists stacked over your elbows and drive your feet into the floor as you press", "Press up and slightly back so the bar finishes over your shoulders"], avoid: "Bouncing the bar off your chest or lifting your butt off the bench." },
  { name: "Incline Bench Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Incline Barbell Bench Press", "Incline Barbell Bench Press (Low Angle)", "Incline Barbell Bench Press (Medium Angle)", "Incline Press"], tips: ["Set the bench to a low incline, around 30 degrees, so the work stays on the upper chest", "Pinch your shoulder blades and keep your upper back flat on the pad", "Lower the bar to your upper chest, just below the collarbones", "Press up and slightly back until your arms are straight over your shoulders"], avoid: "Setting the bench too steep, which turns it into a shoulder press." },
  { name: "Decline Bench Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Decline Barbell Bench Press", "Decline Barbell Press"], tips: ["Hook your legs securely in the pads before you unrack", "Lower the bar to your lower chest with control and a steady pace", "Keep your elbows tucked about 45 degrees and your wrists straight", "Press up without bouncing and rack the bar before you unhook your legs"], avoid: "Dropping the bar fast, because the decline angle makes it easy to lose control." },
  { name: "Wide-Grip Barbell Bench Press", category: "Chest", tips: ["Take a grip wider than shoulder width but keep your forearms vertical at the bottom", "Pinch your shoulder blades and keep your chest high", "Lower the bar to your mid-chest with a shorter range of motion than normal", "Press up while keeping your shoulders pulled back, not rolled forward"], avoid: "Going so wide that your shoulders feel pinched at the bottom." },
  { name: "Reverse-Grip Barbell Bench Press", category: "Chest", tips: ["Use a shoulder-width underhand grip and wrap your thumbs around the bar", "Keep your elbows tucked close to your ribs", "Lower the bar to your lower chest, near the bottom of your sternum", "Press the bar up in a straight line and keep your wrists stiff"], avoid: "Letting your wrists bend back, and loading heavy before your wrists are used to it." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Bench Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Flat Dumbbell Bench Press", "Flat Dumbbell Press", "Dumbbell Press"], tips: ["Sit with the dumbbells on your thighs, then kick them up as you lie back", "Start with the dumbbells above your chest, palms facing your feet", "Lower until your elbows are just below the bench, at about 45 degrees from your sides", "Press up and bring the dumbbells slightly together over your chest"], avoid: "Letting the weights drift out wide or drop below a comfortable stretch." },
  { name: "Incline Dumbbell Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Incline Dumbbell Bench Press"], tips: ["Set the bench to about 30 degrees and keep your back flat on the pad", "Start with the dumbbells above your upper chest, palms forward", "Lower with control until you feel a stretch across your upper chest", "Press up and bring them together without clanking the weights"], avoid: "Using a steep bench angle and letting your shoulders do the work." },
  { name: "Decline Dumbbell Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Decline Dumbbell Bench Press"], tips: ["Get the dumbbells into position carefully before lying back on the decline", "Lower them to your lower chest with your elbows at about 45 degrees", "Press up in a smooth arc until your arms are straight", "Lower the weights slowly and set them down before you sit up"], avoid: "Swinging the dumbbells up with momentum or dropping them to your sides." },
  { name: "Neutral-Grip Dumbbell Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["V Bar Press", "Dumbbell V Press", "V Press"], tips: ["Hold the dumbbells with your palms facing each other", "Keep your elbows tucked close to your ribs as you lower", "Lower until the dumbbells are beside your lower chest", "Press straight up, squeezing your chest and triceps together"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare, which defeats the shoulder-friendly grip." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Dumbbell Bench Press", category: "Chest", tips: ["Brace your core and press your free hand or feet down to stay square on the bench", "Lower the dumbbell until your elbow is just below the bench", "Keep your ribs and hips from twisting toward the weight", "Press straight up and finish with the dumbbell directly over your shoulder"], avoid: "Rotating your torso to muscle the weight up." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Flyes", category: "Chest", aka: ["Dumbbell Chest Fly", "Flat Bench Fly", "Flat Dumbbell Flies"], tips: ["Start with the dumbbells above your chest, palms facing each other, elbows slightly bent", "Open your arms wide like hugging a barrel until you feel a stretch in your chest", "Keep that same elbow bend the whole time", "Squeeze your chest to bring the weights back up in the same arc"], avoid: "Straightening your arms or going so deep that your shoulders strain." },
  { name: "Incline Dumbbell Flyes", category: "Chest", tips: ["Set the bench to about 30 degrees and press the dumbbells up to start", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows and open your arms in a wide arc", "Lower only as far as you feel a stretch in your upper chest", "Bring the dumbbells up as if hugging a tree, then squeeze at the top"], avoid: "Turning the move into a press by bending your elbows more as you lower." },
  { name: "Decline Dumbbell Flyes", category: "Chest", tips: ["Start with the dumbbells above your lower chest and a slight bend in your elbows", "Lower in a wide arc until you feel your chest stretch", "Keep your shoulders pinned back on the bench", "Pull the weights together in the same arc and pause at the top"], avoid: "Using weights so heavy you can't control the arc." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Pullover", category: "Chest", tips: ["Lie across or along the bench holding one dumbbell with both hands over your chest", "Keep a slight bend in your elbows as you lower the weight back behind your head", "Stop when you feel a deep stretch in your chest and lats, ribs down", "Pull the weight back over your chest using your chest and lats"], avoid: "Arching your lower back hard or bending your elbows into a triceps extension." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Flat Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Smith Machine Bench Press", "Smith Machine Press", "Smith Machine V Press", "Dead Stop Smith Machine Press"], tips: ["Set the bench so the bar lowers to your mid-chest, not your neck", "Pinch your shoulder blades and keep your feet planted", "Lower with control to your chest, elbows at about 45 degrees", "Press up and re-hook the bar by rotating your wrists at the end"], avoid: "Placing the bench too far forward or back so the bar path feels awkward." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Incline Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Smith Machine Incline Bench Press", "Smith Incline Press", "Smith Machine Incline"], tips: ["Set the bench to a low incline and line the bar up with your upper chest", "Pinch your shoulder blades down and back", "Lower the bar to your upper chest with your elbows about 45 degrees out", "Press up until your arms are straight, then rack it with the hooks"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders roll up toward your ears as you press." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Decline Press", category: "Chest", tips: ["Position the decline bench so the bar lands on your lower chest", "Brace your feet and keep your shoulder blades back", "Lower slowly to your lower chest with your elbows tucked", "Press up smoothly and re-hook the bar before you sit up"], avoid: "Pressing with your elbows flared wide." },
  { name: "Hammer Strength Flat Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Iso-Lateral Plate-Loaded Flat Press (Hammer Strength)"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so the handles line up with your mid-chest", "Sit tall with your back against the pad and shoulder blades pinched", "Press forward until your arms are nearly straight, without locking out", "Return slowly until you feel a stretch across your chest"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders round forward off the pad." },
  { name: "Hammer Strength Incline Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Iso-Lateral Plate-Loaded Incline Press (Hammer Strength)"], tips: ["Set the seat so the handles start at your upper chest", "Keep your back flat on the pad and your chest up", "Press up and slightly forward, driving through both arms evenly", "Lower under control until your hands are about chest height"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders up as you press." },
  { name: "Iso-Lateral Plate-Loaded Decline Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Hammer Strength Decline Press"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so the handles start near your lower chest", "Brace your back on the pad and keep your shoulders down", "Press each handle down and forward, matching both sides", "Return slowly to a comfortable chest stretch"], avoid: "Letting one arm lead, since each arm moves on its own." },
  { name: "Iso-Lateral Plate-Loaded Wide Chest Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Hammer Strength Wide Chest Press"], tips: ["Set the seat so the handles line up with your mid-chest", "Keep your shoulder blades back against the pad", "Press the handles forward in a wide path, squeezing your chest", "Control the return until your elbows are about in line with your torso"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare high and your shoulders take over." },
  { name: "Converging Chest Press Machine (Selectorized)", category: "Chest", tips: ["Set the seat so the handles line up with your mid-chest", "Sit tall with your back against the pad", "Press forward and let the handles move together, squeezing your chest at the end", "Return slowly, stopping before the weight stack touches"], avoid: "Letting the weight stack slam at the bottom." },
  { name: "Machine Chest Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Machine Chest Press (Seated/Standard)", "Leverage Chest Press", "Machine Bench Press", "Hammer Strength Low Press", "FST-7 Machine Bench Press", "Flat Machine Press", "Seated Machine Press", "Machine Press"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so the handles are at mid-chest height", "Keep your back and head against the pad and your shoulder blades pinched", "Press out until your arms are almost straight", "Come back slowly until you feel a light stretch across your chest"], avoid: "Pressing so fast that you lose control of the return." },
  { name: "Machine Incline Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Machine Incline Chest Press", "Leverage Incline Chest Press", "Dead Stop Incline Machine Press"], tips: ["Set the seat so the handles start near your upper chest", "Keep your back flat on the pad and your chest up", "Press up and forward without shrugging", "Lower slowly until your elbows are just behind your torso"], avoid: "Raising your shoulders up to your ears as you press." },
  { name: "Machine Decline Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Machine Decline Chest Press"], tips: ["Set the seat so your hands start near your lower chest", "Brace your back against the pad and keep your shoulders down", "Press down and forward in a smooth path", "Return slowly and stop short of letting the weights rest"], avoid: "Lifting your hips off the seat to help the press." },
  { name: "Pec Deck", category: "Chest", aka: ["Pec Deck Flye Machine", "Machine Chest Flye", "Chest Fly Machine", "Machine Fly", "Pec Deck Fly", "Machine Fly (FST-7)"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so your upper arms are level with your chest", "Sit tall with your back on the pad and a slight bend in your elbows", "Bring the arms together in front of you and squeeze your chest", "Return slowly until your chest is stretched but your shoulders stay back"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders roll forward or swinging the weight." },
  { name: "Cable Crossovers", category: "Chest", aka: ["Cable Crossovers (Mid-Chest)", "Cable Chest Flyes", "FST-7 Standing Cable Fly", "Cable Chest Fly"], tips: ["Set the pulleys high, step forward and lean slightly with one foot ahead for balance", "Start with your arms wide and a soft bend in your elbows", "Sweep your hands down and together in front of your hips", "Squeeze your chest, then return slowly to the wide position"], avoid: "Turning it into a press by bending your elbows a lot." },
  { name: "High-to-Low Cable Flyes", category: "Chest", aka: ["High-to-Low Cable Flyes (Lower Chest)"], tips: ["Set the pulleys above shoulder height and stand in a staggered stance", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows and your chest proud", "Bring your hands down and together toward your belt line", "Pause with your chest squeezed, then open back up slowly"], avoid: "Leaning forward and rocking your body to move the weight." },
  { name: "Low-to-High Cable Flyes", category: "Chest", aka: ["Low-to-High Cable Flyes (Upper Chest)"], tips: ["Set the pulleys at the bottom and stand in a staggered stance", "Start with your hands near your hips and a soft bend in your elbows", "Sweep your hands up and together to about chin height", "Squeeze your upper chest, then lower slowly"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders up as your hands rise." },
  { name: "Flat Cable Flyes (Bench)", category: "Chest", aka: ["Flat Cable Fly"], tips: ["Place a flat bench between low or mid pulleys and lie back holding a handle in each hand", "Start with your arms wide, palms up or facing in, with a soft bend in your elbows", "Bring your hands together over your chest in a hugging arc", "Return slowly until you feel a stretch, keeping your shoulder blades pinched"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders lift off the bench." },
  { name: "Incline Cable Flyes (Bench)", category: "Chest", aka: ["Incline Cable Fly", "Cable Incline Fly"], tips: ["Set the bench to a low incline between the pulleys", "Lie back with your shoulder blades pinched and a soft bend in your elbows", "Bring your hands together above your upper chest in a wide arc", "Lower slowly and stop when your chest feels stretched"], avoid: "Using so much weight that your elbows bend and it becomes a press." },
  { name: "Cable Scooped Chest Press", category: "Chest", tips: ["Stand in a staggered stance with the handles low near your hips, palms up", "Press forward and up in a scooping arc toward chin height", "Keep your elbows slightly lower than your hands", "Squeeze your upper chest, then return slowly"], avoid: "Leaning back or using your legs to push the weight." },
  { name: "Chest Dips", category: "Chest", aka: ["Dips - Chest Version"], tips: ["Grip the bars, lean your torso forward and let your elbows flare a little", "Lower slowly until you feel a deep stretch across your chest", "Keep your shoulders down and away from your ears", "Press up through your palms until your arms are almost straight"], avoid: "Dropping fast into the bottom, which can strain your shoulders." },
  { name: "Weighted Chest Dips", category: "Chest", tips: ["Master your bodyweight dips first and add weight in small steps", "Lean your torso forward and keep your chest up", "Lower under control to a comfortable stretch, no deeper than your shoulders allow", "Press up smoothly without swinging the belt or weight"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders roll forward at the bottom." },
  { name: "Machine Assisted Chest Dips", category: "Chest", aka: ["Assisted Chest Dips"], tips: ["Set the assist so you can finish every rep with good control", "Kneel or stand on the pad and lean your torso forward", "Lower until your elbows are about at 90 degrees or a comfortable chest stretch", "Press up and slowly lower the weight stack"], avoid: "Using so much assistance that you don't work for it." },
  { name: "Push-Ups", category: "Chest", aka: ["Standard Push-Ups"], tips: ["Place your hands just wider than your shoulders and make your body a straight line", "Squeeze your glutes and brace your core", "Lower your chest to about a fist from the floor, elbows about 45 degrees from your ribs", "Press the floor away until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag or your head drop forward." },
  { name: "Weighted Push-Ups", category: "Chest", tips: ["Have a partner place the plate on your upper back or wear a weighted vest", "Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels", "Lower under control until your chest is close to the floor", "Press up smoothly without letting your hips sag"], avoid: "Adding weight before you can do clean, full-range bodyweight reps." },
  { name: "Decline Push-Ups", category: "Chest", aka: ["Decline Push-Ups (Feet Elevated)"], tips: ["Put your feet on a bench or box and your hands on the floor", "Brace your core so your body stays in a straight line", "Lower your chest toward the floor with elbows about 45 degrees out", "Press up without letting your lower back sag"], avoid: "Setting your feet so high that the movement turns into a shoulder press." },
  { name: "Incline Push-Ups", category: "Chest", aka: ["Incline Push-Ups (Hands Elevated)"], tips: ["Put your hands on a bench or sturdy box and walk your feet back", "Keep your body straight from head to heels", "Lower your chest to the edge of the surface", "Press back up, squeezing your chest at the top"], avoid: "Letting your hips drop toward the surface." },
  { name: "Deficit Push-Ups", category: "Chest", tips: ["Put your hands on two sturdy plates or blocks so your chest can drop lower", "Brace your core and keep your body in a straight line", "Lower slowly until you feel a deep chest stretch", "Press up hard and finish with your arms straight"], avoid: "Dropping into the stretch quickly or letting your shoulders cave forward." },
  // more (added in 2.6.5)
  { name: "Floor Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Barbell Floor Press"], tips: ["Lie on the floor with your knees bent and the bar over your chest", "Lower the bar until your upper arms touch the floor lightly", "Pause for a second without relaxing", "Press back up, driving your feet and keeping your wrists stacked"], avoid: "Bouncing your triceps off the floor." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Floor Press", category: "Chest", tips: ["Lie on the floor with your knees bent and dumbbells over your chest", "Lower until your upper arms touch the floor, elbows about 45 degrees out", "Pause briefly with your arms relaxed", "Press up and bring the dumbbells slightly together"], avoid: "Dropping your elbows quickly onto the floor." },
  { name: "Spoto Press", category: "Chest", tips: ["Set up like a normal bench press with your shoulder blades pinched", "Lower the bar to about an inch above your chest", "Pause there for a full second, keeping your body tight", "Press up without bouncing or losing tension"], avoid: "Touching the bar to your chest and relaxing during the pause." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Squeeze Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Hex Press", "Dumbbell Hex Press"], tips: ["Press the dumbbells together hard from start to finish", "Keep your palms facing each other and the weights touching", "Lower slowly until the dumbbells are at your chest", "Press up while still pushing the dumbbells into each other"], avoid: "Letting the dumbbells drift apart as you press." },
  { name: "Svend Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Plate Squeeze Press"], tips: ["Hold a plate between your palms at chest height and squeeze it hard", "Stand tall with your elbows tucked and your core braced", "Press the plate straight out in front of you", "Bring it back to your chest with your hands still squeezing"], avoid: "Letting the plate slip or rotate in your hands." },
  { name: "Cable Chest Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Standing Cable Chest Press"], tips: ["Stand in a staggered stance with the handles at chest height", "Brace your core and keep your torso still", "Press the handles forward until your arms are nearly straight", "Bring them back slowly until you feel a stretch across your chest"], avoid: "Leaning forward and using your body to push." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Cable Chest Press", category: "Chest", tips: ["Stand in a staggered stance, set the handle at chest height", "Brace your core so your torso does not twist", "Press forward until your arm is nearly straight", "Return slowly while keeping your ribs and hips square"], avoid: "Rotating your torso toward the working arm." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Cable Crossover", category: "Chest", aka: ["Unilateral Cable Fly"], tips: ["Set the pulley high, step forward in a staggered stance", "Start with a soft bend in your elbow and your arm out to the side", "Sweep your hand down and across in front of your body", "Squeeze your chest at the end, then return slowly"], avoid: "Swinging your body or shoulder to move the cable." },
  { name: "Band Chest Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Resistance Band Chest Press"], tips: ["Anchor the band behind you at chest height or wrap it behind your back", "Stand in a staggered stance with your core braced", "Press forward until your arms are nearly straight", "Return slowly and keep tension on the band"], avoid: "Letting the band snap back quickly." },
  { name: "Wide-Grip Push-Ups", category: "Chest", tips: ["Place your hands wider than your shoulders and keep your body in a straight line", "Brace your core and squeeze your glutes", "Lower your chest to the floor with your elbows about 45 to 60 degrees out", "Press up and squeeze your chest at the top"], avoid: "Going so wide that your shoulders feel pinched." },
  { name: "Archer Push-Ups", category: "Chest", tips: ["Place your hands very wide and keep your body in a straight line", "Lower toward one hand while the other arm stays straight", "Lower until your chest is near the floor on the bending side", "Press back up and repeat on the other side"], avoid: "Letting your hips twist or rotating your body to help." },
  { name: "Clap Push-Ups", category: "Chest", aka: ["Plyo Push-Ups"], tips: ["Make sure you can do many strong push-ups first and use a soft surface", "Lower with control, then push explosively so your hands leave the floor", "Clap quickly and place your hands back down with soft elbows", "Reset your body into a straight line before the next rep"], avoid: "Landing with locked arms, which can jam your wrists." },
  { name: "Knee Push-Ups", category: "Chest", aka: ["Kneeling Push-Ups"], tips: ["Kneel with your hands just wider than your shoulders", "Keep a straight line from your head to your knees", "Lower your chest to a fist from the floor with your elbows about 45 degrees out", "Press up and squeeze your chest at the top"], avoid: "Sitting your hips back toward your heels." },
  { name: "Ring Push-Ups", category: "Chest", aka: ["Suspension Push-Ups", "TRX Push-Ups"], tips: ["Set the rings low and brace your whole body from head to toes", "Keep the rings close to your ribs and turn them slightly out at the top", "Lower your chest between the rings with control", "Press up and squeeze your chest at the top"], avoid: "Letting the rings wobble wide, which strains your shoulders." },

  // --- BACK (LATS, RHOMBOIDS, LOWER BACK) ---
  { name: "Deadlift", category: "Back", aka: ["Barbell Deadlift", "Conventional Barbell Deadlift", "Conventional Deadlift", "Heavy Conventional Deadlifts"], tips: ["Stand with the bar over your mid-foot, feet about hip width, and grip just outside your legs", "Take the slack out of the bar, chest up, lats tight, back flat", "Push the floor away and keep the bar dragging close to your legs", "Stand tall by squeezing your glutes, then lower the bar the same way"], avoid: "Rounding your lower back or jerking the bar off the floor." },
  { name: "Sumo Deadlift", category: "Back", aka: ["Sumo Barbell Deadlift"], tips: ["Take a wide stance with toes turned out and grip the bar inside your knees", "Push your knees out over your toes and keep your chest up", "Drive the floor apart and pull the slack out before the bar moves", "Stand tall with your hips through and lock out with your glutes"], avoid: "Letting your hips shoot up first so the lift turns into a back-heavy pull." },
  { name: "Trap Bar Deadlift", category: "Back", aka: ["Trap Bar Deadlift (Hex Bar)", "Hex Bar Deadlift"], tips: ["Stand in the center of the bar with your feet hip width and grip the handles", "Sit your hips back, chest up, shoulders slightly above the handles", "Push through your whole foot and stand up with the bar even beside you", "Lower by hinging your hips and bending your knees together"], avoid: "Letting your knees cave in or rounding your back." },
  { name: "Deficit Barbell Deadlift", category: "Back", tips: ["Stand on a low plate or platform, about one to two inches, no more", "Hinge down and grip the bar with a flat back", "Pull the slack out and drive through your feet", "Keep the bar close and lock out with your hips"], avoid: "Standing on a platform so tall that your back rounds at the start." },
  { name: "Rack Pulls", category: "Back", aka: ["Rack Deadlifts", "Smith Machine Rack Deads"], tips: ["Set the bar in the rack at about knee height", "Brace your core and pull your shoulder blades back and down", "Drive your hips forward and stand tall with the bar close to your legs", "Squeeze your upper back at the top and lower under control"], avoid: "Leaning back hard at lockout or dropping the bar from the top." },
  { name: "Barbell Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Barbell Bent-Over Rows", "Bent-Over Barbell Row", "Bent-Over Row", "Bent Over Row", "Overhand Barbell Row", "Bent Lat Row", "Parallel Bent Over Barbell Row"], tips: ["Hinge forward with a flat back and your knees slightly bent, the bar hanging below your chest", "Brace your core and keep your torso still", "Pull the bar to your lower ribs, driving your elbows back", "Squeeze your shoulder blades, then lower the bar with control"], avoid: "Heaving the bar up with your hips and standing up with each rep." },
  { name: "Reverse-Grip Barbell Rows", category: "Back", aka: ["Reverse Grip Bent-Over Rows", "Reverse-Grip Bent-Over Barbell Row", "Underhand Barbell Row"], tips: ["Use an underhand shoulder-width grip and hinge forward with a flat back", "Keep your elbows close to your sides", "Pull the bar to your lower belly", "Lower slowly until your arms are straight and your lats are stretched"], avoid: "Letting your wrists curl and your biceps do all the work." },
  { name: "Pendlay Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Pendlay Rows"], tips: ["Start every rep with the bar on the floor and your back almost parallel to it", "Brace your core and keep your torso still", "Pull the bar explosively to your lower chest or upper stomach", "Lower it back to the floor and reset before the next rep"], avoid: "Bouncing the bar off the floor or standing up as you pull." },
  { name: "Yates Rows", category: "Back", tips: ["Stand more upright than a normal row, torso at about 30 to 45 degrees, with an underhand grip", "Brace your core and keep your elbows close to your body", "Pull the bar toward your belly button", "Lower under control and keep your back straight"], avoid: "Using so much weight that you jerk your whole body up." },
  { name: "T-Bar Row", category: "Back", aka: ["T-Bar Rows (Barbell Corner)", "Landmine Row", "Overhand Grip T Bar Row"], tips: ["Straddle the bar and hinge forward with a flat back", "Brace your core and keep your chest up", "Pull the handle toward your chest, driving your elbows back", "Squeeze your shoulder blades and lower slowly"], avoid: "Rounding your upper back as you lower the weight." },
  { name: "T-Bar Machine Rows (Chest Supported)", category: "Back", aka: ["Chest-Supported T-Bar Row"], tips: ["Set the chest pad so your arms can fully extend at the bottom", "Keep your chest on the pad and your shoulders down", "Pull the handles toward your lower ribs", "Pause with your shoulder blades squeezed, then lower slowly"], avoid: "Lifting your chest off the pad to move more weight." },
  { name: "Meadows Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Meadows Rows"], tips: ["Stand sideways to a landmine bar, hinge forward with one hand on your knee", "Grip the end of the bar with an overhand grip", "Pull your elbow high and back toward your hip", "Lower until your lat is fully stretched, then repeat"], avoid: "Twisting your torso open to swing the weight up." },
  { name: "Seal Rows (Cambered Bar/Bench)", category: "Back", tips: ["Lie face down on a bench high enough that the bar clears the floor", "Let your arms hang straight below you", "Pull the bar up to the bench, driving your elbows back", "Lower slowly and keep your chest on the bench"], avoid: "Lifting your chest or hips off the bench." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Single-Arm Dumbbell Rows", "Single-Arm Dumbbell Row", "One-Arm Dumbbell Row", "Single-Arm Dumbbell Arc Row", "One-Arm Dumbbell Bent-Over Row", "Neutral Grip Dumbbell Row", "Single Arm Bent Over Row Overhand Grip", "DB Single Arm Bent Over Rows"], tips: ["Put one hand and knee on a bench with a flat back and a braced core", "Let the dumbbell hang under your shoulder", "Pull your elbow toward your hip, keeping your upper arm close", "Lower until your lat is stretched without twisting your torso"], avoid: "Rotating your torso up to swing the dumbbell." },
  { name: "Chest-Supported Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Chest-Supported Dumbbell Rows", "Chest Supported Dumbbell Row on Incline Bench"], tips: ["Lie chest down on an incline bench with the dumbbells hanging", "Keep your head neutral and your shoulders down", "Pull your elbows back toward your hips", "Squeeze your upper back, then lower slowly"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders up to your ears." },
  { name: "Incline Dumbbell Row (Bilateral)", category: "Back", aka: ["Incline Dumbbell Row", "Incline Dumbbell Rows"], tips: ["Lie chest down on an incline bench with a dumbbell in each hand", "Let your arms hang straight, shoulder blades spread", "Row both dumbbells toward your hips, elbows close", "Pause, then lower slowly to a full stretch"], avoid: "Lifting your chest off the bench." },
  { name: "Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown", category: "Back", aka: ["Wide-Grip Pulldown", "Wide-Grip Pulldown HIIT 100's", "Wide-Grip Pulldown HIIT 100's (0s Rest)", "Overhand Grip Lat Pulldown", "Overhand Grip Machine Pulldowns"], tips: ["Grip the bar wider than your shoulders and secure your thighs under the pad", "Lean back slightly, chest up", "Pull the bar to your upper chest, driving your elbows down and back", "Let it rise slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Yanking the bar down with your body swinging." },
  { name: "Close-Grip Lat Pulldown", category: "Back", aka: ["Close-Grip Pulldown", "Close-Grip Front Lat Pulldown"], tips: ["Use a close grip with your palms facing forward", "Sit tall with your thighs locked under the pad", "Pull the bar to your upper chest, keeping your elbows close", "Stretch back up slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Leaning back too far and turning it into a row." },
  { name: "Reverse-Grip Lat Pulldown", category: "Back", aka: ["Reverse-Grip Pulldown", "Underhand Lat Pulldown", "Underhand Cable Pulldowns", "Reverse Grip Pulldown Machine", "Reverse Pulldown Machine"], tips: ["Use an underhand shoulder-width grip", "Sit tall with a slight lean back", "Pull the bar to your upper chest, keeping your elbows tucked", "Let it rise slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Letting your biceps do all the pulling instead of your lats." },
  { name: "Neutral-Grip (V-Bar) Lat Pulldown", category: "Back", aka: ["Neutral Grip Pull Down", "V-Bar Pull Down", "Neutral Grip Lat Pulldown", "Neutral Grip Pulldown"], tips: ["Grip the V-bar with your palms facing each other", "Lean back slightly and keep your chest up", "Pull the handle to your upper chest, elbows down and back", "Stretch up slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Leaning back and swinging the weight." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Cable Lat Pulldown", category: "Back", aka: ["One Arm Lat Pulldown"], tips: ["Sit or kneel facing the cable with one handle in one hand", "Start with your arm fully extended and your shoulder down", "Pull your elbow down toward your hip", "Let it rise slowly to a full stretch"], avoid: "Twisting your torso to pull the weight." },
  { name: "Straight-Arm Pulldown", category: "Back", aka: ["Straight-Arm Cable Pullover", "Cable Rope Straight Arm Pull Downs (FST-7)", "FST-7 Straight Arm Pull Down", "Rope Straight-Arm Pulldown", "Cable Rope Straight Arm Pull Down"], tips: ["Stand facing a high cable with your arms straight and a slight hip hinge", "Keep a slight bend in your elbows", "Sweep the bar down to your thighs using your lats", "Let it rise slowly until you feel a stretch under your armpits"], avoid: "Bending your elbows and turning it into a triceps pushdown." },
  { name: "Seated Cable Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Cable Seated Rows (V-Bar)", "Seated pulley row", "Cable Row"], tips: ["Sit tall with your knees slightly bent and your chest up", "Pull the handle to your lower ribs, driving your elbows back", "Squeeze your shoulder blades together", "Let the handle return slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Rocking your torso back and forth to move the weight." },
  { name: "Cable Seated Rows (Wide Bar)", category: "Back", aka: ["Wide Grip Cable Rows", "Low Cable Row (Wide Bar, Palms Facing)", "Wide Grip Seated Cable Row"], tips: ["Sit tall with your feet braced and grip the wide bar", "Pull the bar to your upper stomach with your elbows out", "Squeeze your upper back and keep your chest up", "Return slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders up as you pull." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Cable Seated Rows", category: "Back", aka: ["Overhand Grip Unilateral High Pulley Row"], tips: ["Sit tall, one hand on the handle and your free hand on your thigh", "Pull your elbow past your torso toward your hip", "Keep your shoulders square and your torso still", "Return slowly to a full stretch"], avoid: "Rotating your torso toward the working arm." },
  { name: "Iso-Lateral Plate-Loaded High Row (Hammer Strength)", category: "Back", aka: ["Hammer Strength High Row"], tips: ["Set the seat so your hands start about shoulder height", "Brace your chest against the pad", "Pull the handles down and back toward your lower ribs", "Return slowly until your lats are stretched"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders and letting one side lead." },
  { name: "Hammer Strength Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Iso-Lateral Plate-Loaded Mid Row", "Leverage Iso Row"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so your chest sits snugly against the pad", "Grip the handles and sit tall", "Pull your elbows back past your torso", "Pause and squeeze your shoulder blades, then return slowly"], avoid: "Leaning back to get the weight moving." },
  { name: "Iso-Lateral Plate-Loaded Low Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Hammer Strength Low Row"], tips: ["Sit with your chest on the pad and your feet planted", "Start with your arms fully extended", "Pull the handles toward your hips with your elbows close", "Squeeze your lats, then return slowly"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders roll forward as you return." },
  { name: "Iso-Lateral Plate-Loaded Front Lat Pulldown", category: "Back", tips: ["Adjust the seat so you can reach the handles with your arms fully extended", "Sit tall with your thighs under the pad", "Pull each handle down toward your shoulders", "Return slowly until your lats are stretched"], avoid: "Using one arm harder than the other, since each side moves on its own." },
  { name: "Diverging Seated Row Machine (Selectorized)", category: "Back", tips: ["Adjust the chest pad so your arms reach the handles fully extended", "Sit tall and pull the handles back along a wide arc", "Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the end", "Return slowly until your upper back is stretched"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders round forward at the start." },
  { name: "Machine Pullover (Nautilus/Plate-Loaded)", category: "Back", tips: ["Adjust the seat so your shoulders line up with the machine's pivot", "Place your elbows on the pads and start with the arms stretched back", "Pull the bar down toward your hips using your lats", "Return slowly to a full lat stretch"], avoid: "Pushing the bar with your hands instead of driving with your elbows." },
  { name: "Pull-Ups", category: "Back", aka: ["Pull-Ups (Pronated Grip)"], tips: ["Hang from the bar with your hands just wider than your shoulders and your shoulder blades pulled down", "Brace your core and keep your legs still", "Pull your chest toward the bar, driving your elbows down and back", "Lower fully until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Kipping or swinging to reach the top." },
  { name: "Weighted Pull-Ups", category: "Back", tips: ["Build up to 10 clean bodyweight reps before adding weight", "Hang with your shoulder blades down and the belt hanging steady", "Pull your chest toward the bar with your elbows driving down", "Lower fully with control to a straight-arm hang"], avoid: "Using partial reps just to handle more weight." },
  { name: "Machine Assisted Pull-Ups", category: "Back", tips: ["Set the weight so you can do all reps with a full range of motion", "Place your knees or feet on the pad and grip the handles", "Pull your chest toward the bar with your shoulders down", "Lower slowly until your arms are fully straight"], avoid: "Using so much assistance that the top and bottom range gets short." },
  { name: "Chin-Ups", category: "Back", aka: ["Chin-Ups (Supinated Grip)", "Wide-Grip Chin-Ups", "Wide Grip Chins", "Chin-Ups (Underhand Grip)"], tips: ["Grip the bar underhand, about shoulder width apart", "Hang with your shoulders down and your core braced", "Pull your chin over the bar, keeping your elbows close to your ribs", "Lower slowly to a full hang"], avoid: "Craning your neck up instead of pulling your chest to the bar." },
  { name: "Neutral-Grip Pull-Ups", category: "Back", aka: ["V-Bar Pullup", "Neutral Grip Chins"], tips: ["Grip the handles with your palms facing each other", "Start from a full hang with your shoulders down", "Pull your chest toward your hands, elbows close to your sides", "Lower slowly and fully"], avoid: "Kicking your legs to get over the bar." },
  { name: "Good Mornings", category: "Back", aka: ["Barbell Good Mornings"], tips: ["Set the bar low on your upper back, feet about shoulder width", "Brace your core and keep a slight bend in your knees", "Push your hips back until your torso is near parallel to the floor", "Squeeze your glutes and drive your hips forward to stand"], avoid: "Rounding your lower back or going heavy before your technique is solid." },
  { name: "Seated Good Mornings", category: "Back", tips: ["Sit on a bench with the bar on your upper back and your feet flat", "Brace your core and keep your chest up", "Hinge forward from your hips until your torso is near parallel", "Drive your torso back up while squeezing your glutes"], avoid: "Rounding your back forward to go deeper." },
  { name: "Back Extensions", category: "Back", aka: ["Back Extensions (45-Degree Hyperextensions)", "Hyperextensions", "Back Extension"], tips: ["Set the pad so it sits just below your hip bones and hook your heels in", "Cross your arms over your chest and keep your neck neutral", "Lower your torso with a flat back", "Lift until your body forms a straight line and squeeze your glutes"], avoid: "Hyperextending your lower back at the top." },
  { name: "Weighted Back Extensions", category: "Back", tips: ["Hold a plate against your chest or behind your head", "Hinge forward with a flat back until you feel a hamstring stretch", "Drive your hips into the pad and rise until your body is straight", "Squeeze your glutes at the top without arching"], avoid: "Swinging up fast with the weight." },
  { name: "Reverse Hyperextensions", category: "Back", tips: ["Lie face down on the pad with your hips at the edge and hold the handles", "Let your legs hang and brace your core", "Lift your legs up until they are in line with your body", "Lower slowly and keep tension without swinging"], avoid: "Swinging your legs with momentum or throwing your lower back into an arch." },
  { name: "Lat Pulldown", category: "Back", aka: ["Lat Pulldown (warm-up)", "Overhand Pull Down", "Machine Pulldown", "Pull-Downs"], tips: ["Sit with your thighs snug under the pad and grip the bar just outside your shoulders", "Lean back slightly and lift your chest", "Pull the bar to your upper chest, driving your elbows down", "Let the bar rise slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Pulling the bar behind your neck or swinging your body." },
  { name: "Machine Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Bent Over Machine Row", "Seated Machine Low Pulley Row", "Seated Machine Row", "Reverse Grip Machine Row"], tips: ["Adjust the seat and chest pad so you can reach the handles with your arms straight", "Sit tall and pull the handles toward your lower ribs", "Squeeze your shoulder blades together", "Return slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Leaning back to help the pull." },
  // more (added in 2.6.5)
  { name: "Helms Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Incline Bench Landmine Row"], tips: ["Lie chest down on an incline bench with the dumbbells hanging", "Pull your elbows out and up so your upper arms are at about 45 degrees", "Squeeze your upper back at the top", "Lower slowly to a full stretch"], avoid: "Lifting your chest off the bench." },
  { name: "Kroc Rows", category: "Back", aka: ["Heavy Dumbbell Rows"], tips: ["Brace one hand on a bench or rack and hold a heavy dumbbell", "Keep your back flat and use a slight body English only at the top", "Pull the dumbbell to your hip for high reps", "Lower to a full stretch with control"], avoid: "Turning it into a heavy swinging jerk with a rounded back." },
  { name: "Gorilla Rows", category: "Back", tips: ["Set two kettlebells or dumbbells between your feet in a wide stance", "Hinge forward with a flat back and your core braced", "Row one weight at a time to your hip while the other stays on the floor", "Lower it to the floor under control and switch"], avoid: "Twisting your torso up to yank the weight." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Machine Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Unilateral Machine Row", "Unilateral Hammer Rows"], tips: ["Sit tall with your chest against the pad", "Grip one handle and start with your arm extended", "Pull your elbow past your torso toward your hip", "Return slowly and keep your shoulders square"], avoid: "Twisting your torso toward the working arm." },
  { name: "Underhand Seated Cable Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Reverse-Grip Seated Cable Row", "Reverse Grip Cable Row", "Seated Cable Row (Underhand Grip)"], tips: ["Sit tall with an underhand grip on the bar or V-handle", "Pull the handle to your lower belly, elbows brushing your sides", "Squeeze your lats and shoulder blades", "Return slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Leaning back too far during the pull." },
  { name: "Close-Grip Pull-Ups", category: "Back", tips: ["Grip the bar with your hands about shoulder width or closer", "Start from a full hang with your shoulders down", "Pull your chest toward the bar, elbows close to your body", "Lower slowly to a full hang"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders roll forward at the top." },
  { name: "Wide-Grip Pull-Ups", category: "Back", tips: ["Grip the bar wider than your shoulders and hang with your shoulder blades down", "Brace your core and keep your legs still", "Pull your elbows down and out until your chin clears the bar", "Lower slowly to a straight-arm hang"], avoid: "Using a grip so wide that you only move halfway." },
  { name: "Weighted Chin-Ups", category: "Back", tips: ["Master your bodyweight chin-ups first, then add weight in small steps", "Hang with an underhand shoulder-width grip and shoulders down", "Pull your chin over the bar, elbows close to your ribs", "Lower to a full hang without swinging"], avoid: "Cutting the bottom short so you hang halfway." },
  { name: "Assisted Chin-Ups", category: "Back", aka: ["Machine Assisted Chin-Ups"], tips: ["Choose a band or machine setting that lets you finish every rep with good form", "Grip underhand, shoulder width, and start from a full hang", "Pull your chin over the bar with your elbows in close", "Lower slowly to a full hang"], avoid: "Letting the band or machine do the pull and skipping the bottom stretch." },
  { name: "Archer Pull-Ups", category: "Back", tips: ["Grip the bar wide and master wide pull-ups first", "Pull toward one hand while the other arm stays long", "Keep your core tight and your legs still", "Lower slowly and alternate sides"], avoid: "Bending both arms equally, which loses the one-arm emphasis." },
  { name: "Negative Pull-Ups", category: "Back", aka: ["Eccentric Pull-Ups"], tips: ["Jump or step up so your chin is over the bar", "Lower yourself slowly over 3 to 5 seconds", "Keep your core braced and shoulders down", "Go all the way down to a straight-arm hang, then reset"], avoid: "Dropping fast through the bottom of the rep." },
  { name: "Commando Pull-Ups", category: "Back", tips: ["Grip the bar with one hand in front of the other, standing sideways to it", "Pull your head to one side of the bar", "Keep your core tight and your legs still", "Lower with control and alternate which side your head goes"], avoid: "Swinging your body to get over the bar." },
  { name: "Scapular Pull-Ups", category: "Back", tips: ["Hang from the bar with straight arms", "Pull your shoulder blades down and back without bending your elbows", "Your body rises a few inches", "Lower slowly back to a full hang"], avoid: "Bending your arms so it turns into a regular pull-up." },
  { name: "Ring Rows", category: "Back", aka: ["Suspension Rows", "TRX Rows"], tips: ["Set the rings at about waist height and lean back with straight arms", "Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels", "Pull your chest to the rings, driving your elbows back", "Lower slowly to full arm extension"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag as you pull." },
  { name: "Superman", category: "Back", aka: ["Superman Holds"], tips: ["Lie face down with your arms and legs extended", "Lift your arms, chest and legs a few inches off the floor together", "Squeeze your glutes and upper back for a second", "Lower slowly and keep your neck neutral"], avoid: "Cranking your neck back or arching your lower back hard." },
  { name: "Snatch-Grip Deadlift", category: "Back", tips: ["Take a very wide grip on the bar and use lighter weight than a regular deadlift", "Sit your hips down and keep your chest up", "Drive through your feet and keep the bar close", "Stand tall and lower under control"], avoid: "Rounding your upper back because the wide grip makes you start lower." },

  // --- LEGS (QUADS, HAMSTRINGS, GLUTES, CALVES) ---
  { name: "Barbell High-Bar Back Squat", category: "Legs", tips: ["Rest the bar on your upper traps, hands just outside your shoulders, elbows down", "Set your feet about shoulder width, toes slightly out", "Sit straight down between your hips, knees tracking over your toes", "Drive up through your whole foot and keep your chest up"], avoid: "Letting your knees cave in or your heels lift off the floor." },
  { name: "Barbell Low-Bar Back Squat", category: "Legs", tips: ["Set the bar low across your rear delts and pull your elbows back and down", "Take a slightly wider stance and push your hips back first", "Lean your torso forward a bit while keeping your back flat", "Drive up through your mid-foot, hips and chest rising together"], avoid: "Letting your hips shoot up first so the lift turns into a good morning." },
  { name: "Front Squat", category: "Legs", aka: ["Barbell Front Squat"], tips: ["Rest the bar on your front delts with your elbows high, in a clean grip or crossed arms", "Keep your chest up and your elbows pointing forward", "Sit straight down and keep your torso upright", "Drive up and keep your elbows high the whole time"], avoid: "Letting your elbows drop, which makes the bar roll forward." },
  { name: "Safety Squat Bar (SSB) Squats", category: "Legs", tips: ["Settle the pads on your shoulders and hold the handles in front", "Brace your core and keep your chest up against the forward pull", "Sit straight down with your knees tracking over your toes", "Drive up and keep your upper back tight"], avoid: "Letting the bar pull you into a round-backed forward lean." },
  { name: "Zercher Squats", category: "Legs", tips: ["Hold the bar in the crooks of your elbows against your stomach, arms crossed", "Keep your chest up and your elbows in tight", "Squat down between your knees", "Drive up and keep the bar close to your body"], avoid: "Letting your torso fold forward as you rise." },
  { name: "Box Squats", category: "Legs", tips: ["Set the box at about parallel height and stand a little wider than usual", "Sit your hips back until you touch the box and stay tight", "Pause briefly without relaxing or rocking back", "Drive your feet through the floor to stand"], avoid: "Dropping onto the box and relaxing your whole body." },
  { name: "Goblet Squats", category: "Legs", aka: ["Dumbbell Goblet Squats"], tips: ["Hold a dumbbell against your chest with both hands", "Stand about shoulder width with your toes slightly out", "Sit straight down between your knees, elbows inside your knees", "Drive up and keep your chest tall"], avoid: "Letting your chest cave forward as you go down." },
  { name: "Kettlebell Goblet Squats", category: "Legs", tips: ["Hold the kettlebell by the horns against your chest", "Keep your elbows pointing down and your chest up", "Sit straight down between your hips", "Drive through your heels and midfoot to stand"], avoid: "Letting the bell pull your shoulders forward." },
  { name: "Heel-Elevated Goblet Squats (Cyclist Squats)", category: "Legs", aka: ["Heels Elevated Dumbbell Squat"], tips: ["Put your heels on a small plate or wedge and hold a weight at your chest", "Keep a narrow stance and your torso upright", "Let your knees travel far forward over your toes", "Drive up and squeeze your quads at the top"], avoid: "Using a heel lift so high that your knees feel pinched." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Squats", category: "Legs", aka: ["Smith Machine Squats (Close Stance)"], tips: ["Place your feet slightly in front of the bar so you can sit back", "Set the bar on your upper traps and unhook", "Squat down with your knees tracking over your toes", "Drive up and re-hook the bar when you are done"], avoid: "Putting your feet directly under the bar, which strains your knees." },
  { name: "Bulgarian Split Squats", category: "Legs", aka: ["Bulgarian Split Squats (Dumbbell)"], tips: ["Put your back foot on a bench and step your front foot far enough forward", "Keep your torso tall and your front knee tracking over your toes", "Lower until your front thigh is about parallel", "Drive up through your front heel and mid-foot"], avoid: "Placing your front foot too close so your knee shoots forward." },
  { name: "Bulgarian Split Squats (Barbell)", category: "Legs", tips: ["Place the bar on your upper back and your rear foot on a bench", "Keep your torso tall and your core braced", "Lower until your front thigh is about parallel", "Drive up through the front foot and keep the bar steady"], avoid: "Leaning forward and letting the bar shift." },
  { name: "Leg Press", category: "Legs", aka: ["Linear Leg Press (45-Degree)", "FST-7 Leg Press", "Parallel Leg Press", "Leg Press (Shoulder Width Stance)"], tips: ["Sit with your back and hips flat on the pad and your feet shoulder width on the platform", "Unlock the sled and lower until your knees are at about 90 degrees", "Push through your whole foot, not just your toes", "Stop short of locking out your knees"], avoid: "Letting your hips curl up off the pad at the bottom." },
  { name: "Horizontal Leg Press (Selectorized)", category: "Legs", tips: ["Adjust the seat so your knees are bent about 90 degrees at the start", "Keep your back and head on the pad", "Push the platform away until your legs are nearly straight", "Return slowly without letting the weights touch"], avoid: "Locking out your knees hard at the end." },
  { name: "Single-Leg Leg Press", category: "Legs", aka: ["Single-Leg Press", "One-Leg Leg Press", "Unilateral Leg Press"], tips: ["Place one foot in the middle of the platform and keep your hips flat", "Lower until your knee reaches about 90 degrees", "Push through your whole foot without letting your knee cave in", "Stop short of locking out"], avoid: "Letting your hips twist or lift off the pad." },
  { name: "Hack Squat", category: "Legs", aka: ["Hack Squat Machine (Linear/Rails)", "Machine Hack Squat"], tips: ["Stand on the platform with your back flat against the pad and feet slightly forward", "Lower slowly until your thighs reach about parallel or lower", "Keep your knees tracking over your toes", "Press through your whole foot to rise"], avoid: "Lifting your heels or letting your knees cave." },
  { name: "Hack Squat Machine (Pivot/Leverage)", category: "Legs", aka: ["Machine Squat Press"], tips: ["Set your shoulders under the pads and your feet shoulder width on the platform", "Release the safety and lower with control", "Keep your lower back against the pad", "Drive through your whole foot and stop just short of lockout"], avoid: "Letting your lower back peel off the pad at the bottom." },
  { name: "Pendulum Squat Machine", category: "Legs", aka: ["Pendulum Squat"], tips: ["Place your feet in the middle of the platform and your shoulders under the pads", "Lower with your knees tracking forward over your toes", "Go as deep as you can with a flat back against the pad", "Press up and keep tension on your quads"], avoid: "Locking out hard, which takes the load off your quads." },
  { name: "V-Squat Machine", category: "Legs", aka: ["V Squat"], tips: ["Place your shoulders under the pads and your feet shoulder width on the plate", "Brace your core and keep your chest up", "Lower until your thighs are at least parallel", "Drive up through your whole foot"], avoid: "Moving your feet so far forward that your hips tuck under." },
  { name: "Belt Squat Machine (Pit Shark)", category: "Legs", tips: ["Fasten the belt snugly around your hips", "Stand tall with your feet shoulder width", "Squat down while keeping your torso upright and your core braced", "Drive up through your whole foot"], avoid: "Leaning forward since the weight hangs from your hips." },
  { name: "Walking Lunges", category: "Legs", aka: ["Dumbbell Walking Lunges", "Barbell / Dumbbell Walking Lunges"], tips: ["Take a long stride and keep your torso upright", "Lower until your back knee almost touches the floor", "Push through your front heel and step through into the next lunge", "Keep your front knee tracking over your toes"], avoid: "Taking steps so short that your knee goes far past your toes." },
  { name: "Barbell Walking Lunges", category: "Legs", tips: ["Rest the bar on your upper back and brace your core", "Take a long step and lower your back knee toward the floor", "Push through your front foot and step forward", "Keep your torso tall the whole way"], avoid: "Letting the bar bounce or your torso tilt forward." },
  { name: "Reverse Lunges", category: "Legs", aka: ["Dumbbell Reverse Lunges"], tips: ["Stand tall, then step one foot straight back", "Lower until both knees are at about 90 degrees", "Keep your front knee over your ankle and your torso upright", "Push through your front heel to stand"], avoid: "Letting your front knee cave in or your heel lift." },
  { name: "Barbell Reverse Lunges", category: "Legs", tips: ["Rest the bar on your upper back and brace your core", "Step back and lower your back knee toward the floor", "Keep your front shin about vertical and your torso tall", "Drive through your front foot to stand and reset"], avoid: "Stepping back too short so your front knee travels too far forward." },
  { name: "Lunges", category: "Legs", aka: ["Forward Lunges", "Dumbbell Lunges"], tips: ["Stand tall and take a controlled step forward", "Lower until both knees are about 90 degrees", "Keep your front knee over your toes and your torso upright", "Push back to the start through your front heel"], avoid: "Letting your back knee slam into the floor." },
  { name: "Leg Extension", category: "Legs", aka: ["Leg Extension Machine", "Machine Leg Extension", "FST-7 Leg Extensions", "Leg Extension (Warm-Up)", "Leg Extensions (Light)", "Leg Extensions (Heavy)"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so your knees line up with the machine's pivot and the pad sits on your lower shins", "Hold the handles and keep your hips down", "Extend your legs until they are nearly straight and squeeze your quads", "Lower slowly without letting the stack rest"], avoid: "Swinging the weight up with momentum." },
  { name: "Single-Leg Extension Machine", category: "Legs", aka: ["Single Leg Leg Extensions", "Unilateral Leg Extension"], tips: ["Set the seat so your knee lines up with the pivot", "Place the pad on your lower shin and hold the handles", "Extend one leg fully and squeeze your quad", "Lower slowly and keep your hips on the seat"], avoid: "Lifting your hips or leaning back to extend." },
  { name: "Sissy Squats", category: "Legs", aka: ["Sissy Squats (Bodyweight)"], tips: ["Hold a post for balance and rise onto your toes", "Lean your whole body back as your knees travel forward", "Lower until you feel a strong quad stretch", "Return up by pushing your knees back and squeezing your quads"], avoid: "Doing deep reps on sore knees or going heavy too soon." },
  { name: "Sissy Squat Machine", category: "Legs", tips: ["Set the pad behind your calves and rise onto your toes", "Lean back as your knees travel forward", "Lower until your quads are stretched", "Return by pushing your knees back and squeezing your quads"], avoid: "Forcing a depth that hurts your knees." },
  { name: "Step-Ups", category: "Legs", aka: ["Dumbbell Step-Ups"], tips: ["Place your whole foot on a bench about knee height", "Drive up through your heel and keep your torso tall", "Stand fully on top, then lower back down slowly", "Finish your reps on one leg before switching"], avoid: "Pushing off the back foot instead of using your front leg." },
  { name: "Squat", category: "Legs", aka: ["Barbell Squat", "Barbell Back Squat", "Back Squat", "Squat HIIT 100's", "Squat HIIT 100's (0s Rest)"], tips: ["Stand about shoulder width with your toes turned slightly out", "Brace your core and sit down and back with your chest up", "Lower until your thighs are about parallel, knees over toes", "Drive up through your whole foot"], avoid: "Letting your knees collapse inward or your heels lift." },
  { name: "Romanian Deadlift (RDL)", category: "Legs", aka: ["Barbell RDL", "Romanian Deadlift"], tips: ["Stand holding the bar at your thighs, knees slightly bent", "Push your hips back and slide the bar down your legs", "Lower until you feel a strong hamstring stretch with a flat back", "Drive your hips forward to stand tall"], avoid: "Rounding your back or bending your knees to squat the weight." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Romanian Deadlift", category: "Legs", aka: ["Dumbbell RDL"], tips: ["Hold the dumbbells at your thighs with your knees slightly bent", "Push your hips back and let the dumbbells slide down your legs", "Lower to about mid-shin with a flat back", "Drive your hips forward and squeeze your glutes"], avoid: "Letting the dumbbells drift away from your legs." },
  { name: "Single-Leg RDL (Dumbbell/Kettlebell)", category: "Legs", tips: ["Stand on one leg with a soft knee and hold the weight in your opposite hand", "Hinge at your hips while your free leg extends behind you", "Keep your hips square and your back flat", "Return by driving your hips forward and squeezing your glute"], avoid: "Opening your hips to the side to reach lower." },
  { name: "Stiff-Legged Deadlift", category: "Legs", aka: ["Stiff-Legged Barbell Deadlift", "Straight Leg Deadlifts", "Straight-Leg Deadlifts", "Barbell Straight Leg Deadlift", "Stiff-Leg Deadlifts"], tips: ["Stand with your legs nearly straight, a slight knee bend, and grip the bar", "Push your hips back and lower the bar down your legs", "Lower until you feel a strong hamstring stretch", "Drive your hips forward to stand tall"], avoid: "Rounding your lower back to reach the floor." },
  { name: "Lying Leg Curls", category: "Legs", aka: ["Lying Leg Curl Machine", "FST-7 Lying Leg Curls", "Lying Hamstring Curls", "Lying Hamstring Curl"], tips: ["Lie face down with the pad just above your heels and your hips pressed into the bench", "Curl your heels toward your glutes", "Squeeze your hamstrings at the top", "Lower slowly until your legs are almost straight"], avoid: "Lifting your hips off the bench to curl more weight." },
  { name: "Seated Leg Curls", category: "Legs", aka: ["Seated Leg Curl Machine", "Seated Hamstring Curl", "FST-7 Seated Leg Curls"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so your knees line up with the pivot and the pad sits just above your heels", "Lock the thigh pad down snugly", "Curl your heels under the seat and squeeze your hamstrings", "Return slowly and stop just before the weights touch"], avoid: "Letting your hips rise off the seat." },
  { name: "Standing Leg Curls", category: "Legs", aka: ["Standing Single-Leg Curl Machine", "Standing Hamstring Curl", "Standing Single Leg Curl", "Standing Single Leg Hamstring Curl"], tips: ["Stand facing the machine with the pad above your heel", "Keep your hips square and your standing leg slightly bent", "Curl your heel toward your glute", "Let the pad return slowly until your leg is nearly straight"], avoid: "Leaning forward or swinging your leg up." },
  { name: "Kneeling Single-Leg Curl Machine", category: "Legs", tips: ["Kneel on the pad with the roller above your heel", "Brace your core so your hips stay still", "Curl your heel toward your glute", "Lower slowly until your leg is almost straight"], avoid: "Arching your lower back to curl more weight." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Leg Curls", category: "Legs", aka: ["Dumbbell Lying Leg Curls"], tips: ["Lie face down and squeeze a dumbbell between your feet", "Keep your hips pressed into the bench", "Curl the dumbbell toward your glutes", "Lower slowly without letting it drop"], avoid: "Using a weight so heavy it slips from your feet." },
  { name: "Glute-Ham Raise (GHR)", category: "Legs", tips: ["Set the pad so your hips hang just past the edge and lock your feet in", "Brace your core and keep your body straight", "Lower your torso until it is nearly parallel to the floor", "Curl your hamstrings to pull yourself back up"], avoid: "Bending at your waist instead of holding a straight line." },
  { name: "Nordic Hamstring Curls", category: "Legs", tips: ["Kneel on a pad with your ankles locked under something sturdy", "Keep your body straight from knees to head", "Lower yourself as slowly as you can, using your hamstrings", "Catch yourself with your hands and push back up"], avoid: "Folding at your hips, which skips the hamstrings." },
  { name: "Cable Pull-Throughs", category: "Legs", tips: ["Stand facing away from the low pulley, rope between your legs", "Hinge at your hips with a flat back and a slight knee bend", "Let the rope pass behind you and feel your hamstrings stretch", "Drive your hips forward and squeeze your glutes"], avoid: "Squatting down instead of pushing your hips back." },
  { name: "Kettlebell Swings", category: "Legs", aka: ["Kettlebell Swing"], tips: ["Stand wider than your shoulders with the bell in front of you", "Hike the bell back between your legs and keep your back flat", "Snap your hips forward so the bell floats to chest height", "Let it fall and hinge again, letting your hips do the work"], avoid: "Lifting the bell with your arms or squatting it." },
  { name: "Leg Curls", category: "Legs", aka: ["Hamstring Curl"], tips: ["Adjust the machine so the pad sits just above your heels", "Keep your hips down and your core braced", "Curl your heels toward your glutes and squeeze", "Return slowly until your legs are almost straight"], avoid: "Using momentum to swing the weight up." },
  { name: "Hip Thrusts", category: "Legs", aka: ["Barbell Hip Thrusts"], tips: ["Rest your upper back on a bench and roll the bar over your hips with a pad", "Plant your feet about hip width with your shins vertical at the top", "Drive through your heels and lift your hips until your body forms a straight line", "Squeeze your glutes at the top and lower under control"], avoid: "Overarching your lower back at the top." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Hip Thrusts", category: "Legs", tips: ["Rest your upper back on a bench with a dumbbell across your hips", "Plant your feet so your shins are vertical at the top", "Drive your hips up and squeeze your glutes", "Lower slowly and keep your chin tucked"], avoid: "Pushing through your toes so your hamstrings take over." },
  { name: "Single-Leg Hip Thrusts", category: "Legs", tips: ["Rest your upper back on a bench, one foot planted and the other leg lifted", "Drive through the planted heel and lift your hips level", "Squeeze your glute at the top", "Lower slowly without letting your hips twist"], avoid: "Letting your hips tilt to the side." },
  { name: "Machine Hip Thrusts", category: "Legs", aka: ["Glute Drive Machine (Plate-Loaded)"], tips: ["Adjust the machine so the pad sits across your hips", "Plant your feet shoulder width with your upper back supported", "Drive your hips up and squeeze your glutes", "Lower your hips slowly until the pad is almost at the floor"], avoid: "Arching your back to finish the rep." },
  { name: "Barbell Glute Bridges", category: "Legs", tips: ["Lie on the floor with your knees bent and the bar over your hips", "Plant your feet hip width", "Drive through your heels to lift your hips until your body is straight", "Squeeze at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Overarching your lower back at the top." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Glute Bridges", category: "Legs", tips: ["Lie on the floor with your knees bent and a dumbbell on your hips", "Plant your feet about hip width", "Lift your hips by driving through your heels", "Squeeze your glutes at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Letting your knees cave inward." },
  { name: "Cable Glute Kickbacks", category: "Legs", tips: ["Attach an ankle cuff to a low pulley and hold the frame for balance", "Hinge forward slightly with a flat back", "Kick your leg back and squeeze your glute at the top", "Return slowly without letting the weight rest"], avoid: "Arching your lower back to get your leg higher." },
  { name: "Standing Machine Glute Kickbacks", category: "Legs", tips: ["Brace your chest against the pad and place your foot on the platform", "Keep your core tight and your hips square", "Press your leg back and squeeze your glute", "Return slowly without letting the weight crash"], avoid: "Swinging your torso to move the weight." },
  { name: "Multi-Hip Machine (Extension)", category: "Legs", tips: ["Adjust the pad so it sits behind your thigh above the knee", "Hold the handles and brace your core", "Extend your leg back and squeeze your glute", "Return slowly and keep your hips steady"], avoid: "Rotating your hips to get your leg higher." },
  { name: "Hip Abductor Machine", category: "Legs", aka: ["Seated Hip Abductor Machine (Outer Thigh)"], tips: ["Sit tall with your back against the pad and your knees against the pads", "Push your knees apart and squeeze your outer hips", "Pause for a second at the widest point", "Return slowly and keep control"], avoid: "Using momentum to swing the knees out." },
  { name: "Hip Adductor Machine", category: "Legs", aka: ["Seated Hip Adductor Machine (Inner Thigh)"], tips: ["Sit tall with your back on the pad and your legs inside the pads", "Squeeze your legs together using your inner thighs", "Pause briefly at the closed position", "Return slowly without letting the weights slam"], avoid: "Setting the starting stretch so wide that your groin feels strained." },
  { name: "Cable Hip Abductions", category: "Legs", tips: ["Attach an ankle cuff to a low pulley and stand sideways to the cable stack", "Hold the frame for balance and keep your torso upright", "Lift your outside leg out to the side, leading with your heel", "Lower slowly and keep your hips square"], avoid: "Leaning your torso away to swing the leg higher." },
  { name: "Deficit Reverse Lunges", category: "Legs", tips: ["Stand on a low platform with your front foot elevated", "Step back and lower your back knee toward the floor", "Keep your torso upright and your front knee over your toes", "Push through your front heel to stand"], avoid: "Using a platform so high that your front knee feels pinched." },
  { name: "Curtsy Lunges", category: "Legs", tips: ["Stand tall and step one foot back and across behind the other", "Lower until your front thigh is about parallel", "Keep your front knee over your toes and hips square", "Push through your front heel to stand"], avoid: "Letting your front knee cave inward." },
  { name: "B-Stance RDLs", category: "Legs", tips: ["Stand with one foot slightly behind, the back foot on the ball of the toes", "Hinge your hips back, with most of the weight on your front leg", "Lower with a flat back until you feel a hamstring stretch", "Drive your hips forward to stand tall"], avoid: "Pushing off the back foot so much that it becomes a two-leg RDL." },
  { name: "Glute Bridges", category: "Legs", aka: ["Glute Bridge"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent and your feet flat, hip width apart", "Press through your heels and lift your hips", "Squeeze your glutes at the top without arching", "Lower slowly and repeat"], avoid: "Pushing through your toes so your hamstrings cramp." },
  { name: "Glute Kickbacks", category: "Legs", tips: ["Get on your hands and knees with your core braced", "Keep your knee bent or straight and kick your leg back toward the ceiling", "Squeeze your glute at the top", "Lower slowly without letting your lower back arch"], avoid: "Swinging your leg so high that your back arches." },
  { name: "Standing Barbell Calf Raises", category: "Legs", tips: ["Rest the bar on your upper back and balance with the balls of your feet on a block", "Lower your heels until you feel a calf stretch", "Rise as high as you can on your toes", "Pause at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Bouncing at the bottom instead of pausing." },
  { name: "Standing Dumbbell Calf Raises", category: "Legs", tips: ["Hold dumbbells at your sides and stand with the balls of your feet on a step", "Lower your heels until you feel a stretch", "Rise as high as you can on your toes", "Pause at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Bending your knees to help the lift." },
  { name: "Standing Calf Raises", category: "Legs", aka: ["Standing Calf Raise Machine", "Standing Calf Press", "FST-7 Standing Calf Raises", "Standing Calf Raise HIIT 100's", "Standing Calf Raise HIIT 100's (0s Rest)"], tips: ["Stand with the pads on your shoulders and the balls of your feet on the platform", "Lower your heels for a deep stretch", "Rise up and squeeze your calves hard", "Pause at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Bouncing off the bottom without a pause." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Calf Raises", category: "Legs", tips: ["Set the bar on your upper back and balls of your feet on a block under the bar", "Lower your heels until you feel a stretch", "Rise up high on your toes", "Pause at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Letting your feet drift too far forward." },
  { name: "Seated Calf Raises", category: "Legs", aka: ["Seated Calf Raise Machine", "Seated Calf Press", "FST-7 Seated Calf Raise"], tips: ["Sit with the pad on your thighs and the balls of your feet on the platform", "Lower your heels for a deep stretch", "Press up as high as you can", "Pause at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Rushing the reps and cutting the stretch short." },
  { name: "Seated Dumbbell Calf Raises", category: "Legs", tips: ["Sit on a bench with a dumbbell across your thighs and the balls of your feet on a block", "Lower your heels until you feel a stretch", "Press up as high as you can", "Pause at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Letting the dumbbell slide off your knees." },
  { name: "Leg Press Calf Raises", category: "Legs", aka: ["Calf Press", "Calf Press On The Leg Press Machine", "Straight Legged Calf Press"], tips: ["Sit in the leg press with your toes on the lower edge of the platform", "Keep your legs almost straight, knees unlocked", "Lower your heels for a stretch, then press up on your toes", "Pause at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Locking your knees hard or letting the platform slip off your feet." },
  { name: "Donkey Calf Raises", category: "Legs", aka: ["Donkey Calf Raise Machine", "Donkey or Leg Press Calf Raise", "Donkey Calf Press", "Donkey Press"], tips: ["Hinge forward with your hips supported and the balls of your feet on a block", "Keep your knees straight and your back flat", "Lower your heels for a deep stretch", "Rise on your toes and pause at the top"], avoid: "Bending your knees to bounce the weight up." },
  { name: "Rotary Calf Machine", category: "Legs", tips: ["Set the seat so your knees are slightly bent and the balls of your feet are on the pedals", "Lower your heels until you feel a stretch", "Press up and squeeze your calves", "Pause at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Letting the weight stack slam on each rep." },
  { name: "Single-Leg Calf Raises", category: "Legs", aka: ["Single-Leg Calf Press", "One-Leg Standing Calf Raise"], tips: ["Stand on one foot on a step with the heel hanging off", "Hold a rail for balance", "Lower your heel for a deep stretch", "Rise as high as you can and pause"], avoid: "Bouncing at the bottom or bending the knee." },
  { name: "Tibialis Raises", category: "Legs", tips: ["Stand with your back against a wall and your heels a foot away", "Keep your legs straight and lift your toes toward your shins", "Pause at the top and squeeze the front of your shins", "Lower slowly"], avoid: "Bending your knees or rushing the reps." },
  { name: "Calf Raises", category: "Legs", tips: ["Stand with the balls of your feet on a step", "Lower your heels until you feel a calf stretch", "Rise up on your toes as high as you can", "Pause at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Bouncing instead of pausing at the bottom." },
  // more (added in 2.6.5)
  { name: "Split Squats", category: "Legs", aka: ["Static Lunges", "Split Squat with Barbell Plate"], tips: ["Take a long stance with your back heel up and your torso upright", "Lower until your front thigh is about parallel", "Keep your front knee over your toes", "Drive up through your front heel and stay in the same stance"], avoid: "Stepping too short so your knee shoots over your toes." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Split Squats", category: "Legs", aka: ["Bulgarian Split Squats on Smith Machine"], tips: ["Set the bar on your upper back and take a long stance", "Keep your torso upright and your front foot flat", "Lower your back knee toward the floor", "Drive up through your front heel"], avoid: "Letting your front knee travel far past your toes." },
  { name: "Bodyweight Squats", category: "Legs", aka: ["Air Squats"], tips: ["Stand about shoulder width with your toes slightly out", "Reach your arms forward for balance", "Sit down and back until your thighs are about parallel", "Drive up through your whole foot"], avoid: "Letting your knees fall inward." },
  { name: "Pause Squats", category: "Legs", tips: ["Squat down with your normal technique and hold the bottom for 2 to 3 seconds", "Stay tight in the hole without relaxing", "Keep your chest up and your knees tracking over your toes", "Drive up out of the bottom without bouncing"], avoid: "Relaxing your back during the pause." },
  { name: "Jump Squats", category: "Legs", tips: ["Stand shoulder width and squat down to about parallel", "Explode upward and jump as high as you can", "Land softly on the balls of your feet and absorb with your knees", "Reset your stance before the next rep"], avoid: "Landing stiff-legged or letting your knees cave." },
  { name: "Pistol Squats", category: "Legs", aka: ["Single-Leg Squats"], tips: ["Stand on one leg with the other leg extended in front", "Reach your arms forward for balance", "Lower as deep as you can with your heel flat", "Drive up through your heel to stand"], avoid: "Letting your knee cave inward or your heel come off the floor." },
  { name: "Cossack Squats", category: "Legs", tips: ["Take a wide stance with your toes turned slightly out", "Shift your weight to one side and squat deep over that leg", "Keep your other leg straight with your toes up", "Drive back to the middle and switch sides"], avoid: "Letting your heel lift or your knee collapse inward." },
  { name: "Jefferson Squats", category: "Legs", tips: ["Straddle a barbell with one foot in front and one behind, hands gripping the bar", "Keep your chest up and your torso tall", "Squat down while the bar hangs between your legs", "Drive up through both feet and switch your stance each set"], avoid: "Twisting your hips so your torso turns." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Sumo Squats", category: "Legs", aka: ["Sumo Squats"], tips: ["Stand with a wide stance and your toes turned out, holding one dumbbell between your legs", "Keep your chest up and your back flat", "Squat down with your knees tracking over your toes", "Drive up and squeeze your glutes at the top"], avoid: "Letting your knees fall inward." },
  { name: "Narrow-Stance Leg Press", category: "Legs", tips: ["Place your feet close together in the middle of the platform", "Lower until your knees are at about 90 degrees", "Push through your whole foot", "Stop short of locking out your knees"], avoid: "Letting your hips curl up off the pad." },
  { name: "Wide-Stance Leg Press", category: "Legs", aka: ["Squat Press Legs Wide"], tips: ["Place your feet wider than your shoulders and toes slightly out", "Lower until your knees are at about 90 degrees", "Push through your whole foot and keep your knees over your toes", "Stop short of locking out your knees"], avoid: "Letting your knees collapse inward." },
  { name: "Wall Sit", category: "Legs", aka: ["Wall Sits"], tips: ["Put your back flat against a wall and slide down until your thighs are parallel to the floor", "Keep your knees over your ankles, feet shoulder width", "Press your back into the wall and breathe steadily", "Hold for the full time and slide up when done"], avoid: "Resting your hands on your thighs." },
  { name: "Lateral Lunges", category: "Legs", aka: ["Side Lunges"], tips: ["Stand tall and take a big step out to one side", "Sit your hips back over that leg with the other leg straight", "Keep your chest up and your foot flat", "Push off and return to standing, then switch"], avoid: "Letting your heel come off the floor." },
  { name: "Jumping Lunges", category: "Legs", aka: ["Split Jumps"], tips: ["Start in a lunge and keep your torso upright", "Explode up and switch your legs in the air", "Land softly in the opposite lunge", "Keep your front knee over your toes"], avoid: "Landing stiff-legged or letting your knee cave." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Hip Thrusts", category: "Legs", tips: ["Sit on the floor with your upper back against a bench and the bar over your hips with a pad", "Plant your feet about hip width", "Drive your hips up and squeeze your glutes", "Lower slowly and re-hook the bar when done"], avoid: "Overarching your lower back." },
  { name: "Glute Frog Pumps", category: "Legs", aka: ["Frog Pumps"], tips: ["Lie on your back with the soles of your feet together and knees dropped out", "Keep your feet close to your hips", "Lift your hips and squeeze your glutes", "Lower slowly and repeat for high reps"], avoid: "Pushing with your lower back instead of your glutes." },
  { name: "Single-Leg Glute Bridges", category: "Legs", tips: ["Lie on your back with one foot flat and the other leg lifted", "Press through the planted heel and lift your hips level", "Squeeze your glute at the top", "Lower slowly and keep your hips square"], avoid: "Letting your hips twist or drop to one side." },
  { name: "Stability Ball Leg Curls", category: "Legs", aka: ["Swiss Ball Leg Curls"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your heels on a stability ball and lift your hips", "Keep your body in a straight line", "Curl the ball toward your glutes", "Roll back slowly without letting your hips drop"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag as you curl." },
  { name: "Slider Leg Curls", category: "Legs", aka: ["Sliding Leg Curls"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your heels on sliders and lift your hips", "Keep your body in a straight line from shoulders to knees", "Curl your heels toward your glutes", "Slide back slowly while keeping your hips up"], avoid: "Dropping your hips when you extend." },
  { name: "Cable Leg Curls", category: "Legs", tips: ["Attach an ankle cuff to a low pulley and face the cable stack", "Hold the frame for balance and keep your hips square", "Curl your heel toward your glute and squeeze", "Lower slowly without letting the weight rest"], avoid: "Leaning forward to curl the weight." },
  { name: "Cable Hip Adduction", category: "Legs", aka: ["Cable Hip Adductions"], tips: ["Attach an ankle cuff to a low pulley and stand sideways to it", "Hold the frame for balance and keep your torso upright", "Pull your working leg across in front of your standing leg", "Return slowly without swinging"], avoid: "Using momentum to swing your leg across." },

  // --- SHOULDERS (DELTOIDS) ---
  { name: "Overhead Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Standing Overhead Barbell Press (Military Press)", "Military Press", "Barbell Shoulder Press", "OHP", "Standing Barbell Press", "Strict Press", "Standing Military Press", "Standing Barbell Overhead Press"], tips: ["Grip the bar just outside your shoulders and rest it on your front delts", "Squeeze your glutes and brace your core so you don't lean back", "Press the bar straight up and move your head through once it passes your forehead", "Lock out with the bar over your mid-foot, then lower to your collarbone"], avoid: "Leaning back and turning the press into an incline press." },
  { name: "Seated Barbell Overhead Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Seated Military Press", "Seated Barbell Military Press"], tips: ["Sit with your back against the pad and your feet planted", "Grip the bar just outside shoulder width", "Press straight up and pull your head slightly back out of the way", "Lower the bar to your upper chest or chin with control"], avoid: "Arching your lower back off the pad." },
  { name: "Behind-The-Neck Barbell Press", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Only do this if your shoulders move well, and use a light weight", "Grip the bar wider than your shoulders and sit tall", "Lower the bar to ear level behind your head, no lower", "Press straight up until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Dropping the bar to the base of your neck, which strains your shoulders." },
  { name: "Push Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Barbell Push Press"], tips: ["Hold the bar on your front delts with your elbows slightly in front", "Dip a few inches by bending your knees, keeping your torso upright", "Drive your legs up explosively and press the bar overhead", "Lock out, then lower the bar back to your shoulders and reset"], avoid: "Dipping so far that it becomes a squat." },
  { name: "Seated Dumbbell Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Seated Dumbbell Shoulder Press"], tips: ["Sit with your back supported and start with the dumbbells at your shoulders", "Keep your forearms vertical and your core braced", "Press up until your arms are nearly straight", "Lower to about ear level with control"], avoid: "Arching your back or letting the dumbbells drift forward." },
  { name: "Standing Dumbbell Shoulder Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Standing Dumbbell Press", "Alternating Dumbbell Shoulder Press (Standing)", "Standing DB Overhead Press (Palms Facing In)"], tips: ["Stand with your feet hip width and the dumbbells at your shoulders", "Squeeze your glutes and brace your core", "Press the dumbbells straight up and slightly together", "Lower to your shoulders with control"], avoid: "Leaning back to finish the press." },
  { name: "Arnold Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Arnold Dumbbell Press"], tips: ["Start with the dumbbells in front of your chest, palms facing you", "Press up while rotating your palms to face forward", "Finish with your arms straight above you", "Reverse the rotation slowly as you lower"], avoid: "Rushing the rotation or swinging the weights." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Dumbbell Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Dumbbell One-Arm Shoulder Press"], tips: ["Stand or sit tall with the dumbbell at your shoulder", "Brace your core so your torso stays upright", "Press the dumbbell straight overhead", "Lower to your shoulder under control"], avoid: "Leaning to the side as the weight goes up." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Overhead Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Smith Machine Shoulder Press"], tips: ["Set the bench so the bar lines up with your chin when you start", "Keep your back flat on the pad and feet planted", "Press the bar straight up until your arms are almost straight", "Lower to your chin and re-hook the bar when done"], avoid: "Pressing too far forward in front of your face." },
  { name: "Iso-Lateral Plate-Loaded Shoulder Press (Hammer Strength)", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Hammer Strength Shoulder Press"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so the handles start at shoulder height", "Sit tall with your back against the pad", "Press both handles up and in a little", "Lower slowly to shoulder height"], avoid: "Letting one arm lead while the other lags." },
  { name: "Machine Shoulder Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Converging Shoulder Press Machine (Selectorized)", "Machine Shoulder (Military) Press"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so the handles are at shoulder height", "Keep your back against the pad and your core braced", "Press up without locking your elbows", "Lower slowly until your hands are near your shoulders"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders up to your ears." },
  { name: "Multi-Press Shoulder Machine", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Set the seat and select the grip so the handles start at shoulder height", "Keep your back against the pad", "Press up and slightly together", "Lower with control and stop before the weights rest"], avoid: "Arching your back to press." },
  { name: "Lateral Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Dumbbell Lateral Raises", "Side Lateral Raise", "Standing Dumbbell Side Raise", "One-Arm Side Lateral Raise", "DB Lateral Reverse Drop Set", "FST-7 Standing Lateral Raises", "Standing Lateral Raises", "One-Arm Side Laterals", "Plate Side Raises", "Partial Side Raises", "Standing Side Raises", "Single Arm DB Lateral Raise", "DB Lateral Drop Sets"], tips: ["Hold light dumbbells at your sides with a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise your arms out to the sides until your hands reach shoulder height", "Lead with your elbows and keep your wrists neutral", "Lower slowly and don't swing"], avoid: "Using momentum or raising your shoulders up to your ears." },
  { name: "Seated Dumbbell Lateral Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Seated Side Lateral Raise", "Seated Lateral Raises", "Seated Side Raises Single Drop Set"], tips: ["Sit tall on a bench so your legs can't help", "Raise the dumbbells out to the sides to shoulder height", "Lead with your elbows and keep a soft bend", "Lower the dumbbells slowly to your sides without swinging"], avoid: "Leaning back to swing the weight up." },
  { name: "Leaning Dumbbell Lateral Raises", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Hold a post with one hand and lean away from it", "Let your free arm hang and raise it out to the side", "Lift until your hand is at shoulder height", "Lower slowly until you feel a stretch"], avoid: "Twisting your body to lift the weight." },
  { name: "Cable Lateral Raises", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Set the cable low and stand sideways to it, holding the handle with your far hand", "Keep a soft bend in your elbow", "Raise your arm out to your side to shoulder height", "Lower slowly against the constant tension"], avoid: "Shrugging or swinging your torso." },
  { name: "Machine Lateral Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Machine Lateral Raises (Selectorized)"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so your shoulders line up with the machine pivot", "Place your arms behind the pads and sit tall", "Raise your arms out to the sides to shoulder height", "Lower slowly without letting the weight rest"], avoid: "Raising past shoulder height with your shoulders hiked." },
  { name: "Barbell Front Raises", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Hold the bar at your thighs with an overhand grip and a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise the bar up to shoulder or eye level", "Keep your core braced and avoid leaning back", "Lower the bar back to your thighs in a controlled arc"], avoid: "Swinging the bar up with your hips." },
  { name: "Front Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Dumbbell Front Raises", "Alternating Deltoid Raise", "Full Frontal Raise", "Standing Front Raises", "DB Front Raise (Thumbs Up, Both Arms)"], tips: ["Hold dumbbells in front of your thighs with a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise one or both arms up to shoulder height", "Keep your torso still and your core braced", "Lower slowly and don't swing"], avoid: "Leaning back to lift the weights higher." },
  { name: "Cable Front Raises", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Face away from a low pulley and hold the handle between your legs", "Keep a soft bend in your elbow and your core braced", "Raise your arm up to shoulder height", "Lower slowly to keep tension on the cable"], avoid: "Leaning back as your arm rises." },
  { name: "Weight Plate Front Raises", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Hold a plate with both hands at the sides at 9 and 3 o'clock", "Raise the plate in front of you to about eye level", "Keep your arms nearly straight and your core braced", "Lower slowly and avoid swinging"], avoid: "Using your back to swing the plate up." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Reverse Flyes", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Dumbbell Reverse Flyes (Rear Delts)", "Bent-Over Rear Delt Raise", "Bent-Over Rear-Delt Raise", "Reverse Fly", "Neutral-Grip Reverse Fly", "Bent-Over Lateral Raise", "Dumbbell Rear Delt Raise", "Dumbbell Bent-Over Lateral Raise", "Rear Dumbbell Raises", "Rear Raises", "Bent Over Rear Delt Fly", "Bent Over Laterals"], tips: ["Hinge forward with a flat back and let the dumbbells hang", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise your arms out to the sides, leading with your elbows", "Squeeze your rear delts and lower slowly"], avoid: "Shrugging your traps and swinging the weight." },
  { name: "Chest-Supported Dumbbell Reverse Flyes", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Dumbbell Lying Rear-Delt Raise", "Incline Rear Delt Flyes", "Chest Supported Dumbbell Rear Raises", "Chest Supported Rear Dumbbell Raises"], tips: ["Lie chest down on an incline bench with a dumbbell in each hand", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise the weights out to the sides to shoulder height", "Squeeze your rear delts and lower slowly"], avoid: "Using too much weight so your traps take over." },
  { name: "Cable Rear Delt Flyes", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Bent Over Cable Rear-Delt Raise", "Bent Over Cable Lateral Raise", "Cable Rear Raises", "Cable Rear Delts", "Standing Cable Rear Raises", "Rear Cable Raises"], tips: ["Set the pulleys at shoulder height and cross the cables so each hand holds the opposite handle", "Step back and keep a soft bend in your elbows", "Pull your arms out and back in a wide arc", "Squeeze your rear delts and return slowly"], avoid: "Pulling with your arms bent into a row." },
  { name: "Reverse Pec Deck", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Reverse Pec Deck Machine (Rear Delts)", "Pec Dec Rear-Delt Fly", "Reverse Machine Flyes", "Machine Rear Delt Fly", "Machine Rear Delt Flye", "Machine Rear Raises"], tips: ["Sit facing the pad with your chest supported and your arms straight", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows", "Sweep your arms out and back to shoulder height", "Squeeze your rear delts and return slowly"], avoid: "Using your back to lean away from the pad." },
  { name: "Face Pulls", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Cable Face Pulls"], tips: ["Set the rope at head height and step back so your arms are straight", "Pull the rope toward your face, splitting your hands apart", "Squeeze your shoulder blades and rear delts, elbows high", "Return slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Leaning back and using your whole body to pull." },
  { name: "Barbell Upright Rows", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Hold the bar with a shoulder-width grip in front of your thighs", "Pull it up along your body, leading with your elbows", "Stop at about chest height", "Lower the bar back to your thighs in a smooth, controlled path"], avoid: "Pulling above chest height if your shoulders feel pinched." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Upright Rows", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Hold the dumbbells in front of your thighs", "Lead with your elbows and pull up along your body", "Stop at about chest height, elbows no higher than your hands", "Lower the dumbbells back to your thighs without dropping them"], avoid: "Shrugging so high that your shoulders pinch." },
  { name: "Cable Upright Rows", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Stand close to a low pulley with a straight bar or rope in front of your thighs", "Pull up along your body, leading with your elbows", "Stop at about chest height", "Lower slowly and keep constant tension"], avoid: "Swinging your torso back to help." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Upright Rows", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Smith Machine One-Arm Upright Row"], tips: ["Stand close to the bar and grip it shoulder width", "Lead with your elbows and pull the bar up along your body", "Stop at about chest height", "Lower the bar back to your thighs slowly along the track"], avoid: "Standing too far from the bar so you lean forward." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Shoulder Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Dumbbell Military Press", "Overhead Dumbbell Shoulder Press", "Dumbbell Shoulder Press HIIT 100's", "Dumbbell Shoulder Press HIIT 100's (0s Rest)"], tips: ["Sit or stand tall with the dumbbells at your shoulders", "Keep your core braced and your forearms vertical", "Press the weights up until your arms are nearly straight", "Lower to shoulder height with control"], avoid: "Flaring your elbows far behind your torso." },
  { name: "Rear Delt Flyes", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Hinge forward with a flat back and dumbbells hanging down", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise your arms out to the sides to shoulder height", "Squeeze and lower slowly"], avoid: "Using momentum or shrugging your traps." },
  { name: "Upright Rows", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Wide-Grip Upright Row", "Close-Grip Upright Row"], tips: ["Hold the weight in front of your thighs with an overhand grip", "Pull it up along your body, leading with your elbows", "Stop at about chest height", "Lower under control"], avoid: "Pulling so high that your shoulders feel pinched." },
  // more (added in 2.6.5)
  { name: "Landmine Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Single-Arm Landmine Press", "Landmine Incline Press"], tips: ["Set one end of the bar in a corner or landmine and hold the other at your shoulder", "Stand tall with your core braced", "Press the bar up and forward in an arc", "Lower slowly back to your shoulder"], avoid: "Leaning back or using your legs to push." },
  { name: "Z Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Seated Floor Press (Z Press)"], tips: ["Sit on the floor with your legs straight out in front of you", "Hold the bar at your shoulders with your core braced", "Press the bar straight overhead without leaning back", "Lower to your collarbone with control"], avoid: "Slouching or leaning back to finish the press." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Push Press", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Hold the dumbbells at your shoulders with your feet hip width", "Dip a few inches, keeping your torso upright", "Drive your legs up and press the dumbbells overhead", "Lower back to your shoulders and reset"], avoid: "Letting the dip turn into a squat." },
  { name: "Kettlebell Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Single-Arm Kettlebell Press"], tips: ["Hold the kettlebell in the rack position with your elbow tucked and your wrist straight", "Brace your core and squeeze your glutes", "Press the bell straight overhead, close to your head", "Lower it back to the rack under control"], avoid: "Letting the bell drift forward or bending your wrist back." },
  { name: "Pike Push-Ups", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Start in a push-up position with your hips high and your body in an inverted V", "Keep your head between your arms", "Lower your head toward the floor in front of your hands", "Press back up through your shoulders"], avoid: "Pushing your hips back so it becomes a regular push-up." },
  { name: "Handstand Push-Ups", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Wall Handstand Push-Ups"], tips: ["Kick up to a wall with your hands about shoulder width and your core braced", "Lower your head to the floor with control", "Keep your elbows at about 45 degrees", "Press up until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Arching your back or dropping fast on to your head." },
  { name: "Lu Raises", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Use very light dumbbells and stand tall", "Raise your arms out to the side and then overhead in a Y shape", "Keep your core braced and your elbows soft", "Lower slowly and avoid shrugging"], avoid: "Using weights so heavy that your traps take over." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Cable Lateral Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["One-Arm Cable Lateral Raise"], tips: ["Stand sideways to a low pulley with the handle in your far hand", "Keep a soft bend in your elbow", "Raise your arm out to the side to shoulder height", "Lower slowly and keep your torso still"], avoid: "Leaning your body to swing the cable up." },
  { name: "Cable Y-Raises", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Set the pulleys low and hold the handles", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise your arms up and out in a Y shape to about ear level", "Return your arms slowly to your sides so the cable stays tight"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders and arching your back." },
  { name: "Reverse Cable Crossovers", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Cable Reverse Flyes"], tips: ["Set both pulleys at shoulder height and cross the cables", "Hold the handles with a soft bend in your elbows", "Pull your arms out and back in a wide arc", "Squeeze your rear delts and return slowly"], avoid: "Pulling with your arms bent so it turns into a row." },
  { name: "Seated Rear Delt Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Seated Bent-Over Rear Delt Raises"], tips: ["Sit on a bench and lean forward with the dumbbells hanging behind your knees", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise your arms out to the sides to shoulder height", "Squeeze your rear delts and lower slowly"], avoid: "Using momentum to swing the weights." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Rear Delt Rows", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Hinge forward with a flat back and dumbbells hanging", "Row the weights up with your elbows flared out at about 90 degrees", "Squeeze your rear delts at the top", "Lower the dumbbells slowly until your arms hang straight down"], avoid: "Pulling with your elbows tucked, which shifts the work to your lats." },
  { name: "Scaption Raises", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Hold light dumbbells and stand tall", "Raise your arms about 30 degrees in front of your sides", "Lift up to shoulder height with your thumbs pointing up", "Lower the dumbbells back to your thighs without swinging"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders as you raise." },

  // --- BICEPS ---
  { name: "Barbell Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Standing Barbell Curls"], tips: ["Stand tall with an underhand shoulder-width grip and your elbows at your sides", "Curl the bar up by bending only at the elbows", "Squeeze your biceps at the top without leaning back", "Lower slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Swinging your hips and back to heave the bar up." },
  { name: "Wide-Grip Barbell Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Wide-Grip Standing Barbell Curl"], tips: ["Take an underhand grip wider than your shoulders", "Keep your elbows pinned near your sides", "Curl the bar up and focus on the inner part of your biceps", "Lower the bar to full arm extension and keep your wrists straight"], avoid: "Letting your wrists bend inward under the weight." },
  { name: "Close-Grip Barbell Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Close-Grip Standing Barbell Curl"], tips: ["Take an underhand grip with your hands closer than shoulder width", "Keep your elbows tight at your sides", "Curl the bar up and squeeze your biceps", "Lower slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Letting your elbows drift forward." },
  { name: "EZ-Bar Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Standing EZ-Bar Curl", "FST-7 Standing EZ-Bar Curls"], tips: ["Hold the EZ-bar on the angled grips with your palms turned slightly up", "Keep your elbows at your sides and your torso still", "Curl up until your forearms are vertical or higher", "Lower slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Rocking your torso to swing the bar." },
  { name: "Alternating Dumbbell Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Alternate Dumbbell Curls", "Seated Dumbbell Curl (alternating)", "Standing Alternating Dumbbell Curls"], tips: ["Stand tall with a dumbbell in each hand, palms forward", "Curl one arm up while turning your palm toward your shoulder", "Squeeze at the top and lower slowly", "Alternate arms while keeping your torso still"], avoid: "Swinging the dumbbell using your back." },
  { name: "Bilateral Dumbbell Curls", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Stand tall with a dumbbell in each hand, palms forward", "Curl both dumbbells up together, elbows at your sides", "Squeeze your biceps at the top", "Lower both dumbbells together to a full stretch without swinging"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders roll forward as you curl." },
  { name: "Incline Dumbbell Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Incline Seated Dumbbell Curls", "Alternate Incline Dumbbell Curl", "Incline Bench Dumbbell Curls"], tips: ["Sit back on an incline bench so your arms hang behind your torso", "Let your elbows stay pointed down and back", "Curl the dumbbells up without moving your upper arms", "Lower slowly for a deep stretch in your biceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows swing forward to cheat the weight up." },
  { name: "Concentration Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Dumbbell Concentration Curls", "Seated Concentration Curls"], tips: ["Sit on a bench with your elbow braced against your inner thigh", "Let the dumbbell hang with your arm straight", "Curl up, turning your palm toward your shoulder", "Squeeze at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Rocking your torso to swing the weight." },
  { name: "Spider Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Dumbbell Spider Curls", "Prone Incline Dumbbell Curl", "Single-Arm Dumbbell Spider Curls", "Spider Curl on an Incline Bench", "FST-7 Straight-Bar Spider Curls", "Barbell Spider Curls"], tips: ["Lie chest down on an incline bench with your arms hanging straight down", "Curl the weight up without letting your elbows move", "Squeeze hard at the top", "Lower slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Lifting your chest off the pad to cheat the curl." },
  { name: "Hammer Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Dumbbell Hammer Curls", "Double Hand Hammer Curl", "Barbell Hammer Curl"], tips: ["Stand tall with dumbbells at your sides, palms facing each other", "Curl the weights up while keeping your palms facing in", "Keep your elbows pinned at your sides", "Lower the dumbbells to your sides until your arms are fully straight"], avoid: "Swinging the dumbbells with your back." },
  { name: "Cross-Body Dumbbell Hammer Curls", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Hold dumbbells at your sides with your palms facing in", "Curl one dumbbell across your body toward the opposite shoulder", "Squeeze at the top and lower slowly", "Alternate arms and keep your torso still"], avoid: "Turning your torso to help the weight across." },
  { name: "EZ-Bar Preacher Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Preacher Curls (EZ-Bar)", "Barbell or EZ-Bar Preacher Curl"], tips: ["Sit with your upper arms flat on the preacher pad and grip the EZ-bar", "Lower the bar until your arms are nearly straight", "Curl up and squeeze your biceps", "Control the descent and don't drop into the bottom"], avoid: "Lifting your elbows off the pad or dropping into a full lockout." },
  { name: "Preacher Curls (Dumbbell)", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Single-Arm Preacher Curl"], tips: ["Rest your upper arm flat on the pad and hold the dumbbell", "Lower until your arm is nearly straight", "Curl the dumbbell up and squeeze at the top", "Lower slowly without letting your elbow lift"], avoid: "Locking out hard at the bottom and straining your elbow." },
  { name: "Machine Preacher Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Selectorized Preacher Curl Machine"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so your upper arms rest flat on the pad", "Grip the handles and lower until your arms are nearly straight", "Curl up and squeeze your biceps", "Lower slowly without letting the weights touch"], avoid: "Lifting your shoulders to heave the weight." },
  { name: "Plate-Loaded Biceps Curl Machine", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Adjust the seat so your elbows line up with the pivot", "Rest your upper arms on the pad", "Curl the handles up and squeeze your biceps", "Lower slowly until your arms are nearly straight"], avoid: "Using momentum or lifting your shoulders." },
  { name: "Cable Curls (Straight Bar)", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Low Cable Curls"], tips: ["Stand facing a low pulley with a straight bar and your elbows at your sides", "Curl the bar up while keeping your torso still", "Squeeze at the top", "Lower slowly and keep tension on the cable"], avoid: "Leaning back as the weight gets heavy." },
  { name: "Cable Curls (EZ-Bar Attachment)", category: "Biceps", aka: ["EZ-Bar Cable Curl"], tips: ["Stand facing a low pulley holding the EZ-bar on the angled grips", "Keep your elbows pinned at your sides", "Curl up and squeeze your biceps", "Lower the bar back down until your arms are straight and the cable stays tight"], avoid: "Letting your elbows drift forward." },
  { name: "Cable Rope Hammer Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["FST-7 Rope Hammer Curl", "Cable Hammer Curls"], tips: ["Stand facing a low pulley with the rope in a neutral grip", "Keep your elbows pinned at your sides", "Curl the rope up and pull the ends apart slightly at the top", "Let the rope travel back down until your arms are straight, keeping tension on the cable"], avoid: "Letting your wrists flex as you curl." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Cable Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Unilateral Cable Curls"], tips: ["Stand facing a low pulley with the handle in one hand", "Keep your upper arm still beside your torso", "Curl up and squeeze your biceps", "Lower slowly and keep your shoulder down"], avoid: "Twisting your body to help the curl." },
  { name: "High Cable Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["High Cable Double Biceps Curls", "Overhead Cable Curl", "High Pulley Curl", "High Pulley Cable Curl", "Guillotine Curls (High Cable)"], tips: ["Stand between two high pulleys with your arms out to the sides, hands at head height", "Keep your upper arms still and pointing out", "Curl the handles toward your head", "Squeeze your biceps and return slowly"], avoid: "Letting your elbows drop below shoulder height." },
  { name: "Behind-the-Back Cable Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Bayesian Curls", "Bayesian Cable Curls"], tips: ["Stand facing away from a low pulley with the handle behind you", "Keep your arm slightly behind your body", "Curl up and squeeze your biceps", "Lower slowly to a full stretch"], avoid: "Leaning forward to cheat the curl." },
  { name: "Drag Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Drag Curls (Barbell/Dumbbell)"], tips: ["Hold a barbell and keep it touching your body as you curl", "Pull your elbows back as the bar slides up your torso", "Squeeze your biceps at the top", "Lower slowly by sliding the bar back down"], avoid: "Swinging the bar out in front of you like a normal curl." },
  { name: "Bicep Curls", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Stand tall with a weight in each hand, palms forward", "Keep your elbows at your sides", "Curl up and squeeze your biceps", "Lower each weight over about two seconds to a full stretch"], avoid: "Swinging your torso to lift the weight." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Single Arm Dumbbell Curl", "Standing Dumbbell Curls", "Standing Dumbbell Curl", "Dumbbell Curl HIIT 100's", "Dumbbell Curl HIIT 100's (0s Rest)"], tips: ["Hold dumbbells at your sides with your palms facing forward", "Curl the weights up, keeping your upper arms still", "Squeeze at the top without leaning back", "Lower slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Letting your elbows move forward." },
  { name: "Preacher Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Preacher Curl"], tips: ["Rest your upper arms on the pad and hold the bar or dumbbells", "Lower until your arms are nearly straight", "Curl up and squeeze at the top", "Control the lowering and keep your elbows on the pad"], avoid: "Dropping fast into the bottom of the rep." },
  { name: "Cable Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Standing Biceps Cable Curl"], tips: ["Stand facing a low pulley and hold the bar with an underhand grip", "Keep your elbows at your sides", "Curl up and squeeze your biceps", "Lower slowly and keep tension on the cable"], avoid: "Rocking your torso as the weight gets heavy." },
  // more (added in 2.6.5)
  { name: "Incline Hammer Curls", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Sit back on an incline bench with your arms hanging and your palms facing in", "Keep your elbows pointing straight down", "Curl the dumbbells up without swinging", "Lower slowly for a full stretch"], avoid: "Letting your elbows move forward." },
  { name: "Barbell Preacher Curls", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Sit with your upper arms flat on the pad and grip the bar underhand", "Lower until your arms are nearly straight", "Curl the bar up and squeeze your biceps", "Lower slowly with control"], avoid: "Lifting your armpits off the pad." },
  { name: "Cable Preacher Curls", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Set the preacher pad in front of a low pulley and rest your upper arms on it", "Hold the bar underhand and keep your arms on the pad", "Curl up and squeeze at the top", "Lower slowly against the constant tension"], avoid: "Dropping your wrists or lifting your elbows." },
  { name: "Lying Cable Curls", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Lie on your back on the floor with your feet toward the pulley", "Hold the bar with an underhand grip and keep your elbows at your sides", "Curl up toward your shoulders", "Lower slowly and keep tension on your biceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows slide forward." },
  { name: "Seated Dumbbell Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["FST-7 Seated Dumbbell Curls"], tips: ["Sit tall on a bench with your back supported", "Hold dumbbells with your palms forward and elbows at your sides", "Curl up and squeeze your biceps", "Lower the dumbbells slowly to a full stretch without leaning back"], avoid: "Leaning back to swing the weights." },
  { name: "Barbell 21s", category: "Biceps", aka: ["21s Curls"], tips: ["Do 7 reps from the bottom to halfway up", "Then 7 reps from halfway to the top", "Then 7 full reps to finish the set", "Use a lighter weight and keep your elbows at your sides"], avoid: "Using a weight so heavy that the last reps turn into swinging." },
  { name: "Band Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Resistance Band Curls"], tips: ["Stand on the band and hold the handles with your palms forward", "Keep your elbows at your sides", "Curl up and squeeze at the top", "Lower slowly and don't let the band snap back"], avoid: "Letting the band pull your arms down quickly." },

  // --- TRICEPS ---
  { name: "EZ-Bar Skull Crushers", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Skullcrushers (Lying Triceps Extension)"], tips: ["Lie on a bench holding the EZ-bar with your arms straight above your chest", "Keep your upper arms still and lower the bar toward your forehead", "Bend only at your elbows", "Extend back up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare wide or your upper arms drift back." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Skull Crushers", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Lying Dumbbell Tricep Extension", "Dumbbell Skullcrusher"], tips: ["Lie on a bench with a dumbbell in each hand above your chest, palms facing in", "Lower the dumbbells toward the sides of your head", "Keep your upper arms vertical", "Extend up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Flaring your elbows out to the sides." },
  { name: "JM Press", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Barbell JM Press"], tips: ["Lie on a bench with a barbell and a close grip, elbows tucked", "Lower the bar toward your chin by bending your elbows", "Stop when your forearms are about vertical", "Press up and slightly back, like a cross between a bench press and a skull crusher"], avoid: "Lowering to your chest like a regular bench press." },
  { name: "Seated Overhead Dumbbell Extension", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Sit tall holding one dumbbell overhead with both hands", "Keep your elbows pointing forward and your upper arms still", "Lower the weight behind your head", "Extend up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare out wide." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Overhead Dumbbell Extension", category: "Triceps", aka: ["One-Arm Triceps Extension", "One-arm overhead dumbbell extensions"], tips: ["Hold a dumbbell overhead with one hand and your elbow pointing up", "Keep your upper arm still beside your head", "Lower the weight behind your head", "Extend up and squeeze"], avoid: "Arching your lower back to push the weight up." },
  { name: "Overhead EZ-Bar Extension", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Hold the EZ-bar overhead with a narrow grip", "Keep your elbows pointing forward", "Lower the bar behind your head by bending your elbows", "Extend back up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Flaring your elbows and arching your back." },
  { name: "Rope Pushdown", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Triceps Rope Pushdown", "Triceps Pushdown - Rope Attachment", "Rope Extension", "FST-7 Rope Push Down"], tips: ["Stand close to a high pulley with the rope and your elbows at your sides", "Press the rope down until your arms are straight", "Pull the ends of the rope apart at the bottom and squeeze", "Return slowly until your forearms are about parallel"], avoid: "Letting your elbows drift forward or leaning over the weight." },
  { name: "Straight Bar Pushdown", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Triceps Straight Bar Pushdown", "Close-Grip Straight Bar Pushdown", "Cable Straight Bar Pushdown", "Wide Grip Cable Pushdown"], tips: ["Stand close to a high pulley holding the straight bar with an overhand grip", "Keep your elbows pinned at your sides", "Push down until your arms are fully straight", "Return slowly without lifting your elbows"], avoid: "Using your body weight to push the bar down." },
  { name: "V-Bar Pushdown", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Triceps V-Bar Pushdown", "Triceps Pushdown - V-Bar Attachment", "V Bar Cable Pushdowns"], tips: ["Stand close to a high pulley with the V-bar in an overhand grip", "Keep your elbows pinned at your sides", "Press down until your arms are straight and squeeze your triceps", "Return slowly until your forearms are parallel"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders round forward." },
  { name: "Reverse-Grip Cable Pushdown", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Reverse Grip Triceps Pushdown", "Reverse Grip Cable Extension"], tips: ["Hold the bar with an underhand grip at a high pulley", "Keep your elbows tucked at your sides", "Press down until your arms are straight", "Return slowly and keep your wrists straight"], avoid: "Letting your wrists bend back under the load." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Cable Pushdown", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Standing One-Arm Rope Pushdown"], tips: ["Hold a single handle on a high pulley with your elbow at your side", "Press down until your arm is straight", "Squeeze your triceps and keep your shoulder still", "Return slowly under control"], avoid: "Twisting your torso to push the weight." },
  { name: "Cable Overhead Extension", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Overhead Cable Rope Extension", "Triceps Overhead Extension with V-Bar", "Overhead Cable Triceps Extension", "Overhead Rope Extension", "Rope Overhead Extension", "Rope Overhead Triceps Extension", "Cable Rope Overhead Extension", "FST-7 Overhead Cable Extension", "FST-7 Overhead Rope Extensions", "Overhead Tricep Cable Extension with Free Range Handles", "Seated Overhead Cable Extension"], tips: ["Face away from a low pulley holding the rope behind your head", "Step forward in a staggered stance with your elbows pointing forward", "Extend your arms up and forward until they are straight", "Return slowly and keep your upper arms still"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare out." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Overhead Cable Extension", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Hold a handle behind your head with your elbow pointing up", "Keep your upper arm still beside your ear", "Extend your arm up until it is straight", "Return slowly and keep tension"], avoid: "Leaning forward to help the extension." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Kickbacks", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Tricep Kickbacks", "Tricep Kickback"], tips: ["Hinge forward with a flat back and your upper arm parallel to the floor", "Keep your elbow at your side and bent 90 degrees", "Extend your arm back until it is straight", "Squeeze your triceps and return slowly"], avoid: "Swinging the weight back with your shoulder." },
  { name: "Cable Kickbacks", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Single-Arm Cable Triceps Kickback", "Bent-Over Cable Triceps Extension"], tips: ["Hinge forward holding a low pulley handle with your elbow at your side", "Keep your upper arm still and parallel to the floor", "Extend your arm back until it is straight", "Squeeze and return slowly"], avoid: "Letting your elbow drop as you extend." },
  { name: "Triceps Dips", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Triceps Dips (Parallel Bars)", "Bar Dips", "Dips - Triceps Version"], tips: ["Grip the bars and keep your torso upright with your elbows pointing back", "Lower until your upper arms are about parallel to the floor", "Keep your shoulders down and your chest up", "Press up until your arms are straight and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Leaning forward so much that it becomes a chest dip." },
  { name: "Weighted Triceps Dips", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Close-Grip Weighted Dip"], tips: ["Master your bodyweight dips first and add weight in small steps", "Keep your torso upright and your elbows close to your sides", "Lower until your upper arms are about parallel to the floor", "Press up smoothly without swinging"], avoid: "Dropping so deep that your shoulders strain." },
  { name: "Bench Dips", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Put your hands on a bench behind you with your legs out", "Keep your back close to the bench and your elbows pointing back", "Lower until your elbows are about 90 degrees", "Press up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders roll forward and sink low." },
  { name: "Selectorized Triceps Extension Machine", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Machine Triceps Extension"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so your elbows line up with the pivot", "Keep your upper arms on the pad", "Press the handles down until your arms are straight", "Return slowly without letting the weights touch"], avoid: "Lifting your shoulders to help the press." },
  { name: "Plate-Loaded Triceps Dip Machine", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Adjust the seat so the handles start near your sides", "Keep your torso upright and your elbows tucked", "Press the handles down until your arms are straight", "Return slowly until your elbows reach about 90 degrees"], avoid: "Leaning forward and using your chest." },
  { name: "Diamond Push-Ups", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Place your hands close together under your chest, forming a diamond with your thumbs and fingers", "Keep your body in a straight line", "Lower your chest toward your hands with your elbows tucked", "Press up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare or your hips sag." },
  { name: "Triceps Extension", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Hold the weight with your arms straight and your elbows pointing forward", "Keep your upper arms still", "Lower the weight by bending only at your elbows", "Extend back up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your upper arms move." },
  { name: "Triceps Pushdown", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Triceps Pressdown", "Cable Pushdown", "Triceps Pressdown HIIT 100's", "Triceps Pressdown HIIT 100's (0s Rest)", "Incline Tricep Pushdown"], tips: ["Stand close to a high pulley with your elbows at your sides", "Press the bar or rope down until your arms are straight", "Squeeze your triceps at the bottom", "Return slowly until your forearms are about parallel"], avoid: "Leaning over the bar and pushing with your body." },
  { name: "Skull Crushers", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Skullcrusher", "Lying Triceps Extension"], tips: ["Lie on a bench with your arms straight above your chest", "Keep your upper arms still and bend at your elbows", "Lower the weight toward your forehead", "Extend back up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare out." },
  { name: "Overhead Triceps Extension", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Hold the weight overhead with your elbows pointing forward", "Keep your upper arms close to your head", "Lower the weight behind your head", "Extend up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Arching your lower back as you extend." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Overhead Extension", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Dumbbell Triceps Extension", "Standing Dumbbell Triceps Extension"], tips: ["Hold one dumbbell overhead with both hands under the top plate", "Keep your elbows pointing forward", "Lower the dumbbell behind your head", "Extend up until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Letting the dumbbell pull your arms forward." },
  { name: "Close-Grip Bench Press", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Close-Grip Barbell Bench Press", "Close Grip Press"], tips: ["Lie on a bench and grip the bar about shoulder width", "Tuck your elbows at about 45 degrees", "Lower the bar to your lower chest", "Press up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Gripping so narrow that your wrists hurt." },
  // more (added in 2.6.5)
  { name: "Machine Triceps Dips", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Seated Dip Machine", "Machine Dips", "Seated Triceps Dips", "Machine Tricep Dips", "Tricep Dip Machine", "Triceps Dip Machine"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so the handles start by your sides", "Keep your torso upright and your elbows tucked", "Press down until your arms are straight", "Return slowly and keep tension on your triceps"], avoid: "Using your shoulders to push the weight." },
  { name: "Assisted Triceps Dips", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Machine Assisted Triceps Dips", "Assisted Dips"], tips: ["Set the assist so you can finish every rep with good form", "Place your knees on the pad and grip the handles", "Keep your torso upright and elbows back", "Lower until your elbows are about 90 degrees and press up"], avoid: "Using so much assistance that you don't work for the rep." },
  { name: "Tate Press", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Dumbbell Tate Press"], tips: ["Lie on a bench with dumbbells over your chest, palms facing your feet", "Bend your elbows so the dumbbells lower toward your chest", "Keep your elbows pointing out to the sides", "Extend the dumbbells back up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Using a weight so heavy that the dumbbells hit your chest." },
  { name: "Cable Skull Crushers", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Lying Cable Triceps Extension"], tips: ["Lie on a bench with your head toward a low pulley and hold the bar", "Keep your upper arms still pointing upward", "Lower the bar toward your forehead", "Extend your arms and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare out wide." },
  { name: "Incline Skull Crushers", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Incline EZ-bar Skullcrushers"], tips: ["Lie back on an incline bench holding the bar or dumbbells with your arms straight", "Keep your upper arms still and pointing up", "Lower the weight toward your forehead", "Extend up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows drift back past your head." },
  { name: "Decline Skull Crushers", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Decline Skullcrusher"], tips: ["Lie on a decline bench and hold the weight over your chest", "Keep your upper arms still and bend only at your elbows", "Lower the weight toward your forehead", "Extend up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Using a decline angle so steep that it's hard to control." },
  { name: "Close-Grip Push-Ups", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Place your hands under your chest, about shoulder width or closer", "Keep your body in a straight line", "Lower your chest with your elbows tucked close to your sides", "Press up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare out." },
  { name: "Close-Grip Dumbbell Press", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Lie on a bench holding the dumbbells with your palms facing in", "Keep your elbows tucked close to your sides", "Lower the dumbbells to your lower chest", "Press up and squeeze your triceps at the top"], avoid: "Letting the dumbbells drift apart." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Close-Grip Bench Press", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Set the bench so the bar lowers to your lower chest", "Grip the bar about shoulder width", "Keep your elbows tucked at about 45 degrees", "Press up and re-hook the bar when done"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare out." },
  { name: "Cross-Body Triceps Extension", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Lie on a bench holding a dumbbell above your chest", "Lower the dumbbell across your body toward the opposite shoulder", "Keep your upper arm still and pointing up", "Extend back up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbow drift away from the starting line." },
  { name: "Weighted Bench Dips", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Put your hands on a bench behind you and place a plate on your lap", "Keep your back close to the bench", "Lower until your elbows are about 90 degrees", "Press up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Dropping so low that your shoulders feel strained." },
  { name: "Ring Dips", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Grip the rings and start in a straight-arm support with the rings turned slightly out", "Keep your torso upright and your elbows close", "Lower until your elbows are about 90 degrees", "Press up and turn the rings out at the top"], avoid: "Letting the rings swing wide and strain your shoulders." },

  // --- TRAPS ---
  { name: "Barbell Shrugs", category: "Traps", aka: ["Barbell Shrug"], tips: ["Stand tall holding the bar at your thighs with an overhand grip", "Lift your shoulders straight up toward your ears", "Squeeze your traps at the top for a second", "Lower slowly and keep your arms straight"], avoid: "Rolling your shoulders in circles or bending your elbows to curl the bar." },
  { name: "Behind-The-Back Barbell Shrugs", category: "Traps", tips: ["Hold the bar behind your thighs with an overhand grip", "Stand tall with your chest up", "Lift your shoulders straight up and squeeze", "Lower the bar until your shoulders are fully relaxed and stretched"], avoid: "Letting your head jut forward." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Shrugs", category: "Traps", aka: ["Dumbbell Shrug", "Dumbbell Shrug (seated)", "Dumbbell Shrug HIIT 100's", "Dumbbell Shrug HIIT 100's (0s Rest)"], tips: ["Stand tall with dumbbells at your sides", "Lift your shoulders straight up toward your ears", "Pause and squeeze at the top", "Lower slowly without rolling your shoulders"], avoid: "Using such heavy dumbbells that your grip gives out." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Shrugs", category: "Traps", tips: ["Stand close to the bar and grip it shoulder width", "Keep your arms straight and your chest up", "Shrug straight up and squeeze at the top", "Lower your shoulders slowly until the bar is fully down"], avoid: "Standing too far forward so your shoulders round." },
  { name: "Cable Shrugs", category: "Traps", tips: ["Stand facing a low pulley with the bar or handles at your thighs", "Keep your arms straight and your chest tall", "Shrug straight up and squeeze at the top", "Lower slowly and keep tension"], avoid: "Leaning back to help lift the weight." },
  { name: "Trap Bar Shrugs", category: "Traps", tips: ["Stand inside the trap bar and grip the handles", "Keep your arms straight and your chest up", "Shrug straight up and squeeze at the top", "Lower the bar slowly"], avoid: "Bending your knees to lift the weight." },
  { name: "Iso-Lateral Plate-Loaded Shrug Machine", category: "Traps", tips: ["Adjust the seat or stand so the handles are at your sides", "Keep your arms straight and your chest tall", "Lift your shoulders straight up and squeeze", "Lower slowly and keep both sides even"], avoid: "Letting one side do more than the other." },
  { name: "Selectorized Shrug Machine", category: "Traps", aka: ["Machine Shrugs"], tips: ["Adjust the pad or handles so your arms hang straight", "Stand or sit tall with your chest up", "Lift your shoulders up and squeeze at the top", "Lower slowly without letting the stack touch"], avoid: "Using momentum to bounce the weight." },
  { name: "Farmer's Walk", category: "Traps", aka: ["Farmer's Walk (Grip Focus)", "Farmer's Carry"], tips: ["Pick up a heavy weight in each hand and stand tall", "Keep your shoulders pulled down and back", "Walk with short, quick steps and don't lean", "Stop and set the weights down with control at the end"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders round forward or leaning to one side." },
  { name: "Shrugs", category: "Traps", tips: ["Hold a weight in each hand and stand tall", "Lift your shoulders straight up toward your ears", "Squeeze at the top", "Lower slowly and keep your arms straight"], avoid: "Rolling your shoulders back and forth." },
  // more (added in 2.6.5)
  { name: "Incline Bench Dumbbell Shrugs", category: "Traps", aka: ["Chest-Supported Dumbbell Shrugs"], tips: ["Lie chest down on an incline bench with the dumbbells hanging", "Keep your arms straight and your head neutral", "Lift your shoulder blades up and back", "Squeeze at the top and lower slowly"], avoid: "Lifting your chest off the bench." },
  { name: "Prone Trap Raises", category: "Traps", tips: ["Lie face down on an incline bench with the dumbbells hanging", "Raise your arms out at about 120 degrees, forming a Y", "Squeeze your lower traps and keep your thumbs up", "Lower your arms slowly until the dumbbells hang straight down"], avoid: "Using a weight so heavy that you arch your back." },
  { name: "Power Shrugs", category: "Traps", tips: ["Hold the bar at your thighs and dip slightly with your knees", "Drive your hips up explosively and shrug hard", "Let the bar rise using your hips and traps, not your arms", "Lower the bar and reset between reps"], avoid: "Pulling with your arms like a curl." },

  // --- FOREARMS & GRIP ---
  { name: "Reverse Curls", category: "Forearms", aka: ["Barbell Reverse Curls", "Reverse-Grip Barbell Curl", "Reverse-Grip Barbell or EZ-Bar Curl"], tips: ["Hold the bar with an overhand grip and your elbows at your sides", "Curl the bar up while keeping your wrists straight", "Squeeze your forearms at the top", "Lower the bar slowly to full arm extension without bending your wrists"], avoid: "Letting your wrists bend back." },
  { name: "EZ-Bar Reverse Curls", category: "Forearms", aka: ["EZ-Bar Reverse-Grip Curls", "Reverse-Grip EZ-Bar Curls"], tips: ["Grip the EZ-bar overhand on the outer angled grips", "Keep your elbows pinned at your sides", "Curl up and squeeze your forearms", "Lower slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Using a weight so heavy that your wrists give way." },
  { name: "Cable Reverse Curls", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Face a low pulley and grip the bar overhand", "Keep your elbows at your sides and your wrists straight", "Curl up and squeeze your forearms", "Lower the bar slowly to full arm extension while keeping the cable tight"], avoid: "Rocking your torso to swing the cable." },
  { name: "Zottman Curls", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Curl the dumbbells up with your palms facing up", "Rotate your palms to face down at the top", "Lower slowly with your palms facing down", "Rotate back to palms up at the bottom and repeat"], avoid: "Rushing the lowering part, which is half the exercise." },
  { name: "Barbell Wrist Curls", category: "Forearms", aka: ["Barbell Wrist Curls (Seated)", "Barbell Wrist Curl", "Barbell Wrist Curl HIIT 100's", "Barbell Wrist Curl HIIT 100's (0s Rest)"], tips: ["Sit with your forearms on your thighs and your wrists hanging over your knees, palms up", "Let the bar roll down to your fingers", "Curl your wrists up and squeeze your forearms", "Lower slowly without lifting your forearms"], avoid: "Using your arms and shoulders to move the weight." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Wrist Curls", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Rest your forearm on a bench or thigh with your palm up", "Let the dumbbell roll toward your fingers", "Curl your wrist up as high as you can", "Lower slowly and keep your forearm still"], avoid: "Lifting your forearm off the bench." },
  { name: "Reverse Wrist Curls", category: "Forearms", aka: ["Reverse Barbell Wrist Curls"], tips: ["Rest your forearms on your thighs with your palms down and wrists hanging off", "Lower the weight by letting your wrists bend down", "Extend your wrists up and squeeze the top of your forearms", "Lower your wrists slowly and keep your forearms on your thighs"], avoid: "Using a weight so heavy that your forearms lift." },
  { name: "Reverse Dumbbell Wrist Curls", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Rest your forearm on a bench with your palm down and wrist off the edge", "Lower the dumbbell by bending your wrist down", "Raise it up and squeeze your forearm", "Lower slowly and keep your forearm still"], avoid: "Letting your forearm slide around." },
  { name: "Behind-The-Back Barbell Wrist Curls", category: "Forearms", aka: ["Behind-The-Back Wrist Curls", "Behind The Back Wrist Curls", "Behind-The-Back Wrist Curl"], tips: ["Hold the bar behind your thighs with an overhand or underhand grip", "Let the bar roll to your fingers", "Curl your wrists up and squeeze", "Lower slowly and keep your arms straight"], avoid: "Bending your elbows to lift the bar." },
  { name: "Wrist Roller", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Hold the roller out in front with your arms straight", "Twist your wrists to roll the rope up, one hand at a time", "When the weight reaches the top, reverse slowly to lower it", "Keep your shoulders down and your core braced"], avoid: "Letting the weight drop quickly." },
  { name: "Dead Hangs", category: "Forearms", aka: ["Dead Hangs (Time)"], tips: ["Hang from a bar with an overhand grip and your arms straight", "Keep your shoulders slightly pulled down", "Breathe steadily and keep your legs still", "Hang for the full time and step down carefully"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders shrug up to your ears." },
  { name: "Plate Pinches (Time)", category: "Forearms", aka: ["Plate Pinches"], tips: ["Pinch two plates together smooth sides out, with your fingers on one side and your thumb on the other", "Hold them at your side with your arm straight", "Squeeze hard and keep the plates from slipping", "Hold for the full time, then set them down"], avoid: "Letting the plates slide because your grip is not tight." },
  { name: "Wrist Curls", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Rest your forearms on your thighs with your palms up", "Let your wrists bend down so the weight rolls to your fingers", "Curl your wrists up and squeeze your forearms", "Lower slowly and keep your forearms still"], avoid: "Using a weight so heavy that your forearms lift." },
  // more (added in 2.6.5)
  { name: "Hand Gripper Squeezes", category: "Forearms", aka: ["Grip Trainer"], tips: ["Hold the gripper in your palm and place your thumb on the handle", "Squeeze the handles all the way closed", "Hold for a second at the top", "Open slowly and fully"], avoid: "Using your arm to squeeze instead of your hand." },
  { name: "Suitcase Carry", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Hold a heavy weight in one hand and stand tall", "Keep your shoulders level and your core braced", "Walk with short, steady steps without leaning", "Switch hands and repeat"], avoid: "Leaning to the side as the weight pulls on you." },
  { name: "Cable Wrist Curls", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Sit facing a low pulley with your forearms on your thighs, palms up", "Let the bar pull your wrists down", "Curl your wrists up and squeeze your forearms", "Lower your wrists slowly for a full stretch before the next rep"], avoid: "Lifting your forearms off your thighs." },
  { name: "Barbell Finger Curls", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Hold the bar with your palms up and let it roll down to your fingertips", "Curl your fingers closed to bring the bar back into your palms", "Then curl your wrists up if you can", "Lower slowly and control the roll"], avoid: "Letting the bar roll off your fingers." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Pronation and Supination", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Hold a dumbbell near one end with your forearm resting on your thigh", "Rotate your forearm so your palm faces up", "Rotate it back so your palm faces down", "Keep your elbow still and move slowly"], avoid: "Using a heavy weight that you can't control." },
  { name: "Towel Hangs", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Drape a towel over a pull-up bar and grip both ends", "Hang with your arms straight", "Keep your shoulders slightly down and your legs still", "Hang for the full time and step down carefully"], avoid: "Letting your grip slip and dropping to the floor." },

  // --- CORE & ABS ---
  { name: "Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Standard Crunches", "Crunches (Finisher)"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent and feet flat", "Place your hands across your chest or lightly behind your head", "Curl your ribs toward your hips and lift your shoulder blades off the floor", "Lower slowly without relaxing your abs"], avoid: "Pulling on your neck with your hands." },
  { name: "Decline Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Decline Bench Crunches"], tips: ["Lock your feet in the pads on a decline bench", "Cross your arms over your chest", "Curl your ribs toward your hips and lift your shoulders", "Lower slowly until your back lightly touches the bench"], avoid: "Swinging up with momentum and sitting all the way up." },
  { name: "Weighted Crunches", category: "Core", tips: ["Hold a plate against your chest and lie on your back with your knees bent", "Keep your chin tucked slightly", "Curl your ribs toward your hips and lift your shoulders", "Lower back down slowly without letting the plate pull your head back"], avoid: "Using a plate so heavy that your neck strains." },
  { name: "Hanging Leg Raises", category: "Core", aka: ["Hanging Straight Leg Raises", "Hanging / Incline Leg Raises"], tips: ["Hang from a bar with your arms straight and your shoulders pulled down", "Keep your legs straight and tighten your core", "Raise your legs to hip height or higher by curling your pelvis up", "Lower slowly without swinging"], avoid: "Swinging your body to throw your legs up." },
  { name: "Hanging Knee Raises", category: "Core", aka: ["Hanging Knee-Ups", "Hanging Knee / Leg Raises"], tips: ["Hang from a bar with your shoulders pulled down", "Bend your knees and lift them toward your chest", "Curl your pelvis up at the top and squeeze your abs", "Lower slowly without swinging"], avoid: "Using momentum to swing your legs." },
  { name: "Captain's Chair Leg Raises", category: "Core", tips: ["Rest your forearms on the pads with your back against the backrest", "Keep your shoulders down and core tight", "Lift your knees or legs up toward your chest", "Lower slowly without letting your back peel off the pad"], avoid: "Swinging your legs with momentum." },
  { name: "Lying Leg Raises", category: "Core", aka: ["Lying Floor Leg Raises"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your hands under your hips and legs straight", "Press your lower back into the floor", "Lift your legs up to vertical", "Lower slowly without letting your lower back arch"], avoid: "Letting your lower back arch off the floor as your legs lower." },
  { name: "Cable Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Cable Crunches (Kneeling)", "Rope Crunches", "Kneeling Cable Crunches", "Lying Cable Crunch"], tips: ["Kneel under a high pulley holding the rope beside your head", "Keep your hips still and pointing straight down", "Curl your ribs toward your hips and crunch down", "Return slowly without letting your hips move"], avoid: "Pulling with your arms instead of your abs." },
  { name: "Cable Crunches (Standing)", category: "Core", tips: ["Stand facing a high pulley and hold the rope near your head", "Keep your hips back and a slight bend in your knees", "Curl your ribs down toward your hips", "Return slowly and stay braced"], avoid: "Bending at your hips instead of curling your spine." },
  { name: "Machine Ab Crunches (Selectorized)", category: "Core", aka: ["Ab Crunch Machine", "Machine Crunches"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so the pad sits against your upper chest", "Hold the handles lightly and keep your hips on the seat", "Curl your ribs toward your hips and squeeze", "Return slowly until your abs are stretched"], avoid: "Pushing with your arms or legs instead of your abs." },
  { name: "Rotary Torso Machine", category: "Core", tips: ["Sit tall with your hips locked against the pad and your arms on the pads", "Rotate your torso to one side using your obliques", "Pause and squeeze at the end", "Return slowly and switch sides"], avoid: "Using your arms and shoulders to swing the weight." },
  { name: "Ab Coaster Machine", category: "Core", tips: ["Kneel on the pad with your forearms against the pads", "Brace your core and keep your hips under control", "Curl your knees and ribs together and squeeze your abs", "Return slowly without letting your lower back arch"], avoid: "Pushing with your hips and legs." },
  { name: "Ab Wheel Rollouts", category: "Core", tips: ["Kneel on a mat holding the wheel with your hips tucked and your abs braced", "Roll out slowly while keeping your back flat", "Stop just before your lower back starts to sag", "Pull the wheel back by tightening your abs and curling your pelvis"], avoid: "Letting your lower back arch as you roll out." },
  { name: "Barbell Rollouts", category: "Core", aka: ["Barbell Ab Rollout"], tips: ["Kneel holding a loaded barbell with your hands shoulder width", "Brace your core and tuck your tailbone", "Roll out slowly while keeping your back flat", "Pull back by tightening your abs"], avoid: "Rolling out so far that your hips sag." },
  { name: "Plank", category: "Core", aka: ["Plank (Time)", "Abdominal Planks"], tips: ["Rest on your forearms with your elbows under your shoulders", "Make a straight line from your head to your heels", "Squeeze your glutes and brace your abs", "Hold the full time and breathe steadily"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag or pike up." },
  { name: "Weighted Plank (Time)", category: "Core", tips: ["Get into a forearm plank and have a partner place a plate on your upper back", "Keep a straight line from head to heels", "Squeeze your glutes and brace your abs", "Hold for the full time with steady breathing"], avoid: "Using more weight than you can hold with a flat back." },
  { name: "Side Plank", category: "Core", aka: ["Side Planks (Time)"], tips: ["Lie on your side and prop yourself on your forearm, elbow under your shoulder", "Lift your hips so your body forms a straight line", "Stack your feet and keep your hips high", "Hold for the full time and switch sides"], avoid: "Letting your hips drop toward the floor." },
  { name: "Russian Twists", category: "Core", tips: ["Sit with your knees bent and lean back slightly with a flat back", "Lift your feet or keep them lightly on the floor", "Rotate your torso from side to side, moving your ribs, not just your arms", "Keep your chest up and your core tight"], avoid: "Rounding your back or just swinging your arms side to side." },
  { name: "Weighted Russian Twists", category: "Core", aka: ["Medicine Ball Russian Twist"], tips: ["Sit with your knees bent and lean back with a flat back, holding a weight at your chest", "Rotate your torso to one side, then the other", "Move your ribs and shoulders, not just your hands", "Keep your chest up and breathe steadily"], avoid: "Using a weight so heavy that you lose your posture." },
  { name: "Bicycle Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Bicycle Kicks"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your hands lightly behind your head", "Lift your shoulders and bring one knee toward your chest", "Rotate your torso to bring your opposite elbow toward that knee", "Switch sides in a smooth pedaling motion"], avoid: "Pulling on your neck or rushing through the reps." },
  { name: "V-Ups", category: "Core", aka: ["V Crunches"], tips: ["Lie flat on your back with your arms overhead and legs straight", "Lift your legs and torso at the same time", "Reach your hands toward your toes at the top", "Lower slowly with control"], avoid: "Throwing your arms to swing up." },
  { name: "Dragon Flags", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on a bench and grip the edge behind your head", "Lift your body into a straight line from shoulders to toes", "Lower your body slowly while keeping it straight", "Stop just above the bench and lift back up"], avoid: "Bending at the hips and dropping your legs." },
  { name: "High-to-Low Cable Woodchoppers", category: "Core", aka: ["Cable Woodchopper"], tips: ["Set the cable high and stand sideways, holding the handle with both hands", "Rotate your torso and pull the handle down across your body to the opposite hip", "Pivot your back foot and keep your arms mostly straight", "Return slowly and switch sides"], avoid: "Using only your arms instead of rotating your torso." },
  { name: "Low-to-High Cable Woodchoppers", category: "Core", tips: ["Set the cable low and stand sideways, holding the handle with both hands", "Rotate your torso and pull the handle up across your body overhead", "Pivot your back foot and keep your arms mostly straight", "Return slowly and switch sides"], avoid: "Straining your lower back by leaning back." },
  { name: "Pallof Press", category: "Core", tips: ["Stand sideways to a cable at chest height and hold the handle at your chest", "Brace your core and keep your hips square", "Press the handle straight out and resist the pull", "Hold a second, then bring it back in"], avoid: "Letting your torso rotate toward the cable." },
  { name: "Dead Bugs", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on your back with your arms up and your knees bent at 90 degrees", "Press your lower back into the floor", "Extend your opposite arm and leg slowly", "Return and switch sides without losing your back position"], avoid: "Letting your lower back arch off the floor." },
  { name: "Hollow Body Hold (Time)", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on your back with your arms overhead and legs straight", "Press your lower back into the floor", "Lift your shoulders and legs a few inches", "Hold the shape for the full time and keep breathing"], avoid: "Letting your lower back arch up." },
  { name: "L-Sit Hold (Time)", category: "Core", tips: ["Place your hands on parallettes, rings or the floor beside your hips", "Press down hard and lift your body off the ground", "Keep your legs straight and out in front", "Hold for the full time"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders shrug up to your ears." },
  { name: "Sit-Ups", category: "Core", aka: ["Incline Sit Ups"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent and feet flat", "Cross your arms over your chest", "Curl all the way up until your torso is upright", "Lower slowly and keep your abs engaged"], avoid: "Yanking up with your neck or throwing your arms." },
  { name: "Leg Raises", category: "Core", aka: ["Leg Lift"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your legs straight and your hands under your hips", "Press your lower back into the floor", "Raise your legs to vertical", "Lower slowly without arching your back"], avoid: "Letting your lower back lift as your legs come down." },
  { name: "Woodchoppers", category: "Core", tips: ["Stand with your feet shoulder width and hold a weight with both hands", "Bring the weight down diagonally across your body", "Rotate through your torso and pivot your back foot", "Return slowly and switch sides"], avoid: "Moving only your arms instead of your whole torso." },
  // more (added in 2.6.5)
  { name: "Bird Dog", category: "Core", aka: ["Bird Dogs"], tips: ["Get on your hands and knees with your back flat", "Extend your opposite arm and leg together", "Keep your hips level and your core braced", "Hold briefly, then return and switch sides"], avoid: "Letting your hips rotate or your back arch." },
  { name: "Mountain Climbers", category: "Core", tips: ["Start in a high plank with your hands under your shoulders", "Drive one knee toward your chest", "Switch legs quickly while keeping your hips low", "Keep your core tight and breathe steadily"], avoid: "Bouncing your hips up and down." },
  { name: "Flutter Kicks", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on your back with your hands under your hips", "Lift your legs a few inches off the floor", "Kick your legs up and down in small alternating motions", "Keep your lower back pressed into the floor"], avoid: "Letting your lower back arch." },
  { name: "Toe Touches", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on your back with your legs straight up in the air", "Reach your hands toward your toes", "Lift your shoulder blades off the floor", "Lower slowly and keep your legs still"], avoid: "Swinging your arms and using momentum." },
  { name: "Heel Taps", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent and feet flat", "Lift your shoulders slightly", "Reach one hand toward the same heel, then the other", "Keep your abs engaged and your movement controlled"], avoid: "Pulling your neck forward." },
  { name: "Toes-to-Bar", category: "Core", tips: ["Hang from a bar with your shoulders pulled down", "Brace your core and lift your toes up toward the bar", "Keep your legs as straight as you can", "Lower slowly without swinging"], avoid: "Kipping wildly instead of controlling the lift." },
  { name: "Hanging Windshield Wipers", category: "Core", aka: ["Windshield Wipers"], tips: ["Hang from a bar and lift your legs up to the bar", "Rotate your legs to one side like a windshield wiper", "Bring them back to the center and rotate to the other side", "Keep your arms straight and your shoulders down"], avoid: "Swinging your body to get your legs across." },
  { name: "Landmine Twists", category: "Core", tips: ["Stand holding the end of a landmine bar at chest height", "Rotate your torso and swing the bar from side to side", "Pivot your feet and keep your arms mostly straight", "Keep your core tight and move with control"], avoid: "Using your arms instead of your torso." },
  { name: "Cable Side Bends", category: "Core", tips: ["Stand sideways to a low pulley and hold the handle at your side", "Bend your torso sideways toward the pulley", "Squeeze your obliques as you stand back up", "Keep your torso in a straight plane, no twisting"], avoid: "Leaning forward or backward instead of straight to the side." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Side Bends", category: "Core", tips: ["Stand tall with a dumbbell in one hand", "Bend sideways toward the dumbbell and keep your hips square", "Squeeze your obliques to stand back up", "Finish the reps on one side before switching"], avoid: "Using a weight so heavy that you twist." },
  { name: "Copenhagen Plank", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on your side with your top leg on a bench and your forearm on the floor", "Lift your hips so your body forms a straight line", "Keep your bottom leg tucked or hovering under the bench", "Hold for the full time and switch sides"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag." },
  { name: "Reverse Plank", category: "Core", tips: ["Sit with your legs straight and your hands behind your hips", "Lift your hips until your body forms a straight line", "Squeeze your glutes and keep your chest open", "Hold the full time and breathe steadily"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag or your head drop back." },
  { name: "Body Saw Plank", category: "Core", tips: ["Get in a forearm plank with your feet on sliders or a towel", "Rock your body forward and back by moving your forearms", "Keep a straight line and your core tight", "Move slowly in a small range"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag as you move back." },
  { name: "Stir the Pot", category: "Core", tips: ["Place your forearms on a stability ball in a plank position", "Brace your core and keep your body straight", "Move your forearms in small circles as if stirring", "Switch directions halfway through"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag or swing." },
  { name: "Decline Sit-Ups", category: "Core", aka: ["Decline Bench Sit-Ups (3/4 Way Down)", "Decline 3/4 Sit-Ups (or Roman Chair)"], tips: ["Lock your feet in the pads on a decline bench", "Cross your arms over your chest", "Curl your torso all the way up", "Lower slowly with control"], avoid: "Pulling on your head and neck." },
  { name: "Weighted Sit-Ups", category: "Core", aka: ["Dumbbell Weighted Sit-Up"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent and hold a plate to your chest", "Curl all the way up to sit upright", "Lower slowly while keeping your abs engaged", "Keep your feet flat and your chin tucked"], avoid: "Using weight so heavy that your back rounds hard." },
  { name: "Stability Ball Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Swiss Ball Crunches", "Ball Crunches"], tips: ["Sit on a stability ball and roll down until your lower back is supported", "Place your hands across your chest", "Curl your ribs toward your hips", "Lower back over the ball slowly for a stretch"], avoid: "Letting the ball roll out from under you." },
  { name: "Stability Ball Rollouts", category: "Core", tips: ["Kneel and place your forearms on the ball", "Brace your core and keep your hips tucked", "Roll the ball forward as far as you control", "Pull back by tightening your abs"], avoid: "Letting your lower back sag." },
  { name: "Seated Knee Tucks", category: "Core", aka: ["Seated Leg Tuck"], tips: ["Sit on the edge of a bench and lean back with your hands beside you", "Extend your legs out and hold your core tight", "Pull your knees toward your chest", "Extend slowly and repeat"], avoid: "Letting your torso collapse backward." },
  { name: "Hanging Oblique Knee Raises", category: "Core", tips: ["Hang from a bar with your shoulders down", "Lift your knees up and slightly to one side", "Squeeze your obliques at the top", "Lower slowly and alternate sides"], avoid: "Swinging your body to get the knees up." },

  // --- CARDIO & FULL BODY CONDITIONING ---
  { name: "Treadmill", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Treadmill Running"], tips: ["Start with a 3 to 5 minute easy warm-up pace", "Stand tall with your eyes forward and let your arms swing naturally", "Land with your feet under your hips rather than reaching far out front", "Keep your hands off the rails once you are settled"], avoid: "Gripping the handrails, which lowers the work and throws off your posture." },
  { name: "Treadmill Sprints", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Warm up for at least 5 minutes before the first sprint", "Hold the side rails while you step on and set the speed, then let go and run", "Drive your knees and pump your arms with your chest tall", "Straddle the belt and slow it down fully during each rest"], avoid: "Hopping on and off a moving belt or sprinting before you are warm." },
  { name: "Stairmaster", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Stairmaster / Step Machine", "StepMill", "Stair Climber", "Gauntlet"], tips: ["Stand upright and place your whole foot on each step", "Keep your hips under you and your chest tall", "Use the rails only lightly for balance", "Choose a pace you can hold with steady breathing"], avoid: "Leaning your weight on the rails or taking tiny toe-only steps." },
  { name: "Rowing Machine", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Rowing Machine (Erg)"], tips: ["Start with your arms straight, shins vertical and your back flat", "Push with your legs first, then lean back slightly, then pull the handle to your lower ribs", "Return in the reverse order: arms, then torso, then knees", "Keep a smooth, steady rhythm"], avoid: "Pulling with your arms first or rounding your lower back." },
  { name: "Stationary Bike", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Stationary Cycling"], tips: ["Set the seat so your knee has a slight bend at the bottom of the pedal stroke", "Keep your back flat and your shoulders relaxed", "Pedal in smooth circles instead of stomping", "Pick a resistance you can hold at a steady cadence"], avoid: "A seat set too low or too high, which stresses your knees." },
  { name: "Assault Bike / Air Bike", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Set the seat so your knee has a slight bend at the bottom", "Push and pull the handles while you pedal", "Start at a manageable pace and build up", "Breathe steadily and rest fully between hard efforts"], avoid: "Starting at a full sprint and burning out in the first few seconds." },
  { name: "Elliptical", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Elliptical Trainer"], tips: ["Stand tall with your whole foot flat on the pedals", "Hold the handles lightly and keep your core braced", "Move in smooth, even strides", "Switch direction now and then to change the load"], avoid: "Leaning on the handles or letting your knees cave in." },
  { name: "Arc Trainer", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Cross Trainer"], tips: ["Stand tall with your feet flat on the pedals", "Hold the handles lightly and keep your core braced", "Take smooth, even strides", "Set the resistance so you can keep a steady pace"], avoid: "Hunching over the console or gripping the handles hard." },
  { name: "Recumbent Bike", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Seated Bike"], tips: ["Adjust the seat so your leg is almost straight at the bottom of each stroke", "Keep your back supported against the seat", "Pedal in smooth circles", "Pick a steady resistance and cadence"], avoid: "Setting the seat too close, which bends your knees too much." },
  { name: "VersaClimber", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Vertical Climber"], tips: ["Stand tall and grip the handles with your arms and legs moving in opposition", "Use long, smooth strokes through your full range", "Keep your core braced", "Find a steady rhythm and breathe regularly"], avoid: "Taking short, choppy strokes and hunching forward." },
  { name: "Jacob's Ladder", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Ladder Climber"], tips: ["Hold the rails lightly and keep your body tall", "Climb with a steady stepping rhythm", "Use your whole foot on each rung", "Pick a pace you can sustain and breathe steadily"], avoid: "Leaning forward and gripping the rails hard." },
  { name: "Arm Bike", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Upper Body Ergometer", "UBE"], tips: ["Adjust the seat height so your shoulders are level with the crank", "Sit tall with your back supported", "Turn the cranks in smooth circles", "Switch directions halfway to balance the work"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders up toward your ears." },
  { name: "SkiErg", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Stand tall with your arms overhead holding the handles", "Pull down using your lats while hinging at your hips and bending your knees", "Finish with your hands near your hips and your core braced", "Return up smoothly and keep a steady rhythm"], avoid: "Pulling only with your arms instead of using your hips and lats." },
  { name: "Jump Rope", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Hold the handles at hip height with your elbows close to your sides", "Turn the rope mainly with your wrists", "Jump just high enough to clear the rope and land softly on the balls of your feet", "Keep your core tight and your posture tall"], avoid: "Jumping too high and swinging your arms in wide circles." },
  { name: "Burpees", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Squat down and place your hands on the floor", "Jump or step your feet back to a plank", "Lower your chest to the floor, then press up", "Jump your feet to your hands and finish with a small jump"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag in the plank." },
  { name: "Box Jumps", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Stand a short distance from the box with your feet shoulder width", "Swing your arms and jump up, landing softly with your knees bent", "Stand up tall at the top", "Step down carefully instead of jumping off"], avoid: "Landing with stiff, locked knees or jumping down from the top." },
  { name: "Sled Push", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Hold the handles with your arms extended and your body leaning forward", "Keep your back flat and your core tight", "Drive with powerful steps and push through the balls of your feet", "Keep your head neutral and breathe steadily"], avoid: "Rounding your back or taking tiny steps." },
  { name: "Sled Pull", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Face the sled with the strap or rope in your hands, or walk backward with the harness", "Sit slightly back with your chest up", "Pull with long strides and keep the rope tight", "Keep your back flat throughout"], avoid: "Rounding your upper back or letting the rope go slack." },
  { name: "Battle Ropes", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Stand with your knees bent and your chest up, holding one end in each hand", "Brace your core and keep your hips back", "Make fast waves with your arms in an alternating pattern", "Keep your shoulders relaxed and breathe steadily"], avoid: "Using only your arms and rounding your back." },
  { name: "Tire Flips", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Squat low with your hands under the tire and your back flat", "Drive up with your legs and hips first", "Push the tire up and over as it rises", "Reset your stance and repeat"], avoid: "Pulling with a rounded back instead of driving with your legs." },
  { name: "Medicine Ball Slams", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Raise the ball overhead with your arms extended", "Brace your core and rise onto your toes", "Slam the ball down hard in front of you", "Squat to pick it up and repeat"], avoid: "Rounding your back as you pick the ball up." },
  // more (added in 2.6.5)
  { name: "Walking", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Walk"], tips: ["Stand tall with your eyes forward", "Let your arms swing naturally", "Land on your heel and roll through to your toes", "Pick a pace where you can still talk"], avoid: "Slouching or staring down at your phone." },
  { name: "Incline Treadmill Walk", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Incline Walking", "12-3-30"], tips: ["Set a moderate incline and a steady walking speed", "Stand tall with your chest up", "Let your arms swing naturally", "Keep your hands off the handrails once you are settled"], avoid: "Holding the handrails, which cuts the work and shifts your posture." },
  { name: "Outdoor Running", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Running", "Run", "Jogging"], tips: ["Run tall with your eyes ahead and your shoulders relaxed", "Take quick, light steps and land under your hips", "Keep your arms bent about 90 degrees and swing them front to back", "Build up pace gradually and keep your breathing steady"], avoid: "Starting out too fast and overstriding." },
  { name: "Outdoor Cycling", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Cycling", "Bike Ride"], tips: ["Make sure your bike fits you and your helmet is on", "Keep your back flat and your elbows soft", "Pedal in smooth circles at a steady cadence", "Stay alert to traffic and ride predictably"], avoid: "Riding with a seat too low, which strains your knees." },
  { name: "Swimming", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Swim"], tips: ["Warm up with a few easy laps first", "Keep your body long and flat in the water", "Rotate your hips and shoulders with each stroke", "Breathe on a steady rhythm"], avoid: "Rushing your strokes and holding your breath." },
  { name: "Hiking", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Hike"], tips: ["Wear sturdy shoes and bring water", "Keep your chest up and take steady steps", "Shorten your stride on steep climbs and lean slightly into the hill", "Use trekking poles on steep or rough ground if you have them"], avoid: "Heading out too far without enough water or food." },
  { name: "Jumping Jacks", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Stand tall with your feet together and arms at your sides", "Jump your feet out and raise your arms overhead", "Jump back to the start", "Land softly on the balls of your feet"], avoid: "Landing with stiff knees." },
  { name: "High Knees", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Stand tall and run in place", "Drive each knee up to hip height", "Pump your arms in rhythm", "Land softly on the balls of your feet and keep your core tight"], avoid: "Leaning back or landing flat-footed and hard." },
  { name: "Shadow Boxing", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Stand with your feet shoulder width and your hands up by your chin", "Throw jabs and crosses with your fists, rotating your hips and shoulders", "Stay light on your feet and keep moving", "Snap each punch back to your guard"], avoid: "Locking out your elbows hard on every punch." },
  { name: "Heavy Bag Work", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Boxing Bag"], tips: ["Wrap your hands or wear gloves before you start", "Keep your hands up and your chin tucked", "Rotate your hips and shoulders into each punch", "Keep your wrists straight on contact"], avoid: "Punching with a bent wrist or dropping your guard." },
  { name: "Hill Sprints", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Warm up thoroughly before your first sprint", "Lean slightly into the hill and drive your knees", "Pump your arms hard and push off the balls of your feet", "Walk back down and rest fully between sprints"], avoid: "Sprinting cold, which risks a pulled hamstring or calf." },

  // --- ADDED FROM THE PHIL HEATH, LOU FERRIGNO, ARNOLD, DORIAN YATES, MOUNTAIN DOG, JAY CUTLER & RONNIE COLEMAN PROGRAMS ---
  // Chest
  { name: "Decline Cable Flyes", category: "Chest", tips: ["Set the pulleys high and use a decline bench or a downward-leaning stance", "Start with your arms wide and a soft bend in your elbows", "Sweep your hands down and together toward your lower chest", "Squeeze for a second, then return slowly"], avoid: "Dropping your shoulders forward as your hands come together." },
  // Back
  { name: "Behind-the-Neck Pulldown", category: "Back", tips: ["Only use this if your shoulders have full mobility, and use a lighter weight", "Sit tall and lean slightly forward", "Pull the bar down to the back of your neck, not lower", "Control the bar back up until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Forcing the bar below ear level or jerking it behind your head." },
  { name: "Close-Grip Chin-Ups", category: "Back", tips: ["Grip the bar underhand with your hands about 6 inches apart", "Hang with your shoulders down", "Pull your chest to the bar, keeping your elbows in close", "Lower slowly to a full hang"], avoid: "Letting your body swing between reps." },
  { name: "Dorian Deadlift", category: "Back", tips: ["Do one warm-up set, then one all-out working set", "Set your back flat and your chest up before the bar moves", "Pull the bar straight up close to your legs", "Stand tall and lower the bar with control, do not drop it"], avoid: "Rounding your back to grind out extra reps at the end of the set." },
  { name: "Inverted Rows", category: "Back", tips: ["Lie under a bar set at waist height and grip it overhand", "Keep your body straight from head to heels", "Pull your chest to the bar, driving your elbows back", "Lower slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Letting your hips drop as you pull." },
  // Legs
  { name: "Barbell Lunges", category: "Legs", tips: ["Rest the bar on your upper back and brace your core", "Step forward into a lunge and lower your back knee toward the floor", "Keep your torso tall and your front knee over your toes", "Push back to the start through your front heel"], avoid: "Letting the bar bounce on your back." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Front Lunges", category: "Legs", aka: ["Smith Machine Lunges"], tips: ["Set the bar on your upper back and place one foot forward", "Keep your torso upright and your front foot flat", "Lower your back knee toward the floor", "Drive up through your front heel and re-hook the bar when done"], avoid: "Stepping so far forward that your front heel lifts." },
  { name: "Vertical Leg Press", category: "Legs", tips: ["Lie on your back with your hips under the sled and your feet on the platform", "Lower the sled until your knees are close to your chest, back still flat", "Press up through your whole foot", "Stop short of locking out your knees"], avoid: "Letting your lower back curl off the pad." },
  // Shoulders
  { name: "Barbell Clean and Press", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Start with the bar on the floor, hips back and your back flat", "Pull the bar explosively and shrug, then drop under it to catch on your shoulders", "Stand tall and brace your core", "Press the bar overhead and lower it back to your shoulders"], avoid: "Curling the bar up with your arms instead of using your hips." },
  { name: "Incline Lateral Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["One-Arm Incline Lateral Raise"], tips: ["Lie chest down on an incline bench with the dumbbells hanging", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise your arms out to the sides to shoulder height", "Lower slowly and keep your chest on the bench"], avoid: "Lifting your chest off the bench to swing the weights." },
  { name: "Machine Lying Rear-Delt Raise", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Lie face down on the pad with your chest supported and hold the handles", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise your arms out and back until they are level with your shoulders", "Squeeze and return slowly"], avoid: "Lifting your chest off the pad." },
  { name: "Prone Dumbbell Y-Raises", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Lie face down on an incline bench with light dumbbells hanging", "Raise your arms up and out in a Y shape", "Keep your thumbs pointing up and your neck neutral", "Lower your arms slowly until the dumbbells hang straight down"], avoid: "Using a weight so heavy that you hike your shoulders." },
  { name: "Scott Press", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Sit tall with your back supported and brace your core", "Press the weight overhead in a smooth path", "Stop just short of locking your elbows", "Lower back to shoulder level with control"], avoid: "Rushing the lowering part or arching your back." },
  // Biceps
  { name: "Machine Incline Curl", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Adjust the seat so your elbows line up with the pivot and your arms rest behind your torso", "Curl the handles up while your upper arms stay still", "Squeeze at the top", "Lower slowly to a full stretch"], avoid: "Lifting your shoulders off the pad." },
  // Triceps
  { name: "Barbell French Press", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Hold the bar overhead with a close grip and your elbows pointing forward", "Keep your upper arms still", "Lower the bar behind your head", "Extend up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Flaring your elbows out." },
  { name: "Barbell Overhead Triceps Extension", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Stand tall holding the bar overhead with a narrow grip", "Keep your elbows pointing forward and your core braced", "Lower the bar behind your head", "Extend up until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Arching your lower back as you push up." },
  { name: "Close Grip French Press", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Lie on a bench with a close grip on the bar above your chest", "Keep your upper arms vertical and your elbows in", "Lower the bar behind your head", "Extend up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare wide." },
  { name: "Crucifix Extension", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Stand or sit with your arms held straight out to the sides at shoulder height", "Keep your upper arms level with the floor", "Bend your elbows to lower the weights toward your head", "Extend back out and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows droop below shoulder height." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Kick Outs", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Triceps Kick Outs"], tips: ["Hinge forward holding a dumbbell with your upper arm tight to your side", "Bend your elbow to 90 degrees", "Extend your arm straight back", "Squeeze your triceps and return slowly"], avoid: "Swinging the weight with your shoulder." },
  { name: "Incline Two-Dumbbell Extension", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Lie back on an incline bench holding a dumbbell in each hand above your chest", "Keep your upper arms still and pointing up", "Lower the dumbbells toward your head", "Extend up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare outward." },
  { name: "Lying French Press", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Laying Overhead Ext. Cambered Bar"], tips: ["Lie on a bench and hold the bar above your chest with a close grip", "Keep your upper arms still", "Lower the bar behind your head", "Extend your arms and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows move out." },
  { name: "Standing French Press", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Stand tall holding the weight overhead with both hands", "Keep your elbows pointing forward and your core braced", "Lower the weight behind your head", "Extend up and squeeze"], avoid: "Arching your back and flaring your elbows." },
  // Forearms
  { name: "Reverse Preacher Curls", category: "Forearms", tips: ["Rest your upper arms on the preacher pad and grip the bar overhand", "Lower until your arms are nearly straight", "Curl up and squeeze your forearms", "Lower slowly and keep your elbows on the pad"], avoid: "Dropping fast at the bottom." },
  // Core
  { name: "Bench Leg Raises", category: "Core", aka: ["Leg Raises Off Bench"], tips: ["Lie on a bench with your hips at the end and hold the sides behind your head", "Keep your legs straight and your core braced", "Raise your legs until they point toward the ceiling", "Lower slowly without letting your lower back arch"], avoid: "Dropping your legs fast." },
  { name: "Bent-Over Twists", category: "Core", tips: ["Stand with a broomstick or bar across your shoulders and hinge forward", "Keep your back flat and your core braced", "Rotate your torso to touch one side, then the other", "Move slowly through the full rotation"], avoid: "Rounding your lower back or twisting fast." },
  { name: "Broomstick Twists", category: "Core", aka: ["Stick Twist"], tips: ["Stand tall with a broomstick across your upper back and your hands out wide", "Keep your hips facing forward", "Rotate your torso from side to side", "Move with control and keep your core tight"], avoid: "Letting your hips swing with your shoulders." },
  { name: "Oblique Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Leg Raised Oblique Crunches"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent and one hand behind your head", "Lift your shoulder and bring your elbow toward your opposite knee", "Squeeze your obliques at the top", "Lower slowly and finish all reps before switching"], avoid: "Pulling on your neck with your hand." },
  { name: "Reverse Crunches", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent and your arms at your sides", "Curl your knees toward your chest and lift your hips off the floor", "Squeeze your lower abs at the top", "Lower slowly without swinging"], avoid: "Using momentum to swing your legs." },
  { name: "Roman Chair Sit-Ups", category: "Core", tips: ["Set your thighs on the pad of a Roman chair and lock your feet in", "Cross your arms over your chest", "Lower back until your torso is just below parallel", "Curl up using your abs"], avoid: "Hyperextending your lower back at the bottom." },
  { name: "Seated Twists", category: "Core", tips: ["Sit on a bench with a bar across your shoulders and your feet planted", "Keep your back tall and your core braced", "Rotate your torso from side to side", "Move slowly and keep your hips facing forward"], avoid: "Swinging the bar quickly or rounding your back." },
  { name: "Side Bend Crunches", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on your side with your knees bent and your hand behind your head", "Lift your torso sideways by squeezing your oblique", "Pause at the top", "Lower slowly and finish all reps before switching"], avoid: "Rotating your torso instead of bending sideways." },
  { name: "Side Knee Raises", category: "Core", tips: ["Stand tall with your hands behind your head", "Lift one knee up and out to the side toward your elbow", "Squeeze your oblique at the top", "Lower slowly and switch sides"], avoid: "Leaning your torso instead of lifting your knee." },
  { name: "Supported Knee Raises", category: "Core", tips: ["Rest your forearms on the pads with your back against the backrest", "Keep your shoulders down", "Bring your knees up toward your chest", "Lower slowly without swinging"], avoid: "Letting your lower back come off the pad." },
  { name: "Tuck-Up Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Tuck Crunch"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent and arms at your sides", "Curl your torso and your knees toward each other", "Squeeze your abs at the top", "Lower slowly and keep tension"], avoid: "Using momentum to rock up." },
  { name: "Vertical Bench Crunches", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on a bench and hold the edge behind your head, legs lifted straight up", "Curl your hips up toward the ceiling", "Squeeze your lower abs at the top", "Lower slowly without swinging"], avoid: "Throwing your legs to create momentum." },
  // Warm-Up & Mobility
  { name: "Banded Pull-Aparts", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Hold a light band at chest height with your arms straight", "Pull the band apart by squeezing your shoulder blades together", "Stop when the band touches your chest", "Return slowly and keep your ribs down"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders up toward your ears." },
  { name: "Bodyweight Warm-Up Exercises", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Start with easy, smooth movements and gradually build the range", "Move through squats, lunges, arm circles and hip openers", "Breathe steadily and keep your movements controlled", "Stop before anything feels sharp or pinchy"], avoid: "Rushing through the moves or bouncing at the end of your range." },
  { name: "Dive Bomber Push-Ups", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Start in a pike position with your hips high and hands shoulder width", "Bend your elbows and sweep your chest down and forward close to the floor", "Push through to a cobra-like position with your hips low", "Reverse the path to return"], avoid: "Rushing the movement and sagging your lower back." },
  { name: "Front and Lateral Leg Swings", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Hold a wall or rack for balance and stand tall", "Swing one leg forward and back with a smooth rhythm, then side to side", "Start small and gradually increase the range", "Keep your torso still and switch legs"], avoid: "Swinging so hard that you lose your balance." },
  { name: "Inchworms", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Stand tall, then fold forward and place your hands on the floor", "Walk your hands out to a plank position", "Walk your feet toward your hands", "Stand up and repeat"], avoid: "Bending your knees a lot or letting your hips sag in the plank." },
  { name: "Isometric Lateral Lunges", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Take a wide stance and shift your weight to one side", "Sit your hips back and keep the other leg straight", "Keep your chest up and your heel down", "Hold the bottom position and breathe, then switch sides"], avoid: "Letting your knee cave inward or your heel lift." },
  { name: "Low Lunge Hold", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Step into a lunge and lower your back knee toward the floor", "Keep your torso tall and your front knee over your ankle", "Squeeze the glute of your back leg to feel the hip flexor stretch", "Hold and breathe, then switch sides"], avoid: "Arching your lower back to get deeper." },
  { name: "Lying Crossover Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Lie on your back with your arms out to the sides", "Bring one knee across your body toward the opposite side", "Keep both shoulders on the floor", "Hold and breathe, then switch sides"], avoid: "Forcing the knee down hard or lifting your shoulders." },
  { name: "Lying Hip Twist", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent and your arms out to the sides", "Slowly drop both knees to one side", "Keep your shoulders on the floor", "Bring your knees back to center and switch sides"], avoid: "Forcing your knees down or letting your shoulders lift." },
  { name: "One-Arm Dumbbell Lateral External Rotation", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Lie on your side with a very light dumbbell in your top hand and your elbow tucked at your side", "Keep your elbow bent at 90 degrees", "Rotate your forearm up toward the ceiling", "Lower slowly with control"], avoid: "Using a heavy weight or lifting your elbow away from your side." },
  { name: "One-Arm Dumbbell Upright External Rotation", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Stand holding a light dumbbell with your elbow bent at 90 degrees and tucked at your side", "Rotate your forearm outward without moving your elbow", "Pause briefly at the end", "Return slowly with control"], avoid: "Letting your elbow drift away from your body." },
  { name: "Prone Around The World", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Lie face down with your arms by your sides and your thumbs pointing up", "Lift your arms and sweep them in a wide arc out and overhead", "Keep your arms off the floor and your neck neutral", "Return along the same path slowly"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders and arching your lower back." },
  { name: "Prone IYT Raises", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Lie face down with your forehead off the floor", "Raise your arms into a Y shape, then a T, then a W, one at a time", "Squeeze your shoulder blades back and down", "Use no weight or very light weights and move slowly"], avoid: "Using heavy weights, which turns it into a shrug." },
  { name: "Seated Forward Toe Reach", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Sit on the floor with your legs straight in front of you", "Hinge forward from your hips and reach toward your toes", "Keep your back as long as you can", "Hold and breathe steadily"], avoid: "Rounding your back hard and bouncing." },
  { name: "Upper Body Foam Rolling", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Place the roller under your upper back and cross your arms", "Roll slowly from your mid back up toward your shoulders", "Pause on tender spots for a few breaths", "Keep your core braced"], avoid: "Rolling over your lower back or neck, or moving too fast." },

  // more warm-up & mobility (added in 2.6.5)
  { name: "Cat-Cow", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Cat Cow Stretch"], tips: ["Start on your hands and knees with your hands under your shoulders", "Round your spine up toward the ceiling and tuck your chin", "Then arch your back, drop your belly and look slightly forward", "Move slowly with your breath"], avoid: "Rushing through it or forcing an extreme range." },
  { name: "World's Greatest Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Step into a deep lunge with your hands on the floor inside your front foot", "Rotate your torso toward your front leg and reach your arm to the ceiling", "Return your hand to the floor and straighten your front leg", "Switch sides and repeat"], avoid: "Rushing and letting your back knee collapse." },
  { name: "90/90 Hip Switches", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["90 90 Hip Stretch"], tips: ["Sit with your front knee bent at 90 degrees and your back knee bent at 90 degrees", "Sit tall with your chest up", "Rotate your knees across to switch sides", "Move slowly and keep your hips low"], avoid: "Leaning back on your hands and forcing the rotation." },
  { name: "Band Shoulder Dislocates", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Shoulder Dislocates"], tips: ["Hold a band or stick with a wide grip in front of your thighs", "Keep your arms straight and lift the band overhead", "Move it behind your back as far as comfortable", "Return slowly and narrow your grip if you feel pinching"], avoid: "Using a grip so narrow that it forces your shoulders." },
  { name: "Arm Circles", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Stand tall and hold your arms straight out to the sides", "Make small circles, then gradually bigger ones", "Switch directions halfway through", "Keep your shoulders relaxed and down"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulders or swinging wildly." },
  { name: "Scapular Push-Ups", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Start in a push-up position with your arms straight", "Let your chest sink between your shoulder blades without bending your elbows", "Push the floor away and spread your shoulder blades apart", "Keep your core tight"], avoid: "Bending your elbows or sagging your hips." },
  { name: "Thoracic Rotations", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Open Books"], tips: ["Start on your hands and knees with one hand behind your head", "Rotate your elbow down toward the opposite arm", "Then open up and rotate it toward the ceiling", "Keep your hips still and move with your breath"], avoid: "Moving from your lower back instead of your upper back." },
  { name: "Hip Flexor Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Kneeling Hip Flexor Stretch"], tips: ["Kneel on one knee with your other foot flat in front of you", "Tuck your pelvis under and squeeze your back glute", "Lean forward slightly until you feel the front of your hip stretch", "Hold and breathe, then switch sides"], avoid: "Arching your lower back instead of tucking your pelvis." },
  { name: "Hamstring Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Lie on your back and loop a strap or towel around one foot", "Keep your leg as straight as you can and pull it toward you", "Keep your other leg relaxed on the floor", "Hold and breathe, then switch sides"], avoid: "Bouncing or pulling until it feels sharp." },
  { name: "Child's Pose", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Kneel and sit your hips back toward your heels", "Reach your arms forward along the floor", "Rest your forehead down and relax your neck", "Breathe deeply into your back"], avoid: "Forcing your hips down if your knees feel uncomfortable." },
  { name: "Pigeon Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Bring one knee forward and angle your shin across your body", "Extend your other leg straight back", "Keep your hips square and fold forward over your front leg", "Hold and breathe, then switch sides"], avoid: "Letting your hips tilt, or pushing on a sore knee." },
  { name: "Lower Body Foam Rolling", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", tips: ["Place the roller under your quads, hamstrings, glutes or calves", "Roll slowly over the muscle using your arms for support", "Pause on tender spots for a few breaths", "Keep your core braced"], avoid: "Rolling directly over your joints or moving too fast." },

  // --- ADDED FROM THE KRIS GETHIN 12 WEEKS TO MUSCLE PLAN (the rest of its exercises are listed above under other names) ---
  { name: "Bent-Knee Hip Raises", category: "Core", aka: ["Bent-Knee Hip Raise"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent and lifted over your hips", "Curl your hips up off the floor toward your ribs", "Squeeze your lower abs", "Lower slowly with control"], avoid: "Swinging your legs to lift your hips." },
  { name: "Decline Reverse Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Decline Reverse Crunch"], tips: ["Lie on a decline bench with your head at the high end and hold the handles behind your head", "Start with your knees bent over your hips", "Curl your hips up toward your ribs", "Lower slowly with control"], avoid: "Dropping your legs fast at the bottom." },
  { name: "Incline Reverse Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Incline Reverse Crunch"], tips: ["Lie on an incline bench with your head up and hold the top of the bench", "Bring your knees toward your chest", "Lift your hips off the bench", "Lower slowly and keep tension"], avoid: "Swinging your legs to get your hips up." },
  { name: "Weighted Decline Sit-Ups", category: "Core", aka: ["Decline Weighted Sit-Up"], tips: ["Lock your feet in a decline bench and hold a plate at your chest", "Curl all the way up with control", "Lower slowly while keeping your abs tight", "Keep your chin tucked slightly"], avoid: "Yanking on your neck to rise." },
  { name: "Jackknife Sit-Ups", category: "Core", aka: ["Jackknife", "Jackknives"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your arms overhead and legs straight", "Lift your torso and legs together", "Reach your hands toward your feet at the top", "Lower slowly and don't let your lower back arch"], avoid: "Using momentum to swing your arms up." },
  { name: "Crunches (Legs on Bench)", category: "Core", aka: ["Crunch - Legs On Bench", "Legs-on-Bench Crunches"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your calves up on a bench and your knees bent 90 degrees", "Place your hands across your chest", "Curl your ribs toward your hips and lift your shoulders", "Lower slowly and keep your abs tight"], avoid: "Pulling your head forward with your hands." },
  { name: "Bottoms Up", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on your back with your legs lifted straight up over your hips", "Lift your hips straight up toward the ceiling by curling your pelvis", "Squeeze your lower abs at the top", "Lower slowly and keep control"], avoid: "Swinging your legs to get your hips up." },
  { name: "Leg Pull-Ins", category: "Core", aka: ["Leg Pull-In"], tips: ["Sit on the edge of a bench and lean back with your hands behind you", "Extend your legs in front of you", "Pull your knees toward your chest", "Extend slowly and repeat"], avoid: "Letting your torso fall back." },
  { name: "Incline Leg Pull-Ins", category: "Core", aka: ["Incline Leg Pull-In"], tips: ["Lie on an incline bench and hold the top of the bench", "Extend your legs out in front of you", "Pull your knees to your chest", "Extend slowly and keep tension"], avoid: "Letting your lower back arch as your legs extend." },
  { name: "Stability Ball Pull-Ins", category: "Core", aka: ["Exercise Ball Pull-In", "Swiss Ball Pull-Ins", "Ball Knee Tucks"], tips: ["Get in a push-up position with your shins on a stability ball", "Keep your hands under your shoulders and your core braced", "Pull your knees toward your chest", "Roll back out slowly while keeping your hips level"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag when your legs straighten." },
  { name: "Cross-Body Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Cross-Body Crunch", "Crossover Crunch"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent and one hand behind your head", "Lift your shoulder and rotate your elbow toward the opposite knee", "Squeeze your obliques at the top", "Lower slowly and switch sides"], avoid: "Pulling on your neck." },
  { name: "Cable Reverse Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Cable Reverse Crunch"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your ankles hooked to a low pulley and your hands holding something stable", "Bring your knees toward your chest and lift your hips", "Squeeze your lower abs at the top", "Lower slowly and keep tension"], avoid: "Swinging your legs." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Squats", category: "Legs", aka: ["Dumbbell Squat"], tips: ["Hold dumbbells at your sides and stand about shoulder width", "Brace your core and keep your chest up", "Squat down until your thighs are about parallel", "Drive up through your whole foot"], avoid: "Letting the dumbbells pull you forward." },
  { name: "Wide-Stance Squat", category: "Legs", aka: ["Wide Stance Barbell Squat", "Wide Stance Squat", "Wide-Stance Barbell Squat"], tips: ["Take a stance clearly wider than your shoulders with your toes turned out", "Keep your chest up and sit straight down between your legs", "Push your knees out over your toes", "Drive up and squeeze your glutes and inner thighs"], avoid: "Letting your knees cave inward." },
  { name: "Narrow-Stance Squat", category: "Legs", aka: ["Narrow Stance Squat"], tips: ["Place your feet closer than shoulder width with your toes forward", "Keep your torso upright and your core braced", "Squat down so your knees travel forward over your toes", "Drive up through your whole foot"], avoid: "Letting your heels lift off the floor." },
  { name: "Stiff-Legged Dumbbell Deadlift", category: "Legs", aka: ["Stiff-Legged Dumbbell Deadlifts", "DB Straight Leg Deadlifts", "Dumbbell Stiff-Leg Deadlift"], tips: ["Hold dumbbells in front of your thighs with your knees slightly bent", "Push your hips back and lower the weights down your legs", "Lower until you feel a strong hamstring stretch with a flat back", "Drive your hips forward to stand"], avoid: "Rounding your lower back." },
  { name: "Cuban Press", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Use light dumbbells and start with an upright row, elbows high", "Rotate your forearms up so the dumbbells point to the ceiling", "Press overhead until your arms are straight", "Reverse the steps slowly back down"], avoid: "Using weights so heavy that you can't rotate your arms smoothly." },
  { name: "Side Lateral to Front Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Side Laterals to Front Raise", "Chest Supported Side to Front Raise", "Front to Side Raises"], tips: ["Hold light dumbbells at your sides", "Raise your arms out to the side to shoulder height", "Lower, then raise your arms to the front to shoulder height", "That's one rep, keep your torso still"], avoid: "Swinging your body to move the weights." },
  { name: "Chest-Supported Dumbbell Front Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Front Incline Dumbbell Raise", "Chest-Supported Dumbbell Front Raise", "Incline Bench Front Raises", "Spider Bench Front Raises", "FST-7 Spider Bench Front Raises"], tips: ["Lie chest down on an incline bench with the dumbbells hanging in front", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise your arms forward to about head height", "Lower slowly and keep your chest on the bench"], avoid: "Lifting your chest off the bench." },
  { name: "Barbell Incline Shoulder Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Barbell Incline Shoulder Raise"], tips: ["Use a light barbell and set the bench at about 45 degrees", "Keep your elbows slightly bent and your core braced", "Raise the bar to about eye level in a smooth arc", "Lower the bar back down along the same arc"], avoid: "Using momentum to heave the bar up." },
  { name: "Seated Cable Shoulder Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Cable Shoulder Press"], tips: ["Sit between the cable stacks with the handles at shoulder height", "Keep your back against the pad and your core braced", "Press the handles overhead and bring your hands slightly together", "Lower to shoulder height with control"], avoid: "Arching your back to finish the press." },
  { name: "Seated Reverse-Grip Barbell Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Seated Barbell Military Press (reverse-grip)", "Seated Reverse Grip Shoulder Press with EZ Bar"], tips: ["Sit tall with your back supported and grip the bar underhand at shoulder width", "Keep your elbows slightly in front of the bar", "Press up until your arms are almost straight", "Lower to your upper chest with control"], avoid: "Loading too heavy before your wrists adapt to the underhand grip." },
  { name: "Bent-Over Dumbbell Rows", category: "Back", aka: ["Bent Over Two-Dumbbell Row", "Bent-Over Dumbbell Lat Row", "Two-Dumbbell Row"], tips: ["Hinge forward with a flat back, knees slightly bent, a dumbbell in each hand", "Let the dumbbells hang below your chest", "Row both to your lower ribs with your elbows close", "Lower slowly and keep your torso still"], avoid: "Standing up as you pull or rounding your back." },
  { name: "Bent-Over Trap Rows", category: "Back", aka: ["Bent-Over Trap Row", "Bent Trap Row"], tips: ["Hinge forward with a flat back and your arms hanging", "Pull your elbows out to the sides, at about 45 to 90 degrees from your torso", "Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the top", "Lower the bar until your arms are straight without rounding your back"], avoid: "Pulling with your biceps instead of squeezing your upper back." },
  { name: "Low Rows", category: "Back", tips: ["Sit tall at a low pulley with your knees slightly bent", "Pull the handle to your lower belly with your elbows close", "Squeeze your shoulder blades at the end", "Return slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Leaning back and rocking to get the weight moving." },
  { name: "Incline Close-Grip Bench Press", category: "Triceps", tips: ["Set the bench to a low incline and grip the bar about shoulder width", "Keep your elbows tucked at about 45 degrees", "Lower the bar to your upper chest", "Press up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Using a steep bench so your shoulders take over." },

  // --- ADDED FOR THE SUPER SHREDDED 8 SUPERSETS (the rest of its exercises are listed above) ---
  { name: "Seated Barbell Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Seated Barbell Curl"], tips: ["Sit tall on a bench with your feet planted and an underhand grip on the bar", "Rest your elbows near your thighs and keep your back upright", "Curl up and squeeze your biceps", "Lower the bar slowly to a full stretch without letting your elbows drift forward"], avoid: "Leaning back to help the weight up." },
  { name: "Low Cable Crossovers", category: "Chest", aka: ["Cable Crossover (Low Pulley)", "Low Pulley Cable Crossover", "Cable Crossover from Low Pulley"], tips: ["Set the pulleys at the bottom and use a staggered stance", "Start with your hands by your hips and a soft elbow bend", "Sweep your hands up and together to about chin height", "Squeeze your upper chest, then lower slowly"], avoid: "Using your back and shoulders to swing the weight up." },
  { name: "High Cable Crossovers", category: "Chest", aka: ["Cable Crossover (High Pulley)", "High Pulley Cable Crossover"], tips: ["Set the pulleys high and use a staggered stance", "Start with your arms wide and a soft elbow bend", "Bring your hands down and together in front of your hips", "Squeeze your chest and return slowly to the wide position"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders round forward as you pull down." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Behind-The-Neck Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Smith-Machine Seated Behind-The-Neck Shoulder Press"], tips: ["Only do this if your shoulders move well, and use a light weight", "Sit with your back straight and the bar lined up behind your head", "Lower the bar to ear level, no lower", "Press up until your arms are almost straight"], avoid: "Lowering the bar to the base of your neck." },
  { name: "Lying Cable Rear Delt Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Lying Cable Rear Delt Raise", "Lying Cable Rear Delt Flye"], tips: ["Lie on your back on a bench between low pulleys", "Cross the cables so each hand holds the opposite handle", "Pull your arms out to your sides with a soft bend in your elbows", "Squeeze your rear delts and return slowly"], avoid: "Arching your back off the bench." },
  { name: "Oblique Cable Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Oblique Cable Crunch", "Standing Oblique Cable Crunch"], tips: ["Kneel under a high pulley holding the rope beside your head", "Crunch down and rotate one elbow toward the opposite knee", "Squeeze your obliques at the bottom", "Return slowly and keep your hips still"], avoid: "Pulling with your arms." },
  { name: "Standing Lat Pulldown", category: "Back", tips: ["Stand facing the high pulley and hold the bar with your arms straight overhead", "Lean slightly forward with a flat back and your core braced", "Pull the bar down toward your upper chest, elbows down and back", "Let it rise slowly to a full stretch"], avoid: "Using your whole body to yank the weight down." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Behind-The-Back Shrugs", category: "Traps", aka: ["Smith Machine Behind-The-Back Barbell Shrug"], tips: ["Stand in front of the bar and hold it behind your thighs", "Keep your chest up and arms straight", "Shrug straight up and squeeze at the top", "Lower slowly and re-hook the bar when done"], avoid: "Leaning forward as you shrug." },

  // --- ADDED FOR THE SUPERSET SPLITS (Arnold Blueprint, Buendia and Kris Gethin plans) ---
  { name: "Incline Close-Grip Dumbbell Press", category: "Triceps", aka: ["DB Incline Close Grip Press"], tips: ["Set the bench to a low incline with the dumbbells touching over your chest", "Keep your palms facing each other", "Lower the dumbbells to your upper chest with your elbows tucked", "Press up and squeeze your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your elbows flare as the weight rises." },
  { name: "Lying Lateral Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Lying Side Laterals"], tips: ["Lie on your side on a bench holding a light dumbbell with the top arm", "Keep a soft bend in your elbow", "Raise the dumbbell up in a wide arc to shoulder height", "Lower the dumbbell slowly back to your side without letting it drop"], avoid: "Rolling your torso to swing the weight." },
  { name: "Front and Back Barbell Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Front to Rear Barbell Press"], tips: ["Use a light weight and sit tall", "Press the bar overhead from the front of your head, then lower it", "Press it overhead from behind your head, then lower again", "Do one front and one back for each rep and stop if your shoulders pinch"], avoid: "Lowering behind your neck too far or going heavy." },
  { name: "Cable Fly Ladders", category: "Chest", aka: ["Cable Fly (Ladders)"], tips: ["Pick a light weight and set the pulleys at mid height", "Do one rep with your hands at the low position, then middle, then high without resting", "Keep a soft bend in your elbows and your chest proud", "Finish all three heights for one set before resting"], avoid: "Starting too heavy and swinging the weight to finish." },
  { name: "Triceps Rockers", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Rockers"], tips: ["Lie back like a skull crusher with a light weight", "Keep your upper arms still and pointing up", "Bend and straighten your elbows in a smooth rocking motion", "Squeeze your triceps with each rep"], avoid: "Using too much weight and swinging your upper arms." },
  { name: "Between-The-Legs Cable Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Leaning Forward Cable in Between Your Legs Curls"], tips: ["Stand over a low pulley with the cable running between your feet", "Hinge slightly forward with your elbows at your sides", "Curl the handle up toward your chest", "Lower slowly and keep tension on your biceps"], avoid: "Bending your back to heave the weight." },
  { name: "Plate Preacher Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Preacher Curls with Barbell Plate"], tips: ["Hold a weight plate at its sides at the bottom edge", "Rest your upper arms on a preacher pad", "Curl the plate up toward your chin", "Lower slowly with control"], avoid: "Letting the plate slip or your elbows leave the pad." },
  { name: "Row Curls", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Use a light to moderate weight and keep your elbows at your sides", "Curl the weight up with controlled form", "Squeeze your biceps at the top", "Lower slowly and don't let your body swing"], avoid: "Using your back and momentum instead of your arms." },
  // --- ADDED FOR THE 2.16.0 UPDATE (more exercises, each with its own tips) ---
  { name: "Bent-Over Cable Crossover", category: "Chest", aka: ["Bentover Cable Crossover", "Bent Over Cable Crossover", "Bent-Over Cable Flyes"], tips: ["Set both pulleys high, hold a handle in each hand and step forward into a staggered stance", "Hinge forward at your hips to about 45 degrees with a flat back and a soft bend in your elbows", "Sweep your hands down and together in a wide arc until they meet in front of your lower chest", "Squeeze your chest for a second, then open your arms slowly until you feel a stretch"], avoid: "Rounding your back or bending your elbows so it turns into a press." },
  { name: "Pause Bench Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Paused Bench Press"], tips: ["Set up as for a normal bench press: eyes under the bar, shoulder blades pinched together, feet planted", "Lower the bar under control until it touches your mid-chest", "Hold it still on your chest for one to two seconds without relaxing your upper back", "Press up hard and finish with your elbows locked"], avoid: "Letting the bar sink into your chest or bouncing out of the pause." },
  { name: "Barbell Pullover", category: "Chest", aka: ["Barbell Pullovers", "Straight-Bar Pullover"], tips: ["Lie on a bench holding a light barbell over your chest with your hands about shoulder width apart", "Keep a slight bend in your elbows and brace your core", "Lower the bar in an arc back over your head until you feel a deep stretch in your chest and lats", "Pull the bar back over your chest, keeping your elbows in the same position"], avoid: "Arching your lower back or using more weight than you can control behind your head." },
  { name: "Reverse-Grip Incline Bench Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Reverse-Grip Incline Press"], tips: ["Set the bench to a low incline and lie back with your feet planted", "Take an underhand grip about shoulder width", "Lower the bar toward your upper chest with your elbows tucked", "Press up and slightly back until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Using a grip that is too wide or flaring your elbows." },
  { name: "Half-Kneeling Single-Arm Lat Pulldown", category: "Back", aka: ["Half-Kneeling Lat Pulldown", "Kneeling Single-Arm Pulldown"], tips: ["Kneel on one knee facing the cable with your other foot flat, holding the handle in one hand", "Sit tall and brace your core without leaning back", "Pull your elbow down and into your side, as if putting it in your back pocket", "Let your arm rise slowly until you feel a full stretch in your lat"], avoid: "Twisting your torso or leaning back to pull the weight down." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Deadlift", category: "Back", aka: ["Dumbbell Deadlifts"], tips: ["Stand with a dumbbell on the floor beside each foot, feet hip width apart", "Push your hips back, bend your knees and grip the weights with a flat back and your chest up", "Drive through your whole foot and stand up tall, keeping the dumbbells close to your legs", "Lower them under control by pushing your hips back first"], avoid: "Rounding your back or letting the dumbbells swing away from your legs." },
  { name: "Renegade Rows", category: "Back", aka: ["Renegade Row"], tips: ["Start in a high plank with your hands on two dumbbells and your feet wide for balance", "Brace your core and squeeze your glutes so your hips stay level", "Row one dumbbell to your hip without letting your hips rotate", "Lower it with control, then switch sides"], avoid: "Letting your hips twist open as you row. Use lighter dumbbells if they do." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Smith Machine Bent-Over Row", "Smith Machine Rows"], tips: ["Stand with your feet under the bar, hinge forward with a flat back and grip the bar just wider than your shoulders", "Unhook the bar and keep a slight bend in your knees", "Row the bar toward your lower ribs, driving your elbows back", "Lower slowly until your arms are straight and re-hook the bar when you are done"], avoid: "Standing up as you pull or rounding your back." },
  { name: "Hex Bar Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Trap Bar Row", "Hex Bar Rows"], tips: ["Stand inside the hex bar and hinge forward with a flat back", "Grip the handles and brace your core", "Row the bar toward your hips by driving your elbows back", "Lower slowly without rounding your back"], avoid: "Using your hips to heave the weight up." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Deadlifts", category: "Back", aka: ["Smith Machine Deadlift"], tips: ["Stand with the bar over your mid-foot and your feet hip width", "Hinge back with a flat back and grip the bar just outside your legs", "Push the floor away and keep your hips and shoulders rising together", "Lock out by squeezing your glutes and lower along the same path"], avoid: "Pulling with your back instead of pushing with your legs and hips." },
  { name: "Reverse Hack Squat", category: "Legs", aka: ["Reverse Hack Squats"], tips: ["Set the machine so your chest is against the pad and your feet are on the platform", "Brace your core and keep your back flat against the pad", "Squat down until your thighs are about parallel", "Drive up through your whole foot without locking your knees hard"], avoid: "Letting your knees cave in or your heels lift." },
  { name: "Barbell Hack Squat", category: "Legs", aka: ["Barbell Hack Squats"], tips: ["Hold the bar behind your legs with an overhand grip", "Keep your chest up and your heels slightly raised if needed", "Squat down while keeping the bar close to your legs", "Drive up through your whole foot"], avoid: "Letting the bar drift away from your legs or rounding your back." },
  { name: "Wedge Squat", category: "Legs", aka: ["Wedge Squats"], tips: ["Place your heels on a low wedge or plates", "Stand with your feet about shoulder width", "Squat down while keeping your torso upright", "Drive up through your whole foot and keep your knees tracking over your toes"], avoid: "Letting your heels lift off the wedge." },
  { name: "Reverse Nordic Curls", category: "Legs", aka: ["Reverse Nordic", "Reverse Nordics"], tips: ["Kneel on a pad with your hips extended and your body in a straight line from knees to head", "Brace your core and squeeze your glutes", "Lean back slowly as far as you can control, keeping your hips forward", "Pull yourself back up using your quads"], avoid: "Bending at your hips or dropping back faster than you can control." },
  { name: "Single-Leg Lying Leg Curl", category: "Legs", aka: ["Single-Leg Lying Leg Curls", "Unilateral Lying Leg Curl", "Unilateral Lying Hamstring Curl"], tips: ["Lie face down on the machine with the pad just above one heel", "Keep your hips pressed into the bench and your other leg relaxed", "Curl the pad toward your glute and squeeze your hamstring", "Lower slowly until your leg is nearly straight, and finish all reps before switching"], avoid: "Lifting your hips off the bench or swinging the weight up." },
  { name: "Lateral Step-Ups", category: "Legs", aka: ["Lateral Step-Up", "Side Step-Ups"], tips: ["Stand sideways next to a sturdy box or bench with your near foot flat on top", "Drive through that heel to lift your body up, keeping your chest tall", "Tap your other foot on the box without pushing off it", "Lower slowly back to the floor and finish all reps on one side"], avoid: "Pushing off your back foot or using a box so high that your hips shift." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Romanian Deadlift", category: "Legs", aka: ["Smith Machine RDL"], tips: ["Stand with your feet hip width and the bar at your thighs, with a soft bend in your knees", "Push your hips straight back and slide the bar down your legs", "Lower until you feel a strong stretch in your hamstrings with a flat back", "Drive your hips forward to stand tall and squeeze your glutes"], avoid: "Rounding your back or bending your knees so much that it becomes a squat." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Cleans", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Dumbbell Clean"], tips: ["Start with the dumbbells at your sides and push your hips back", "Explosively extend your hips and shrug as the weights rise", "Pull your elbows up and catch the dumbbells at your shoulders", "Stand tall and lower them back with control"], avoid: "Curling the weights up with your arms instead of using your hips." },
  { name: "Barbell Power Cleans", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Barbell Power Clean", "Power Clean", "Power Cleans"], tips: ["Set up with the bar over your mid-foot, a flat back and your arms straight", "Push with your legs to bring the bar off the floor", "Explode your hips and shrug as the bar passes your knees", "Pull yourself under the bar and catch it on your shoulders"], avoid: "Pulling with your arms early or rounding your back." },
  { name: "Bradford Press", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Bradford Presses"], tips: ["Hold a light barbell at your upper chest with a grip slightly wider than your shoulders", "Press it up just past your forehead without locking out", "Lower it behind your head to the base of your neck, then press back up", "Keep your core braced and your head tucked back out of the way"], avoid: "Going heavy or forcing the bar behind your head when your shoulders feel tight." },
  { name: "Cable Rear Delt Rows", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Cable Rear Delt Row"], tips: ["Set the pulley at chest height, hold the handles with an overhand grip and step back", "Hinge slightly forward and keep your torso still", "Pull your elbows out wide to about 90 degrees from your body", "Squeeze your rear delts and return slowly"], avoid: "Pulling with your elbows close to your sides, which turns it into a lat row." },
  { name: "Overhead Carry", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Waiter Walk", "Overhead Farmer's Walk", "Overhead Carries"], tips: ["Press a weight overhead with your arm straight and your biceps near your ear", "Brace your core and keep your ribs down", "Walk with short, steady steps without leaning away from the weight", "Lower it carefully and switch arms"], avoid: "Letting your lower back arch or your elbow bend as you walk." },
  { name: "Waiter Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Waiter Curl"], tips: ["Hold one dumbbell upright by its top end, cupped in both palms like a tray", "Stand tall with your elbows pinned at your sides", "Curl the dumbbell up toward your chest", "Lower slowly while keeping your palms cupped under the weight"], avoid: "Swinging your torso or letting the dumbbell tip toward you." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Preacher Hammer Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Preacher Hammer Curl", "Preacher Hammer Curls"], tips: ["Set the preacher pad so your armpits are against the top and your arms rest on the pad", "Hold the dumbbells with your palms facing each other", "Curl up without lifting your elbows off the pad", "Lower slowly until your arms are almost straight"], avoid: "Letting your elbows lift off the pad or dropping the weights at the bottom." },
  { name: "Bodyweight Triceps Extensions", category: "Triceps", aka: ["Bodyweight Triceps Extension", "Bodyweight Skull Crushers"], tips: ["Set a bar in a rack or Smith machine at about waist height and grip it shoulder width apart", "Walk your feet back until your body is in a straight, slanted line", "Bend your elbows and lower your forehead toward the bar", "Extend your arms back up by squeezing your triceps"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag or your elbows flare out wide." },
  { name: "Barbell High Pulls", category: "Traps", aka: ["Barbell High Pull", "High Pulls"], tips: ["Hold the bar at your thighs with an overhand grip and your hands just outside your legs", "Push your hips back, then drive them forward as you shrug and pull the bar up", "Lead with your elbows and bring the bar to about chest height", "Lower under control and reset your stance"], avoid: "Pulling with your arms before your hips and shoulders have moved." },
  { name: "Neck Crunches", category: "Traps", aka: ["Neck Curls", "Neck Flexion", "Neck Crunch"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your knees bent", "Tuck your chin slightly toward your chest", "Lift your head a few inches using your neck muscles", "Lower slowly and keep the movement small"], avoid: "Pulling your head forward with your hands or jerking up." },
  { name: "Plank Shoulder Taps", category: "Core", aka: ["Shoulder Taps", "Plank Shoulder Tap"], tips: ["Start in a high plank with your feet wider than shoulder width", "Brace your core and squeeze your glutes", "Tap one shoulder with the opposite hand, then switch", "Keep your hips level without rocking side to side"], avoid: "Letting your hips swing as you lift each hand." },
  { name: "Plank Jacks", category: "Core", aka: ["Plank Jack"], tips: ["Start in a forearm or high plank with your body in a straight line", "Jump your feet out wide and then back together", "Keep your hips level and your core tight", "Land softly on the balls of your feet"], avoid: "Letting your hips pike up or sag as your feet jump." },
  { name: "Bear Crawls", category: "Core", aka: ["Bear Crawl"], tips: ["Start on your hands and toes with your knees an inch off the floor and your back flat", "Move your opposite hand and foot forward together", "Keep your hips low and level, your core braced and your head neutral", "Take small, controlled steps, then crawl backward if you have space"], avoid: "Letting your hips rise high or swaying side to side." },
  { name: "Smith Machine Crunches", category: "Core", aka: ["Smith Machine Crunch"], tips: ["Kneel or sit facing the bar with a light plate or the bar held to your chest", "Brace your core and tuck your pelvis", "Curl your ribs toward your hips instead of bending at your hips", "Return slowly with tension on your abs"], avoid: "Pulling with your arms or bending only at your hips." },
  { name: "Sandbag Carry", category: "Forearms", aka: ["Sandbag Carries"], tips: ["Hug the sandbag against your chest with your arms wrapped under it", "Stand tall with your core braced", "Walk with short, steady steps without leaning back", "Set the bag down by bending your knees, not your back"], avoid: "Leaning back to balance the bag or rounding your upper back." },
  { name: "Rucking", category: "Cardio", aka: ["Ruck", "Weighted Walking"], tips: ["Load a backpack with a weight you can carry comfortably, about 10 percent of your body weight to start", "Pack the weight high on your back and tighten the straps so it doesn't bounce", "Walk at a brisk pace with a tall posture and your shoulders back", "Take shorter steps on hills and build up time before adding weight"], avoid: "Loading too much weight too soon or leaning forward from your waist." },
  { name: "Wall Slides", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Wall Slide"], tips: ["Stand with your back, head and hips against a wall and your arms in a goalpost position", "Press your forearms and the backs of your hands into the wall", "Slide your arms up overhead without letting your ribs flare", "Slide them back down slowly"], avoid: "Arching your lower back or letting your arms peel off the wall." },
  { name: "Hip Circles", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Standing Hip Circles", "Hip Circle"], tips: ["Stand on one leg holding a wall or rack for balance and lift the other knee to hip height", "Rotate your hip in a big, slow circle", "Do the same number of circles in each direction", "Keep your torso still and tall"], avoid: "Swinging your knee fast or leaning your torso to make the circle." },
  { name: "Ankle Mobility Rocks", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Ankle Rocks", "Ankle Mobility", "Knee-to-Wall Ankle Stretch"], tips: ["Place one foot a few inches from a wall with your whole foot flat", "Drive your knee forward toward the wall without lifting your heel", "Hold for a second at the end, then straighten back", "Move your foot a little farther from the wall once it feels easy"], avoid: "Letting your heel lift or your knee cave inward." },
  { name: "Deep Squat Hold", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Deep Squat Stretch", "Prying Squat Hold"], tips: ["Stand with your feet a bit wider than your shoulders and your toes turned out slightly", "Sit down into a deep squat with your heels flat", "Press your elbows into your knees and keep your chest up", "Hold and breathe, shifting side to side if it feels tight"], avoid: "Letting your heels lift or your knees cave in. Hold a rack for balance if needed." },
  { name: "Standing Quad Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Quad Stretch", "Standing Quadriceps Stretch"], tips: ["Stand tall holding a wall or rack, bend one knee and grab your ankle", "Keep your knees close together and tuck your hips under", "Pull your heel toward your glute until you feel a stretch in the front of your thigh", "Hold and breathe, then switch legs"], avoid: "Arching your lower back or letting your knee drift forward." },
  { name: "Calf Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Wall Calf Stretch", "Standing Calf Stretch"], tips: ["Place your hands on a wall and step one foot back with your heel flat on the floor", "Keep your back leg straight and your toes pointing forward", "Lean forward until you feel a stretch in your calf", "Hold and breathe, then switch legs"], avoid: "Letting your back heel lift or your foot turn out." },
  { name: "Doorway Chest Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Doorway Pec Stretch", "Chest Stretch"], tips: ["Stand in a doorway with your forearms on the frame and your elbows at about shoulder height", "Step one foot forward through the door until you feel a stretch across your chest", "Keep your ribs down and your neck relaxed", "Hold and breathe, then move your arms a little higher or lower to feel a different part"], avoid: "Pushing so far that your shoulders feel pinched." },
  { name: "Cross-Body Shoulder Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Cross-Arm Shoulder Stretch", "Cross Body Arm Stretch"], tips: ["Bring one arm straight across your chest at shoulder height", "Hold it just above the elbow with your other hand and pull it in gently", "Keep your shoulders down and your torso facing forward", "Hold and breathe, then switch arms"], avoid: "Shrugging your shoulder up or twisting your torso." },
  { name: "Overhead Triceps Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Triceps Stretch", "Overhead Tricep Stretch"], tips: ["Raise one arm and bend your elbow so your hand reaches down your back", "Use your other hand to gently press the elbow back and down", "Keep your ribs down and your head upright", "Hold and breathe, then switch arms"], avoid: "Arching your lower back or pulling hard on the elbow." },
  { name: "Kneeling Lat Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Bench Lat Stretch", "Lat Stretch"], tips: ["Kneel in front of a bench with your elbows on it and your palms together", "Sit your hips back toward your heels and let your chest sink down", "Keep your back flat and feel the stretch along your sides and under your arms", "Hold and breathe"], avoid: "Arching your lower back instead of stretching through your lats." },
  { name: "Knee-to-Chest Stretch", category: "Warm-Up & Mobility", aka: ["Single Knee to Chest Stretch", "Knee to Chest"], tips: ["Lie on your back with your legs straight", "Pull one knee toward your chest with both hands", "Keep the other leg flat and your head down on the floor", "Hold and breathe, then switch legs"], avoid: "Lifting your head or letting your lower back twist." },
  // --- ADDED FOR THE 2.17.0 UPDATE (every exercise the built-in programs use, so each one is in the list with its own tips) ---
  { name: "EZ-Bar Front Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["EZ Bar Front Raises"], tips: ["Hold an EZ-bar at your thighs with an overhand grip on the angled parts and a soft bend in your elbows", "Raise the bar in front of you to about eye level", "Keep your core braced and avoid leaning back", "Lower slowly back to your thighs"], avoid: "Swinging the bar up with your lower back." },
  { name: "Seated Cable Chest Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Seated Cable Press"], tips: ["Sit on a bench between two cables set at chest height, with your back supported and the handles at your chest", "Brace your core and keep your shoulder blades pulled back", "Press the handles straight forward until your arms are almost straight", "Return slowly until you feel a stretch across your chest"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders roll forward or your back peel off the pad." },
  { name: "Cable Rope Curls", category: "Biceps", aka: ["Rope Cable Curl"], tips: ["Stand facing a low pulley holding the rope with your palms facing up", "Keep your elbows pinned at your sides", "Curl the rope up and pull the ends slightly apart at the top", "Lower slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Swinging your torso or letting your elbows drift forward." },
  { name: "Incline Cable Front Raises", category: "Shoulders", tips: ["Set a bench to a low incline and sit back with your back supported and a low pulley by your feet", "Hold the handle with a soft bend in your elbow", "Raise your arm forward to about eye level", "Lower slowly and keep tension on the cable"], avoid: "Leaning back off the bench or swinging the handle up." },
  { name: "Seated Cable Lateral Raises", category: "Shoulders", aka: ["Cable Seated Lateral Raise"], tips: ["Sit tall on a bench with a low pulley beside you and hold the handle in the hand farthest from it", "Keep a soft bend in your elbow", "Raise your arm out to the side to shoulder height", "Lower slowly and keep tension on the cable"], avoid: "Shrugging or leaning your torso to swing the handle up." },
  { name: "Chest-Supported Cable Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Chest Supported Cable Rows"], tips: ["Set an incline bench facing a low pulley and lie chest down on it", "Hold the handles with your arms straight and your shoulder blades spread", "Row your elbows back toward your hips and squeeze your shoulder blades together", "Return slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Lifting your chest off the bench or shrugging your shoulders." },
  { name: "Incline Close-Grip Push-Ups", category: "Chest", aka: ["Incline Close Grip Push-ups"], tips: ["Place your hands close together on a bench or bar, shoulder width or narrower", "Walk your feet back until your body is in a straight line", "Lower your chest to your hands with your elbows tucked", "Press back up until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag or your elbows flare out." },
  { name: "Incline Elbow-to-Knee Twist Crunch", category: "Core", aka: ["Incline Elbow to Knee Twist Crunch"], tips: ["Lie on an incline bench with your knees bent and your hands lightly behind your head", "Lift your shoulders and twist to bring one elbow toward the opposite knee", "Squeeze your obliques at the top", "Lower slowly and alternate sides"], avoid: "Pulling on your neck or just swinging your elbows." },
  { name: "Reverse-Grip Dumbbell Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Reverse Grip Dumbbell Bent Over Row", "Reverse Grip Single Arm Row"], tips: ["Hinge forward with a flat back, holding a dumbbell with an underhand grip", "Let the dumbbell hang straight down", "Row it toward your hip, keeping your elbow close to your side", "Lower slowly to a full stretch"], avoid: "Twisting your torso or flaring your elbow out." },
  { name: "Plate Hammer Curls", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Hold a weight plate by its sides with your palms facing each other at your thighs", "Keep your elbows pinned at your sides", "Curl the plate up toward your chest", "Lower it slowly until your arms are straight"], avoid: "Swinging your body or letting the plate drop." },
  { name: "Low Incline Dumbbell Press", category: "Chest", tips: ["Set the bench to a low incline, about 15 to 30 degrees, and lie back with your feet planted", "Bring the dumbbells to your upper chest with your wrists stacked over your elbows", "Press up and slightly together until your arms are straight", "Lower slowly with your elbows at about 45 to 60 degrees"], avoid: "Setting the bench so steep that it turns into a shoulder press." },
  { name: "Single-Arm Low Incline Dumbbell Press", category: "Chest", aka: ["Unilateral Low Incline Dumbbell Press"], tips: ["Set the bench to a low incline and hold one dumbbell at your upper chest", "Brace your core and keep your shoulders flat on the bench", "Press the dumbbell up until your arm is straight", "Lower slowly without letting your torso twist, and finish all reps before switching"], avoid: "Letting your torso rotate as you press." },
  { name: "Neutral-Grip Seated Cable Row", category: "Back", aka: ["Neutral Grip Low Cable Row", "Neutral Grip Cable Row", "V-Bar Cable Row", "Close Grip Pulley Row"], tips: ["Sit tall with your knees slightly bent and a neutral-grip handle in both hands", "Keep your chest up and your back flat", "Pull the handle to your lower ribs, keeping your elbows close to your sides", "Squeeze your shoulder blades, then let the handle return slowly"], avoid: "Rocking your torso back and forth to move the weight." },
  { name: "Dead/Curl/Press", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Pick a pair of dumbbells light enough to keep good form for the whole set", "Deadlift them up with a flat back and your hips driving forward", "Curl them to your shoulders without swinging", "Press them overhead, then lower back to the floor under control"], avoid: "Rounding your back on the deadlift or swinging the weights up on the curl." },
  { name: "Steady State Cardio + Twists", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Pick a pace you can hold for the whole time while still talking", "Keep your posture tall and your breathing steady", "Add standing twists by rotating your torso with your arms across your chest", "Keep your hips facing forward and move with control"], avoid: "Rushing the twists or leaning on the machine." },
  { name: "Neck Crunches with Plate", category: "Traps", tips: ["Lie on your back with a light plate resting on your forehead", "Keep your chin slightly tucked", "Lift your head a few inches using your neck muscles", "Lower slowly and keep the movement small"], avoid: "Using a heavy plate or jerking your head up." },
  { name: "Weighted Scissor Crunch", category: "Core", tips: ["Lie on your back holding a light plate at your chest", "Lift your shoulders and extend your legs a few inches above the floor", "Cross your legs over and under each other in a scissor motion", "Keep your lower back pressed into the floor"], avoid: "Letting your lower back arch as your legs move." },
  { name: "Treadmill or Bike (Warm-Up)", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Start at an easy pace for 5 to 10 minutes", "Raise the effort gradually until you break a light sweat", "Keep your posture tall and your breathing relaxed", "Finish feeling warm, not tired"], avoid: "Going too hard and wasting energy before your workout." },
  { name: "Moderate Pace Cardio", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Pick a pace where you can talk in short sentences", "Keep your posture tall and your breathing steady", "Hold the same effort for the whole session", "Cool down with a few easy minutes at the end"], avoid: "Starting too fast and fading halfway through." },
  { name: "Active Recovery / Light Cardio", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Keep the effort very easy so you could hold a conversation", "Pick low-impact movement such as walking, cycling or swimming", "Focus on loosening up rather than getting tired", "Finish with a few stretches"], avoid: "Turning your recovery day into a hard workout." },
  { name: "Cardio", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Warm up for a few minutes at an easy pace", "Pick a pace you can hold with steady breathing", "Keep your posture tall and your shoulders relaxed", "Cool down with a few easy minutes at the end"], avoid: "Gripping the machine or rushing the pace in the first few minutes." },
  { name: "Barbell Bent Over Row to Straight Leg Deadlift", category: "Back", tips: ["Hinge forward with a flat back and row the bar to your lower ribs", "Lower the bar back to straight arms", "Push your hips back and lower the bar down your legs with a slight knee bend", "Stand tall by driving your hips forward and repeat"], avoid: "Rounding your lower back during the transition." },
  { name: "Cable Chest Fly to Cable Press", category: "Chest", tips: ["Stand between two cables with your chest up and a soft bend in your elbows", "Bring your hands together in front of your chest in a wide arc", "Pull your hands back to your chest", "Press straight out and return slowly"], avoid: "Letting your shoulders roll forward or your elbows flare during the press." },
  { name: "Arnold Dumbbell Curl with Resistance Band", category: "Biceps", tips: ["Stand on the band and hold the handles with your palms facing you", "Curl up while rotating your palms to face forward", "Squeeze your biceps at the top", "Lower slowly and rotate back"], avoid: "Swinging your torso or letting the band snap back." },
  { name: "Freestanding Squat with Resistance Band Support", category: "Legs", tips: ["Anchor the band and hold it for balance, with your feet shoulder width", "Keep your chest up and your core braced", "Squat down while using the band only for light support", "Drive up through your whole foot"], avoid: "Leaning on the band so hard that your legs do less work." },
  { name: "Push Up / Jumping Jacks (Tabata)", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Alternate 20 seconds of push-ups with 10 seconds of jumping jacks", "Keep your body in a straight line during the push-ups", "Land softly on the balls of your feet during the jacks", "Keep a steady pace so you can finish all the rounds"], avoid: "Letting your hips sag when you get tired." },
  { name: "Kettlebell Swing / Smith Machine Hang Power Clean (Tabata)", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Alternate 20 seconds of swings with 10 seconds of hang power cleans", "Hinge your hips back and snap them forward on each swing", "Keep the bar close to your body on the clean", "Stay braced and keep a flat back"], avoid: "Squatting the swing or rounding your back." },
  { name: "Dead Landmines / Burpee (Tabata)", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Alternate 20 seconds of landmine deadlifts with 10 seconds of burpees", "Keep your back flat and push your hips back on the deadlift", "Land softly and keep your core tight on the burpees", "Keep a steady pace across all the rounds"], avoid: "Rounding your back or rushing the burpees." },
  { name: "Squat / Kettlebell Snatch (Tabata)", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Alternate 20 seconds of squats with 10 seconds of kettlebell snatches", "Keep your chest up and your knees tracking over your toes on the squat", "Snap your hips and punch the kettlebell overhead on the snatch", "Use a light weight so your form stays crisp"], avoid: "Curling the kettlebell up with your arm." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Lunge / Mountain Climbers (Tabata)", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Alternate 20 seconds of dumbbell lunges with 10 seconds of mountain climbers", "Step far enough forward to keep your front shin vertical", "Keep your hips low and your core tight on the climbers", "Keep a steady pace across all the rounds"], avoid: "Letting your front knee cave inward." },
  { name: "Crunch / Cable Woodchopper (Tabata)", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Alternate 20 seconds of crunches with 10 seconds of cable woodchoppers", "Curl your ribs toward your hips on the crunch", "Rotate your torso and pivot your back foot on the chop", "Keep your movements controlled even when you tire"], avoid: "Pulling on your neck or using only your arms on the chop." },
  { name: "Kettlebell Snatch / Step Ups (Tabata)", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Alternate 20 seconds of kettlebell snatches with 10 seconds of step-ups", "Snap your hips and punch the kettlebell overhead", "Plant your whole foot on the box and drive up with your front leg", "Use a light weight and a stable box"], avoid: "Pushing off your back foot on the step-ups." },
  { name: "Dumbbell Clean / Bench Hop Overs (Tabata)", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Alternate 20 seconds of dumbbell cleans with 10 seconds of bench hop overs", "Use your hips to power the clean", "Land softly with your knees bent when hopping over the bench", "Keep a pace you can sustain"], avoid: "Landing stiff-legged or jumping too close to the bench." },
  { name: "Dead Landmines / Jumping Jacks (Tabata)", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Alternate 20 seconds of landmine deadlifts with 10 seconds of jumping jacks", "Keep your back flat and push your hips back on the deadlift", "Land softly on the balls of your feet during the jacks", "Keep a steady pace across all the rounds"], avoid: "Rounding your back on the landmine deadlift." },
  { name: "Reverse Crunch / Barbell Roll Out (Tabata)", category: "Cardio", tips: ["Alternate 20 seconds of reverse crunches with 10 seconds of barbell rollouts", "Curl your hips off the floor on the reverse crunch", "Brace your core and roll out only as far as you can control", "Pull back by tightening your abs"], avoid: "Letting your lower back sag on the rollout." }
];
